cell,model,tier,task,snapshot,repeat,raw_file,judge_prompt_version,judge_outcome,invented_count,invented_major,invented_minor,invented,voice,clarity,tone,overall,comment,error
gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-01-early-content__n-a__r1,gemma4-e2b,Minimum,news-bulletin,snap-01-early-content,1,raw/gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-01-early-content__n-a__r1.json,judge/v3,Model,4,0,4,"[minor] They are always there, demanding tribute or plunder. (stated as fact; briefing gives no ongoing activity or tribute demands) | [minor] They continue their usual tribal arrangements. (ongoing status not in briefing) | [minor] Another dreary weather prediction for another unremarkable week. (implies earlier predictions; this is the first bulletin) | [minor] The Red Gully Raiders maintain their presence in three settlements. (presence/ongoing status stated as fact beyond the faction count)",3,4,3,3,"Accurate on the two headline items and the faction counts, but the raider and clan paragraphs are filler with unsupported claims of ongoing behaviour (tribute demands, tribal arrangements), and the first item runs only two sentences of take. The dry voice is generic rather than distinct, and the first item's ""meager supplies"" colour is bland.",
gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-01-early-content__n-a__r2,gemma4-e2b,Minimum,news-bulletin,snap-01-early-content,2,raw/gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-01-early-content__n-a__r2.json,judge/v3,Model,4,0,4,"[minor] Red Gully Raiders have three settlements active this cycle. (""active this cycle"" adds an ongoing status the briefing does not report) | [minor] They continue their usual business of whatever it is they do best. (implies an ongoing activity stated as fact, though it is vague) | [minor] They remain stubbornly rooted in their current arrangement. (adds status or behaviour for the Clans that the briefing does not give) | [minor] Another predictable inconvenience for anyone trying to keep the lights on. (implies a consequence of the cold snap (power strain) and that cold snaps recur)",3,4,3,3,"The first item is accurate and the dry remarks are serviceable, but the second and third items pad with faction-size filler and vague, slightly invented status claims. Several jokes are generic, and the sentences about the Raiders and the Clans say little. The cold snap item is also too short, with only one remark and no real take.",
gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-01-early-content__n-a__r3,gemma4-e2b,Minimum,news-bulletin,snap-01-early-content,3,raw/gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-01-early-content__n-a__r3.json,judge/v3,Model,2,0,2,"[minor] Another predictable weather pattern for this time of year. (implies seasonal normality; briefing gives only the forecast, and this is stated as fact) | [minor] It seems they are always finding a way to monetize the landscape. (implies an ongoing pattern of Tarn Union behaviour not in briefing, though hedged with 'it seems')",3,4,3,3,"Accurate and sticks to the briefing, but it is short of the 70-word minimum, and each item has only about 3 short sentences with generic wit. The 'predictable for this time of year' line states an unsupported claim as fact, and the clans' complaints are a hedged guess that wanders into the Seven Ash Clans without any link to the hills.",
gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-02-early-content__n-a__r1,gemma4-e2b,Minimum,news-bulletin,snap-02-early-content,1,raw/gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-02-early-content__n-a__r1.json,judge/v3,Model,3,0,3,[minor] they always abandon things when things get inconvenient (stated as fact; implies a pattern of abandonment the briefing does not give) | [minor] The Glimmer Coast Company reports a profitable week. (repeats old news from the latest bulletin as if new; not in the briefing's new items) | [minor] The Tannerfolk continue their conflict with the Hollow Spire Pirates. (repeats old news; ongoing status presented as current),3,4,3,3,"The lead item is accurate and tidy, but the second and third items recycle old news and even a prior bulletin's joke about the Company's profitable week. The wit is generic, and the word count is thin on fresh material, though it stays within the facts.",
gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-02-early-content__n-a__r2,gemma4-e2b,Minimum,news-bulletin,snap-02-early-content,2,raw/gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-02-early-content__n-a__r2.json,judge/v3,Model,3,0,3,"[minor] This suggests a temporary lull in their usual theatrics. (implied consequence stated as fact, not framed as a guess) | [minor] The Glimmer Coast Company continues its usual profitable run. They report another week of success (repeats old news: the profitable-week claim comes from an earlier bulletin, and is not in the current briefing) | [minor] The Tannerfolk remain engaged in conflict with the Hollow Spire Pirates. (repeats old news as ongoing status; the briefing only gives that they are at war, which is fine, but this is presented as an item)",3,4,3,3,"Leads correctly with the abandoned camp and frames most guesses properly, but the second and third items pad with old news and a stale Glimmer Coast joke, and the wit is generic rather than sharp. The 'lull' claim is stated as fact rather than a guess.",
gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-02-early-content__n-a__r3,gemma4-e2b,Minimum,news-bulletin,snap-02-early-content,3,raw/gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-02-early-content__n-a__r3.json,judge/v3,Model,3,0,3,"[minor] The Glimmer Coast Company continues its profitable run. (ongoing status not in briefing; repeats old news from the earlier bulletin's claim of a profitable week) | [minor] It is a predictable move for those who prefer to leave things messy behind. (implies the camp was left messy, a consequence the briefing does not give, stated as fact) | [minor] The Tannerfolk continue their conflict with the Hollow Spire Pirates. (repeats old news as an ongoing state, though it is framed as not new and the war is in the briefing)",3,4,3,3,"Accurate on the lead item and mostly dry, but the second and third items just rehash old bulletins, and the jokes are generic (""better scenery"", ""whims of the Outlanders""). The Glimmer Coast item makes a vague claim and pads rather than finding a fresh angle in the briefing, such as the faction sizes.",
gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-03-early-strained__n-a__r1,gemma4-e2b,Minimum,news-bulletin,snap-03-early-strained,1,raw/gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-03-early-strained__n-a__r1.json,judge/v3,Model,3,0,3,"[minor] The Ashen Hand remain scattered across four settlements. (""scattered"" and ""remain"" imply an ongoing state the briefing does not report) | [minor] The Kinn of the Long Grass are moving south. (repeats old news as if current; the earlier bulletin said fires in the south, not that they move south, and presents it as ongoing) | [minor] The Merrow Freeholds continue their cautious travel patterns. (repeats old news as an ongoing status)",3,4,3,3,"The quiet-week framing is sound and the guesses are hedged, but two items just restate old bulletins with little wit, and the Kinn item treats old news as current. The humour is thin, and 'One assumes' is used twice in near-identical ways.",
gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-03-early-strained__n-a__r2,gemma4-e2b,Minimum,news-bulletin,snap-03-early-strained,2,raw/gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-03-early-strained__n-a__r2.json,judge/v3,Model,3,0,3,"[minor] The Ashen Hand remain where they have been (ongoing status not in briefing) | [minor] The Kinn of the Long Grass are reportedly moving south due to grass fires. (repeats old news as current; also the earlier bulletin said fires were in the south, not that they moved south) | [minor] the Merrow Freeholds continue their cautious travel patterns (repeats old news as ongoing status)",3,4,3,3,"Accurate on faction counts and the guesses are framed properly, but the second item presents the earlier Kinn bulletin as present news and slightly changes it (moving south). The wit is mild and the third item is a flat recitation of numbers rather than a dry take.",
gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-03-early-strained__n-a__r3,gemma4-e2b,Minimum,news-bulletin,snap-03-early-strained,3,raw/gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-03-early-strained__n-a__r3.json,judge/v3,Model,6,0,6,"[minor] The Ashen Hand remain where they are (ongoing status not in briefing; implies no movement) | [minor] the Merrow Freeholds continue their cautious travel patterns (repeats old news as ongoing status; 'continue' not reported) | [minor] The Kinn of the Long Grass are reportedly moving due to grass fires in the south. (repeats old news from the latest bulletin as if current) | [minor] They claim they are not seeking conflict. (repeats old news from the latest bulletin) | [minor] The current distribution of settlements remains unchanged. (comparison with an earlier state the briefing does not give) | [minor] The Merrow Freeholds maintain seven outposts. (briefing says settlements, not outposts; minor wording shift)",3,4,3,3,"Clear, but the second item re-presents the previous bulletin's Kinn story as current, and the status claims go beyond the briefing. The wit is thin and the third item is largely a flat restatement of numbers; it only lightly meets the dry-remark requirement.
",
gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-04-early-strained__n-a__r1,gemma4-e2b,Minimum,news-bulletin,snap-04-early-strained,1,raw/gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-04-early-strained__n-a__r1.json,judge/v3,Model,3,0,3,"[minor] is still seeking news of its reporter Tomas Quell (""still"" implies an ongoing search the briefing does not report) | [minor] even if it’s just on a piece of rotting wood (states the ferry was rotting, which the briefing does not say) | [minor] Another piece of local mischief (implies earlier similar incidents, which the briefing does not give; this is the first bulletin)",3,4,3,3,"The bulletin is clear and uses the briefing's facts with properly hedged guesses, but the wit is generic and a few small embellishments slip in (""still seeking"", ""rotting wood"", ""Another piece""). It also merges two items into one paragraph and does not use the faction facts.",
gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-04-early-strained__n-a__r2,gemma4-e2b,Minimum,news-bulletin,snap-04-early-strained,2,raw/gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-04-early-strained__n-a__r2.json,judge/v3,Model,2,0,2,"[minor] even if it’s just a piece of rotting timber (implies the ferry was rotting; the briefing gives no condition for it) | [minor] Lowmere seems to offer little material for serious reporting (a hedged opinion, but it edges toward stating a cause for the Dispatch pulling out)",3,3,3,3,"The facts are accurate, but the bulletin breaks the format: the first paragraph merges two items and the second is not a full item with a fact and a take. It is also short on the required three-sentence items, and the jokes are mild and generic. The 'rotting timber' line adds a small unsupported detail.",
gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-04-early-strained__n-a__r3,gemma4-e2b,Minimum,news-bulletin,snap-04-early-strained,3,raw/gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-04-early-strained__n-a__r3.json,judge/v3,Model,2,0,2,"[minor] This suggests Lowmere has become sufficiently unremarkable for our interests. (implied cause for the Dispatch stopping reporters, stated as fact rather than a guess) | [minor] Another piece of local mischief (implies earlier similar incidents; the briefing gives none)",3,3,3,2,"The bulletin is dry in places but thin: it has only 2 paragraphs, and the ferry burning is merged into the Tomas Quell item with a weak joke. It also falls well short of the required length and sentence count, and it states a cause for the reporter ban as fact. The Lowmere item is also odd, because the Dispatch is the writer's own outlet, yet the text speaks of it as 'they' and 'our' inconsistently.",
gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-05-early-desperate__n-a__r1,gemma4-e2b,Minimum,news-bulletin,snap-05-early-desperate,1,raw/gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-05-early-desperate__n-a__r1.json,judge/v3,Model,3,1,2,"[minor] Scythe Tooth raids have been noted in three locations. (repeats old news as if current; presented without being framed as background) | The Ferrow Mutual has requested increased patrols. They have inquired about the funding for these efforts. (repeats old news from an earlier bulletin and changes it: the earlier bulletin said the Mutual asked members to share patrols, and that its members asked who is paying, not the Mutual) | [minor] This suggests a predictable pattern of petty larceny. (inference stated as fact; 'petty' is an added characterisation of the raids)",3,3,3,2,"Only the first item is new, and the other two recycle earlier bulletins as if current, with the Ferrow item garbling who asked whom. The wit is thin, with some flat lines, and the first item is padded with a restatement of the fact.",
gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-05-early-desperate__n-a__r2,gemma4-e2b,Minimum,news-bulletin,snap-05-early-desperate,2,raw/gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-05-early-desperate__n-a__r2.json,judge/v3,Model,3,0,3,"[minor] They have always preferred their own arrangements. (stated as fact; the briefing gives no history of the Clans' preferences) | [minor] Scythe Tooth raids are reported at three settlements. (repeats old news as if current, with no 'earlier' framing) | [minor] The Ferrow Mutual has requested shared patrols. (repeats old news from an earlier bulletin as if new)",3,4,3,3,"It leads correctly with the market closure, but then presents two old items as fresh news, and the wit is thin and generic. It is also short on the required sentence count, and the first item has only three brief sentences with little real take.",
gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-05-early-desperate__n-a__r3,gemma4-e2b,Minimum,news-bulletin,snap-05-early-desperate,3,raw/gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-05-early-desperate__n-a__r3.json,judge/v3,Model,5,0,5,"[minor] They have always preferred to keep their dealings to themselves. (stated as fact; briefing gives no history of Gorse Clans' trading habits, and it contradicts the earlier bulletin showing them trading furs for grain) | [minor] Scythe Tooth raids have been reported at three settlements. (repeats old news as if current, with no 'earlier' framing) | [minor] The Ferrow Mutual has requested shared patrols. (repeats old news from the previous bulletin as if new) | [minor] The factions remain in their established patterns. (unreported status claim stated as fact) | [minor] It is a quiet week, which is hardly a novelty. (contradicts the market closure it just reported and implies a comparison with earlier weeks not in briefing)",3,4,3,2,"It leads correctly with the market closure, but presents old raid and patrol news as current and pads the last item with vacuous claims; the wit is mild and the 'always preferred' claim contradicts earlier trading. Third item says quiet week after reporting a closure, and word count is under the 70 minimum.",
gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-06-early-content__n-a__r1,gemma4-e2b,Minimum,news-bulletin,snap-06-early-content,1,raw/gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-06-early-content__n-a__r1.json,judge/v3,Model,4,0,4,"[minor] They took supplies from a vessel moving through the delta waters. (adds detail: that it was moving and what was taken; the briefing says only a robbery of a grain barge) | [minor] The Calder Combine reports good harvests along the delta. (repeats old news as a main item, presented as current rather than background) | [minor] This suggests the Combine is managing its resources adequately. (inference stated as fact, not framed as a guess) | [minor] just another Tuesday for the pirates (implies robberies are routine, a comparison with earlier state not in the briefing (framed as a guess, so borderline))",3,4,3,2,"The Ditch Kings item is accurate but padded by restating the same fact. The second item recycles old news as if current and adds a guess about a 'shortfall' that contradicts the good-harvest report. The wit is generic and the third item is filler, though acceptable for a quiet week.​",
gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-06-early-content__n-a__r2,gemma4-e2b,Minimum,news-bulletin,snap-06-early-content,2,raw/gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-06-early-content__n-a__r2.json,judge/v3,Model,4,0,4,[minor] The pirates made off with some provisions. (added outcome of the robbery; briefing only says the barge was robbed) | [minor] The Calder Combine reports good harvests along the delta. (repeats old news as if current; presented as an item in this bulletin) | [minor] They always report good harvests when things are otherwise predictable. (stated as fact; implies a pattern of reporting the briefing does not give) | [minor] Three settlements are holding steady. (adds a status ('holding steady') the briefing does not report),3,4,3,3,"The bulletin leads correctly with the new item, but it pads with a repeat of old news presented as a current item and adds small unsupported details. The humour is thin, with 'predictable' used three times, and the item on the Sundered Throne is filler with weak wit.",
gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-06-early-content__n-a__r3,gemma4-e2b,Minimum,news-bulletin,snap-06-early-content,3,raw/gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-06-early-content__n-a__r3.json,judge/v3,Model,5,0,5,"[minor] The pirates managed to take some provisions from a transport vessel. (""some provisions"" implies a partial take; the briefing only says a grain barge was robbed, with no amount given) | [minor] They are three settlements in total, and they have not made any noise lately. (""not made any noise lately"" adds an ongoing status beyond ""quiet behind its walls"") | [minor] It is probably just a sign that they are waiting for something to happen. (hedged with ""probably"", but still an inference about the Throne's intent; borderline, not counted as a fact) | [minor] The Calder Combine continues to report good harvests along the delta. (repeats old news and presents it as ongoing/new (""continues to report"") rather than as background) | [minor] They claim the yield is excellent this cycle. (repeats old news; ""excellent this cycle"" is a restatement with a slight change, no new briefing support)",3,4,3,3,"The lead item is accurate and the dry guesses are properly hedged, but two of the three items just rehash old news and quiet-faction filler, and the Combine harvest is presented as ongoing rather than as brief background. The wit is mild and the first item's joke is muddled.",
gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-07-mid-strained__n-a__r1,gemma4-e2b,Minimum,news-bulletin,snap-07-mid-strained,1,raw/gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-07-mid-strained__n-a__r1.json,judge/v3,Model,4,0,4,"[minor] This is hardly news. (implies the tolls are unsurprising or a repeat, which the briefing does not support; the tolls are new) | [minor] Vex's Crew has two settlements operating. ('operating' adds an ongoing activity status the briefing does not report) | [minor] The Iron Covenant has eight settlements scattered about. ('scattered about' adds an unsupported detail about their layout) | [minor] It is a quiet week, which is always the most tedious sort of week. (contradicts the lead item, since a new toll demand means the week was not quiet)",3,4,3,3,"Facts stay close to the briefing and the guesses are properly hedged, but the toll news is dismissed as 'hardly news' and then the bulletin calls the week quiet. The wit is generic, the Vex and Covenant items are filler, and there is no link to the earlier bulletins' dry observational style or to the gorge context.",
gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-07-mid-strained__n-a__r2,gemma4-e2b,Minimum,news-bulletin,snap-07-mid-strained,2,raw/gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-07-mid-strained__n-a__r2.json,judge/v3,Model,3,0,3,"[minor] They are always maintaining, which is a full-time job for pirates. (states ongoing activity as fact; briefing only gives the settlement count) | [minor] which suggests a lot of internal squabbling (implied cause/inference about the Covenant not in briefing, though hedged as 'suggests') | [minor] Vex's Crew maintains its two settlements. (ongoing activity/status not reported in briefing)",3,3,3,3,"The dry voice is serviceable, but the items are thin: two of the three are filler about faction sizes, and the lead item is dismissed as 'hardly news' despite being the only new fact. It also has fewer than three sentences per item in places and the first item lacks a real wry take, while the pirate 'always maintaining' line states unsupported activity.",
gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-07-mid-strained__n-a__r3,gemma4-e2b,Minimum,news-bulletin,snap-07-mid-strained,3,raw/gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-07-mid-strained__n-a__r3.json,judge/v3,Model,4,1,3,"Vex's Crew has two settlements operating nearby. (briefing gives no location for Vex's Crew; 'nearby' places them somewhere unsupported) | [minor] They are always operating nearby, which is usually the problem. (ongoing activity and implied cause not in briefing) | [minor] They are perpetually short on supplies, as usual. (ongoing status not in briefing; extends one lost wagon into a chronic shortage) | [minor] This is hardly news. (implies the toll demand was expected or previously known, which the briefing does not say)",3,4,3,2,"The toll item is correct, but the Vex's Crew item adds an unsupported location and the Iron Covenant item pads with invented chronic shortage. Its dry voice is generic, and the item about the Covenant's wearing patience is stated as a guess without any basis in the briefing.",
gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-08-mid-content__n-a__r1,gemma4-e2b,Minimum,news-bulletin,snap-08-mid-content,1,raw/gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-08-mid-content__n-a__r1.json,judge/v3,Model,4,0,4,"[minor] It sits there, presumably, gathering dust while the merchants argue over its worth. (framed as a guess, but location and merchants arguing implied; borderline, mostly hedged) | [minor] The Lantern Accord continues its trade fair preparations at Lantern Hill. (repeats old news and adds an ongoing status (preparations); earlier bulletin said the fair opens next week) | [minor] The Ninefingers Gang remains quiet after their failed raid on Gladwater. (repeats old news from the latest bulletin, presented as a current status without new information) | [minor] They promise fair prices, which is always a bold claim in this line of work. (repeats old news from an earlier bulletin)",3,4,3,3,"Leads correctly with the one new item, but pads the bulletin with two items repeated from earlier bulletins as if current, and the jokes are mild and partly recycled (fair prices promise). The new item gets little actual wit beyond the dust remark.",
gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-08-mid-content__n-a__r2,gemma4-e2b,Minimum,news-bulletin,snap-08-mid-content,2,raw/gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-08-mid-content__n-a__r2.json,judge/v3,Model,4,0,4,"[minor] The Lantern Accord continues its trade fair preparations at Lantern Hill. (repeats old news as ongoing; briefing gives only that the fair is being hosted, and an earlier bulletin said it opens next week, not that preparations continue) | [minor] The Reedmother's Children report a good fishing season. They claim the river is full and the fish are foolish. (repeats old news, presented as a fresh item rather than brief background) | [minor] They promise fair prices, which is usually a hollow thing out here. (repeats old news; the 'usually hollow' claim is stated as fact about the rim) | [minor] It sits there, presumably, gathering dust while the traders argue over its worth. (claims the sculpture is at Lantern Hill and traders are arguing over its worth; hedged with 'presumably' but the argument is stated as fact)",3,4,3,3,"The first item is properly led and hedged, but two of the three items just rehash old bulletins as if they were current news, and the quiet-week option (faction sizes, date) went unused. The wit is thin and generic, and the final item admits it has nothing new to report.",
gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-08-mid-content__n-a__r3,gemma4-e2b,Minimum,news-bulletin,snap-08-mid-content,3,raw/gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-08-mid-content__n-a__r3.json,judge/v3,Model,5,0,5,"[minor] The Lantern Accord continues its trade fair preparations. (ongoing activity not in briefing; fair is old news, and earlier bulletin said it opens next week, so 'continues preparations' is a status claim) | [minor] They are always busy with their displays. (stated as fact; added detail about the Accord not in briefing) | [minor] The Reedmother's Children report the river is full. They claim the fish are foolish. (repeats old news presented as new; the fishing season was covered in an earlier bulletin) | [minor] This sounds like a predictable seasonal complaint. (mischaracterises a good fishing report as a complaint) | [minor] It sits there, presumably, gathering dust while the traders argue over its worth. (traders arguing over its worth is stated beyond the guess; briefing only says it is the talk of traders)",3,4,3,3,"The lead item is correct, but the second and third items rehash old news as if it were new and add unsupported colour, including calling a good fishing report a complaint. The wit is thin and generic, and the guesses are repetitive ('One assumes' twice), so the voice feels formulaic.",
gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-09-mid-desperate__n-a__r1,gemma4-e2b,Minimum,news-bulletin,snap-09-mid-desperate,1,raw/gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-09-mid-desperate__n-a__r1.json,judge/v3,Model,3,0,3,"[minor] concerning fishing rights (repeats old news; the fishing-rights cause appears only in an earlier bulletin, not the current briefing, and is presented as a continuing fact) | [minor] continues without apparent resolution (ongoing status of the war not reported in the briefing) | [minor] They are currently engaged with the Embertail Tribe. (repeats old news about the war as ongoing activity, and duplicates the previous item)",3,4,3,3,"The Malley item is accurate and the guess is properly framed, but the other two items recycle the old war news and repeat each other. The wit is thin and the prose is flat, so it reads as generic rather than sardonic.",
gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-09-mid-desperate__n-a__r2,gemma4-e2b,Minimum,news-bulletin,snap-09-mid-desperate,2,raw/gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-09-mid-desperate__n-a__r2.json,judge/v3,Model,2,0,2,"[minor] The Embertail Tribe continues its conflict with The Gray Wharf Syndicate. (repeats old news; war was already covered, and 'continues' implies an ongoing status not reported) | [minor] They remain engaged with the Embertail Tribe. (repeats old news as an ongoing status the briefing does not report)",2,4,3,2,"The Malley item is accurate but thin, and the rest pads the bulletin by restating the already-covered war twice with generic filler. The voice is flat rather than sardonic, with little real wit and no new information.",
gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-09-mid-desperate__n-a__r3,gemma4-e2b,Minimum,news-bulletin,snap-09-mid-desperate,3,raw/gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-09-mid-desperate__n-a__r3.json,judge/v3,Model,4,0,4,"[minor] The Embertail Tribe remains engaged with The Gray Wharf Syndicate. (ongoing status of the war is not reported in the briefing; implies it is still active) | [minor] This conflict concerns fishing rights, as previously noted. (repeats old news; the fishing-rights cause comes from an earlier bulletin, not this briefing) | [minor] It is a predictable squabble over sustenance. (asserts the fishing-rights cause and frames it as sustenance, which is added interpretation) | [minor] This distribution suggests a certain level of established routine. (inference stated as fact, not framed as a guess)",3,4,3,3,"Accurate on Malley's death and faction counts, but the voice is flat and generic rather than sardonic, and the second item re-reports old news. The third item is filler with little wit; the opening guess about the Lancers is the best line.",
gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-10-mid-strained__n-a__r1,gemma4-e2b,Minimum,news-bulletin,snap-10-mid-strained,1,raw/gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-10-mid-strained__n-a__r1.json,judge/v3,Model,4,0,4,"[minor] Stonecutter Raiders are currently holding captives from the Ochre Hand. (repeats old news as a separate item; presented as a current item rather than brief background) | [minor] The Weir Federation continues to maintain a bounty on Stonecutter leaders. (repeats old news as a full item; 'continues to maintain' is an ongoing status the briefing does not report) | [minor] They are always holding something, it seems. (implies a habitual pattern of captive-taking not in the briefing, though hedged with 'it seems') | [minor] It is a predictable pattern for outlanders; they always want to pay for trouble. (generalisation stated as fact about outlanders, implying a past pattern the briefing does not give)",3,4,3,3,"Only one new item exists, yet two of the three paragraphs just restate old news, which the task said to avoid (two items were enough). The dry voice is present but generic, and the first item's speculation about desperation and trade terms is mild filler, though hedged correctly.",
gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-10-mid-strained__n-a__r2,gemma4-e2b,Minimum,news-bulletin,snap-10-mid-strained,2,raw/gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-10-mid-strained__n-a__r2.json,judge/v3,Model,4,0,4,"[minor] Stonecutter Raiders are still holding captives from the Ochre Hand. (repeats old news as an ongoing status, presented as a fresh item) | [minor] The Weir Federation maintains its bounty on Stonecutter leaders. (repeats old news; the 'maintains' status is not reported in the briefing) | [minor] One assumes they are desperate enough to offer coin for people they already have. (garbled: the Ochre Hand does not hold the captives, so this is a muddled claim, though framed as a guess) | [minor] They are clearly keen on keeping the local riff-raff busy. (an inference about motive stated as fact ('clearly'))",3,2,3,2,"Two of the three items repeat old news as if current, and the first item's joke is confused, since the Ochre Hand does not hold the captives. The dry voice is generic, and there is little new content beyond the one real fact.",
gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-10-mid-strained__n-a__r3,gemma4-e2b,Minimum,news-bulletin,snap-10-mid-strained,3,raw/gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-10-mid-strained__n-a__r3.json,judge/v3,Model,4,0,4,"[minor] This suggests a predictable cycle of violence and ransom. (inference about a recurring cycle, stated as fact without a briefing basis) | [minor] Stonecutter Raiders are currently holding captives from the Ochre Hand. (repeats old news as a new item) | [minor] The Weir Federation maintains a bounty on Stonecutter leaders. (repeats old news as a new item) | [minor] This is standard procedure for those who cause trouble. (added claim about a standard practice, stated as fact)",3,4,3,3,"Only the first item is new; the other two repeat earlier bulletins as current news, and the bounty line nearly copies the previous bulletin's joke. The wit is thin and generic, and the item about captives wanting the price is muddled.",
gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-11-mid-content__n-a__r1,gemma4-e2b,Minimum,news-bulletin,snap-11-mid-content,1,raw/gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-11-mid-content__n-a__r1.json,judge/v3,Model,4,0,4,"[minor] This suggests a temporary truce, which is usually just a pause before the next inevitable squabble. (inference about the feast stated as fact (a temporary truce); the briefing only says a peace feast was held) | [minor] Reports indicate the Hearthguard Compact is still offering prizes for new inventions. (repeats old news as an ongoing status, 'still offering', which the briefing does not report) | [minor] The Mire Rats remain a nuisance (ongoing status not in the briefing; also repeats old news) | [minor] now they are somewhere else entirely (stated as fact; the briefing does not say where they went, and the line contradicts 'whereabouts unconfirmed')",3,4,3,3,"The lead item is correct and in order, but items two and three rehash old news as ongoing, which the task forbids. The wit is generic ('shiny trinkets', 'inevitable squabble') and doesn't match the sharper earlier bulletins.",
gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-11-mid-content__n-a__r2,gemma4-e2b,Minimum,news-bulletin,snap-11-mid-content,2,raw/gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-11-mid-content__n-a__r2.json,judge/v3,Model,4,0,4,"[minor] This suggests a temporary truce, which is always a fragile thing. (inference stated as fact: the feast is called a truce and temporary, which the briefing does not say) | [minor] Reports indicate that the Hearthguard Compact continues to offer prizes for new inventions. (repeats old news as a current, ongoing status; the briefing says only that the earlier bulletin covered it) | [minor] The Mire Rats remain a nuisance, though they are not currently near the eastern marsh. (repeats old news and adds an ongoing status ('remain a nuisance') that the briefing does not report) | [minor] Their current whereabouts are, predictably, a mystery. (repeats old news; the earlier bulletin said where they went was unclear, but this is presented as a current update)",3,4,3,2,"The lead item is correct and the dry tone is passable, but two of the three items re-run old news as current developments, which the task forbids, and the remarks are generic. The 'temporary truce' line also asserts an inference as fact. The word count is also short of 70 words only in spirit; the real issue is padding with stale news.",
gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-11-mid-content__n-a__r3,gemma4-e2b,Minimum,news-bulletin,snap-11-mid-content,3,raw/gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-11-mid-content__n-a__r3.json,judge/v3,Model,4,0,4,"[minor] This suggests a temporary truce, which is usually just a pause before the next inevitable squabble. (inference stated as fact: calls the peace temporary, though the briefing only reports a feast) | [minor] Reports indicate the Hearthguard Compact continues to offer prizes for new inventions. (repeats old news as a current, ongoing status the briefing does not report) | [minor] The Mire Rats remain a nuisance, though their whereabouts are still murky. (repeats old news and adds an ongoing status ('remain a nuisance') the briefing does not give) | [minor] They were driven out of the eastern marsh previously. (repeats old news, though it is framed as background)",3,4,3,3,"The lead item is correct, but two of the three items are padded with old news. The wit is generic, and it reads as filler on a quiet week instead of using the faction numbers or the date.",
gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-12-mid-desperate__n-a__r1,gemma4-e2b,Minimum,news-bulletin,snap-12-mid-desperate,1,raw/gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-12-mid-desperate__n-a__r1.json,judge/v3,Model,3,0,3,[minor] given the usual tedious dance between the Empire and the Outlanders (implies a history of repeated exchanges the briefing does not give) | [minor] The Gallows Crew continues to hold a doctor. (repeats old news as an ongoing status without framing it as background) | [minor] which is a welcome respite from the usual regional commotion (implies regional commotion the briefing does not report),3,4,3,3,"The lead item is correct and the guesses are properly hedged. The second item mostly rehashes old news, and the third is thin filler. The wit is generic, and the 'tedious dance' line implies a history the briefing does not support. The piece also omits the captive status and the fallout background in any useful way.",
gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-12-mid-desperate__n-a__r2,gemma4-e2b,Minimum,news-bulletin,snap-12-mid-desperate,2,raw/gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-12-mid-desperate__n-a__r2.json,judge/v3,Model,4,0,4,"[minor] The Gallows Crew continues to hold a doctor. (repeats old news as an ongoing status; the briefing gives it only as earlier background) | [minor] It is a predictable pattern for those who deal in illicit trade. (implies a trade and a pattern of behaviour the briefing does not give, stated as fact) | [minor] apparently undisturbed by the regional unpleasantness (claims a status inside the Empire's walls that the briefing does not report, only loosely hedged) | [minor] Such gestures rarely signal anything of real consequence in these dusty corners. (generalisation stated as fact about past envoy visits; the briefing gives none)",3,4,3,3,"The lead item is accurate and in the right dry register, but the wit is generic, and the second and third items pad with old news and unsupported claims about illicit trade and the Empire's condition. The bulletin also runs short of the 70-word minimum.",
gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-12-mid-desperate__n-a__r3,gemma4-e2b,Minimum,news-bulletin,snap-12-mid-desperate,3,raw/gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-12-mid-desperate__n-a__r3.json,judge/v3,Model,4,0,4,"[minor] Such exchanges rarely signal anything of real consequence in this dreary expanse. (stated as fact; implies a history of past exchanges the briefing does not give) | [minor] The Gallows Crew continues to hold a doctor at their camp. (repeats old news as an ongoing status without framing it as background) | [minor] It is a predictable pattern for those who deal in such small, desperate possessions. (implies a pattern of past behaviour the briefing does not give) | [minor] The Saltmarch Assembly remains in its usual state of quiet assembly. (ongoing status not in the briefing; 'quiet' belongs to the Glass Throne)",3,4,3,3,"Accurate on the lead item and roughly in voice, but the second item rehashes old news and the third is filler. The wit is bland and the added claims about patterns and a 'usual state' go beyond the briefing; the dry takes are generic and not very funny.
",
gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-13-mid-strained__n-a__r1,gemma4-e2b,Minimum,news-bulletin,snap-13-mid-strained,1,raw/gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-13-mid-strained__n-a__r1.json,judge/v3,Model,5,2,3,"The owners are offering compensation for the loss of goods. (the reward detail comes from an earlier bulletin, not the briefing's facts, and it is changed from a reward for return to compensation) | [minor] The Rustback Raiders were heard to have targeted a caravan on the old highway. (repeats old news as if newly heard) | Six settlements are currently involved in this tiresome exchange. (wrong: six is the Sun Throne's settlement count, while the tribute demands went to the Cobalt Free Towns (seven settlements)) | [minor] It hardly changes the balance of power, but it does give the Empire something to grumble about. (implied consequence not in the briefing) | [minor] It seems the Empire has a very reliable, if tedious, revenue stream to rely on. (contradicts the new refusal and implies tribute is being paid; hedged but unsupported)",3,3,3,2,"The dry voice is serviceable, but the second item repeats old news and distorts it (compensation instead of reward), and the third misstates the six settlements as involved in the tribute exchange. The new item is correct but gets padded with old material instead of a proper quiet-week treatment.",
gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-13-mid-strained__n-a__r2,gemma4-e2b,Minimum,news-bulletin,snap-13-mid-strained,2,raw/gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-13-mid-strained__n-a__r2.json,judge/v3,Model,4,1,3,"They are offering rewards for the goods and for explanations of their methods. (misattributes the reward to the raiders; the earlier bulletin said the caravan's owners offered it, and 'methods' changes the story) | [minor] The Rustback Raiders have been active again, hitting a caravan on the old highway. (repeats old news as if new; 'active again' implies fresh activity) | [minor] The Sun Throne continues its tiresome demands for tribute across the rim. (repeats old news (the tribute demand) as ongoing, and 'across the rim' widens the scope) | [minor] They are probably just trying to save a few scraps of coin. (motive is a guess, but 'a few scraps' is an implied scale that the briefing does not give)",3,3,3,2,"The raider item is old news retold as new, and it wrongly makes the raiders the ones offering rewards, which is a major error. The tribute item is also split into two overlapping paragraphs, so the bulletin is padded and the wit is generic.",
gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-13-mid-strained__n-a__r3,gemma4-e2b,Minimum,news-bulletin,snap-13-mid-strained,3,raw/gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-13-mid-strained__n-a__r3.json,judge/v3,Model,5,0,5,"[minor] They seem quite keen on avoiding paperwork, which is always a good sign. (implies a motive for refusal not in briefing, though hedged with 'seem' and mostly wit) | [minor] The Rustback Raiders are still active on the old highway. (ongoing activity not reported; the briefing only says they hit a caravan earlier) | [minor] They continue their usual business of making things inconvenient for anyone with a cargo. (ongoing activity stated as fact, not in briefing) | [minor] The Sun Throne continues its tiresome demands for tribute. (repeats old news as a separate item; second item is a duplicate of the lead's context) | [minor] The Rustback Raiders are still active on the old highway. (repeats old news: the caravan raid was covered in an earlier bulletin and is presented as current)",3,4,3,3,"The lead item is accurate and suitably dry, but the second and third items pad with old news presented as ongoing, and the wit is generic. Fewer items would have been better than rehashing the tribute demand and the raid.",
gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-14-mid-content__n-a__r1,gemma4-e2b,Minimum,news-bulletin,snap-14-mid-content,1,raw/gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-14-mid-content__n-a__r1.json,judge/v3,Model,5,1,4,"The League trades furs for steel from the Tribe. (the briefing gives no trade terms; the furs and steel come from an earlier bulletin, and the direction is garbled (the earlier bulletin has the League getting furs and the Tribe getting steel, but this line says the League trades furs for steel from the Tribe)) | [minor] His crewmates are reportedly conflicted about the experience. (repeats old news and recycles the earlier bulletin's crewmate reaction, which is not in the current briefing) | [minor] The Fernhollow League and the Blue Antler Tribe have a trade pact. (repeats old news and presents it as new, not as background) | [minor] A released Brackwater Corsair spoke of being well fed by his captors. (repeats old news as a fresh item; the briefing says he is talking about his captors' kindness, and 'well fed' comes from the earlier bulletin) | [minor] just another Tuesday for maritime larceny (implies raids like this are routine, a comparison with earlier states the briefing does not give)",3,3,3,2,"Two of the three items repeat old news as if it were fresh, and the furs-for-steel line garbles the earlier bulletin's trade terms. The raid item itself is fine but thin, and the wit is generic.",
gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-14-mid-content__n-a__r2,gemma4-e2b,Minimum,news-bulletin,snap-14-mid-content,2,raw/gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-14-mid-content__n-a__r2.json,judge/v3,Model,4,0,4,"[minor] The Brackwater Corsairs have been spotted near the river. (briefing says raided a barge on the river, not that they were spotted near it; added status) | [minor] One assumes this is just another Tuesday for maritime larceny. (implies raiding is routine; framed as an assumption, so mild, and Tuesday is a figure of speech) | [minor] The League secures furs, and the Tribe gets steel. (repeats old news as current present-tense item; details come from earlier bulletin, not new) | [minor] His crewmates are reportedly conflicted. (repeats old news; reworded from earlier bulletin's reaction, which is not in the briefing)",3,4,3,2,"Only the first item is new; the second and third re-present old news (the trade pact and the released Corsair) as if fresh, which the task forbids. The wit is mild and partly recycled from earlier bulletins, though the writing is clear.",
gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-14-mid-content__n-a__r3,gemma4-e2b,Minimum,news-bulletin,snap-14-mid-content,3,raw/gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-14-mid-content__n-a__r3.json,judge/v3,Model,4,0,4,"[minor] They exchange furs for steel. (repeats old news as present fact; the earlier bulletin gave the furs/steel detail, and the briefing's pact item does not) | [minor] The Blue Antler Tribe and the Fernhollow League have a trade pact. (repeats old news, presented without being framed as background) | [minor] The Brackwater Corsairs are still active. (ongoing activity the briefing does not report) | [minor] The Corsairs are always busy, I suppose. (implies ongoing habitual activity beyond the briefing, though hedged)",3,4,3,3,"The lead item is accurate, but the second item repeats the old trade pact, including the furs-for-steel detail, with no new information, and the third item is padding with no new fact. The dry voice is generic and the jokes are thin, and the output is short of the 70-word minimum.",
gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-15-late-content__n-a__r1,gemma4-e2b,Minimum,news-bulletin,snap-15-late-content,1,raw/gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-15-late-content__n-a__r1.json,judge/v3,Model,3,1,2,"[minor] The Fox-Lantern Tribe's spring games continue. The archery dispute is now on its third day (repeats old news; the briefing lists the games as earlier coverage, and the archery argument comes from an earlier bulletin, not the briefing) | [minor] The Greywater Concord has a new speaker. (repeats old news presented as a current item, not as background) | She promised less bother for the outlanders. (changes the earlier promise (lower tolls and fewer speeches) into something the briefing does not say; Concord members are outlanders themselves)",3,4,3,2,"The first item is accurate and suitably guarded, but two of the three items just rehash old news as current, and the speaker's promise is misstated. The text also falls short of the required three sentences per item, and the ""synth-tea"" joke is weak.",
gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-15-late-content__n-a__r2,gemma4-e2b,Minimum,news-bulletin,snap-15-late-content,2,raw/gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-15-late-content__n-a__r2.json,judge/v3,Model,5,0,5,"[minor] They are apparently interested in his business. (inference about why the Choir asks; hedged with 'apparently' but 'his business' implies Leopold has a business, not in briefing) | [minor] The Greywater Concord has elected a new speaker. (repeats old news, presented as current without framing as background) | [minor] They promised lower tolls, which is usually a hollow gesture. (repeats old news; also 'they' is wrong, the earlier bulletin says the speaker (she) promised) | [minor] The Fox-Lantern Tribe is holding its spring games. (repeats old news, presented as current) | [minor] The archery dispute is ongoing, as expected. (repeats old news and claims ongoing status the briefing does not report)",3,4,3,3,"The lead item is correct and hedged, but the other two items just restate old news as if current, and the archery dispute is claimed as ongoing. The wit is mild and generic, and the bulletin runs short on words and on the three-sentence-per-item requirement for the final item's substance.␀",
gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-15-late-content__n-a__r3,gemma4-e2b,Minimum,news-bulletin,snap-15-late-content,3,raw/gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-15-late-content__n-a__r3.json,judge/v3,Model,5,1,4,"[minor] They seem interested in someone who is likely trouble. (Inference about Leopold stated as likely fact; the briefing says nothing about who he is.) | Grinning Jack's Men are reportedly making moves near the outer rim. (Invented event and location; the briefing gives no activity for Grinning Jack's Men.) | [minor] They always make moves. (Claims a habitual pattern of behaviour that the briefing does not give.) | [minor] Archery remains a point of contention, as expected. (Repeats old news as current; the argument comes from an earlier bulletin and the briefing does not say it is ongoing.) | [minor] The Fox-Lantern Tribe's spring games continue their proceedings. (Repeats old news and implies the games are still running, which the briefing does not report.)",3,4,3,2,"The Leopold item is handled acceptably, but the Grinning Jack's Men item is invented from nothing and the tribe item recycles old news as if current. The wit is also thin and generic, and the item is not a three-sentence fact plus a take.}",
gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-16-late-desperate__n-a__r1,gemma4-e2b,Minimum,news-bulletin,snap-16-late-desperate,1,raw/gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-16-late-desperate__n-a__r1.json,judge/v3,Model,3,0,3,"[minor] even when those assets are a pirate (calls Kael a pirate; briefing calls him a mercenary, though Dunmore's Free Company is pirates, so this links him to the faction unsupported) | [minor] The Lantern Accord has set a price on Kael Dunmore's head. ... Mercenary Kael Dunmore now carries a price (repeats the same fact twice as two separate items, presenting the briefing's duplicate as distinct news) | [minor] It seems the mercenary trade remains a reliable source of local commerce. (implies status of mercenary trade not in briefing, though hedged with 'it seems')",3,3,3,3,"The dry voice is present but generic, and the first two items say the same thing, so the bulletin feels padded. The Glass Throne item adds nothing new and the heatwave background is missing; the 'pirate' label for a mercenary is a mild slip.",
gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-16-late-desperate__n-a__r2,gemma4-e2b,Minimum,news-bulletin,snap-16-late-desperate,2,raw/gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-16-late-desperate__n-a__r2.json,judge/v3,Model,3,0,3,"[minor] This suggests the mercenary is still capable of causing trouble. (inference stated as fact about his current ability; briefing gives only the ambush) | [minor] It is hardly surprising that the Outlanders are concerned with such matters. (implied motive/state of the Accord not in briefing, stated as fact) | [minor] The Glass Throne maintains a quiet presence behind its walls. (briefing says quiet behind its walls; 'maintains a presence' and 'preferred state of inaction' add an ongoing status not reported)",3,3,3,3,"The first two items restate the same bounty twice as if separate news, so the bulletin is padded and repetitive, and the wit is mild and generic. It stays within briefing facts, but the jokes are weak and the Empire item adds little.",
gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-16-late-desperate__n-a__r3,gemma4-e2b,Minimum,news-bulletin,snap-16-late-desperate,3,raw/gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-16-late-desperate__n-a__r3.json,judge/v3,Model,3,0,3,"[minor] This suggests a certain level of organized desperation among the Outlanders. (inference about the Accord's state stated as fact (hedged only by 'suggests')) | [minor] It is predictable that such incidents generate new forms of commerce. (general claim stated as fact, implies consequence not in briefing) | [minor] The Glass Throne maintains a quiet presence behind its walls. (briefing says quiet behind walls, but 'maintains a presence' adds ongoing status; low risk)",3,3,3,3,"Facts are mostly faithful, but the first two items are the same news restated, which reads as padding, and the humour is mild and generic rather than sharp. Hedged guesses are used correctly, and the Glass Throne item is a fair quiet-week filler.",
gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-17-late-strained__n-a__r1,gemma4-e2b,Minimum,news-bulletin,snap-17-late-strained,1,raw/gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-17-late-strained__n-a__r1.json,judge/v3,Model,4,0,4,"[minor] The Shattered Empire continues its expansionary maneuvers against the Ashford Compact. (ongoing activity: briefing says expanding by force and at war, but not continuing maneuvers against the Compact specifically) | [minor] until someone gets tired of the constant skirmishes (framed as a guess, but 'constant skirmishes' implies ongoing fighting the briefing does not report) | [minor] The Kestrel Tribe maintains its four settlements quietly. ('quietly' is an unreported status; briefing only gives the count) | [minor] The Bonecutter Gang remains in their two settlements. (implies an ongoing status the briefing does not report)",3,4,3,3,"It handles the quiet week acceptably by commenting on faction sizes and frames its guesses as guesses. But the wit is generic, it does not use the war or the date, and it adds minor status claims, so it falls short of Ilse's sharper voice.",
gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-17-late-strained__n-a__r2,gemma4-e2b,Minimum,news-bulletin,snap-17-late-strained,2,raw/gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-17-late-strained__n-a__r2.json,judge/v3,Model,4,0,4,"[minor] The Shattered Empire continues its expansion. (briefing says expanding by force; 'continues' implies ongoing activity as a status, mild addition) | [minor] They are preparing for whatever the Empire throws at them next. (implied purpose of the gathering, stated as fact rather than guess) | [minor] They remain an unmoving fixture in this shifting landscape. (implies unchanged status over time; briefing gives only the settlement count) | [minor] The Ashford Compact militias are reportedly gathering at Harlow Ford. (repeats old news as current, though framed as background)",3,4,3,3,"It correctly treats the week as quiet and stays within the briefing's names, but the wit is thin and generic. It also restates old news in the present tense and gives the militias a purpose the briefing never states. The Kestrel item is filler, and the sentences are choppy with little actual humor.}",
gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-17-late-strained__n-a__r3,gemma4-e2b,Minimum,news-bulletin,snap-17-late-strained,3,raw/gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-17-late-strained__n-a__r3.json,judge/v3,Model,3,0,3,"[minor] They remain a quiet entity in this volatile landscape. (quiet status of the Kestrel Tribe is not in the briefing) | [minor] They are the usual pirates, making a predictable nuisance. (ongoing activity (nuisance-making) not reported in the briefing) | [minor] The Shattered Empire continues its expansionist posture. (briefing says expanding by force; 'continues' is a mild added status, near restatement)",3,4,3,3,"Accurate to the factions and handles the quiet week as instructed, but the voice is generic and flat, with short choppy sentences and few real jokes. The Kestrel and Bonecutter items add small unsupported claims about their behavior, and the Bonecutter item offers little wit.",
gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-18-late-desperate__n-a__r1,gemma4-e2b,Minimum,news-bulletin,snap-18-late-desperate,1,raw/gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-18-late-desperate__n-a__r1.json,judge/v3,Model,4,0,4,"[minor] A Wren's Hollow caravan went missing in a blizzard (briefing says the caravan was lost, not merely missing; softened but close) | [minor] The Thistle Commonwealth has opened its granaries for access. Reaching them remains the main obstacle, as usual. (repeats old news; this was in the latest bulletin and is not in the briefing's new items) | [minor] The factions remain as they have been. (comparison with an earlier state the briefing does not give) | [minor] This is not a surprise. (stated as fact; implies expectation the briefing does not support)",2,4,3,2,"The second item repeats the previous bulletin's news as if current, and the third is a flat recital of faction counts. The voice is generic, with little earnest worry and weak, filler-like wit.",
gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-18-late-desperate__n-a__r2,gemma4-e2b,Minimum,news-bulletin,snap-18-late-desperate,2,raw/gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-18-late-desperate__n-a__r2.json,judge/v3,Model,4,0,4,"[minor] A caravan near the Wailing Moth villages was lost in a blizzard. (omits that it was a Wren's Hollow caravan; not invented, but vague. Not a fact error) | [minor] The Thistle Commonwealth has opened its granaries. Anyone can try to reach them now. (repeats old news from the latest bulletin as if new) | [minor] The Harrow Teeth are still robbing stranded travellers. (repeats old news; also asserts ongoing activity the briefing does not report) | [minor] This is just the usual business out here. (implies caravan losses are routine, which the briefing does not state)",2,3,3,2,"The lead item omits that the lost caravan was Wren's Hollow's, and two of the three items rehash old news as current. Items are also short of three sentences with a dry take, and the voice is flat rather than earnest and worried.",
gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-18-late-desperate__n-a__r3,gemma4-e2b,Minimum,news-bulletin,snap-18-late-desperate,3,raw/gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-18-late-desperate__n-a__r3.json,judge/v3,Model,6,0,6,"[minor] went missing in a blizzard (briefing says the caravan was lost, not missing; slight change of fact) | [minor] This is just another Tuesday out here. (names a weekday; the date is day 805, no weekday given, and implies this is routine) | [minor] The Thistle Commonwealth has opened its granaries. (repeats old news from the latest bulletin, presented as new) | [minor] Anyone can reach them, but getting there is the real hurdle. (repeats old news and the earlier joke about reaching the granaries) | [minor] The faction counts remain as they were. (claims no change from before, which the briefing does not report) | [minor] Harrow Teeth pirates still hold four settlements. ('still' implies a comparison with an earlier state the briefing does not give)",3,4,3,2,"The second item recycles the previous bulletin's granary news and joke as if new, which the task forbids, and the third is a flat list of faction counts. The caravan item is fine, but the piece is thin and the voice is only generic dry, not worried or earnest.}",
gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-19-late-desperate__n-a__r1,gemma4-e2b,Minimum,news-bulletin,snap-19-late-desperate,1,raw/gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-19-late-desperate__n-a__r1.json,judge/v3,Model,5,1,4,"[minor] They are currently besieging the Marrow League settlements. (implies siege of multiple settlements; briefing only says besieging the Marrow League) | [minor] The Starling Tribe remains in its four settlements. (implies ongoing status the briefing does not report (stays put)) | [minor] They offered aid to the remnants of Fenwick. (repeats old news as if current, though loosely framed as background) | [minor] It is a predictable pattern for tribes to offer temporary sanctuary. (claims a pattern and that sanctuary is temporary; stated as fact, not in briefing) | Last Lantern remains an unlisted entity in our current accounting. (Last Lantern is named in the briefing as a faction at war with the Sun Throne; calling it unlisted contradicts it)",3,3,3,2,"The output misreads Last Lantern as unlisted when the briefing names it as at war with the Sun Throne, and the third item is empty filler. The Starling item rehashes old news with a dubious generalisation, and the wit is thin, so it is not ready to ship.
",
gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-19-late-desperate__n-a__r2,gemma4-e2b,Minimum,news-bulletin,snap-19-late-desperate,2,raw/gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-19-late-desperate__n-a__r2.json,judge/v3,Model,4,0,4,"[minor] They have razed Fenwick and are currently besieging the Marrow League. (repeats old news: the razing of Fenwick was already covered, presented here as fresh) | [minor] They offered sanctuary to the remnants of Fenwick. (repeats old news from an earlier bulletin, presented as current) | [minor] The Marrow League remains at three settlements. (repeats old news about the League being down to three, and 'remains' implies an ongoing status) | [minor] One assumes this relentless approach will yield predictable results. ('relentless' adds characterisation, though the sentence is framed as a guess so it barely counts)",3,4,3,3,"The bulletin is clear and accurate to the briefing, but two of its three items rehash old news as current, and the wit is generic rather than sardonic. The third item is padding with no new fact and no real joke.",
gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-19-late-desperate__n-a__r3,gemma4-e2b,Minimum,news-bulletin,snap-19-late-desperate,3,raw/gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-19-late-desperate__n-a__r3.json,judge/v3,Model,4,0,4,"[minor] They have razed Fenwick and are now besieging the Marrow League. (repeats old news: the razing of Fenwick was already covered, though it is paired with the new siege and not presented as a fresh event) | [minor] This dwindling number suggests a steady decline, which is hardly surprising. (inference stated as fact; the briefing gives no steady decline, only the count of three (the earlier bulletin mentions seven at the start of the year, but this is not the writer's own framing)) | [minor] The Starling Tribe remains a minor player. (status claim not in briefing, stated as fact) | [minor] now they simply exist. (ongoing status the briefing does not report)",2,4,2,2,"The bulletin is clear and uses its facts accurately, but the voice is flat and generic with little sardonic wit, and it pads a third item with the Tribe's offer of aid, which is old news. The dry remarks are weak and the Last Lantern war is ignored.",
gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-20-late-strained__n-a__r1,gemma4-e2b,Minimum,news-bulletin,snap-20-late-strained,1,raw/gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-20-late-strained__n-a__r1.json,judge/v3,Model,3,0,3,[minor] This is hardly a surprise in these parts. (stated as fact; implies a pattern of such offers the briefing does not give) | [minor] They remain stubbornly separate from the larger squabbles. (ongoing status/neutrality not in briefing; stated as fact) | [minor] It is a predictable cycle of conflict. (implies earlier wars or a repeating pattern not in briefing),3,4,3,3,"Leads correctly with the governorship offer and mostly stays within the briefing, but the Tribe's ""stubbornly separate"" stance is asserted as fact, and the wit is generic with little of the sharpness of the earlier bulletins. The last item is padding, and ""manage both sides simultaneously"" is muddled.",
gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-20-late-strained__n-a__r2,gemma4-e2b,Minimum,news-bulletin,snap-20-late-strained,2,raw/gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-20-late-strained__n-a__r2.json,judge/v3,Model,3,0,3,"[minor] They remain stubbornly separate from the larger conflicts. (ongoing status not in briefing; tribe's neutrality stated as fact) | [minor] The Free Coast Alliance continues to hold its two towns. (repeats old news as an ongoing status) | [minor] the inevitable skirmishes (implies skirmishes near Varrowgate and presents inevitability as fact, not in briefing)",3,4,3,3,"It leads correctly with the governorship offer and hedges its guesses, but the wit is mild and generic, and it adds unsupported status claims (Tribe aloof from conflicts, skirmishes) while recycling the Alliance's two towns as a third item.",
gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-20-late-strained__n-a__r3,gemma4-e2b,Minimum,news-bulletin,snap-20-late-strained,3,raw/gemma4-e2b__news-bulletin__snap-20-late-strained__n-a__r3.json,judge/v3,Model,3,0,3,[minor] This is hardly a surprise in these parts. (implied context/inference stated as fact; briefing gives no basis that such offers are expected) | [minor] They remain stubbornly separate from the larger squabbles. (ongoing status not in briefing; tribe's neutrality is not reported) | [minor] The Free Coast Alliance holds two towns. Their resolve remains as predictable as the tide. (repeats old news; the two-towns item was in the earlier bulletin and is presented as current news; resolve is a repeat of the earlier joke),3,4,3,3,"The lead item is correct and in order, but the second and third items pad with old or unreported material (the Alliance's two towns were already covered, and the Tribe's aloofness is added). The wit is mild and partly recycles the earlier bulletin's resolve joke, and the Governorship item is too thin to carry the piece.",
gemma4-e2b__inheritance-handoff__snap-09-mid-desperate__n-a__r1,gemma4-e2b,Minimum,inheritance-handoff,snap-09-mid-desperate,1,raw/gemma4-e2b__inheritance-handoff__snap-09-mid-desperate__n-a__r1.json,judge/v3,Model,4,2,2,"Tamsin stood by the charred remains of their shared gear. (charred shared gear is an invented object/event not in the briefing) | The silence of the Lancers' camp pressed in. (places Tamsin at the Lancers' camp, where Joska died, which the briefing does not do) | [minor] She traced the rough texture of the broken weapon (broken weapon is an added detail tied to the fight, not given in the briefing) | [minor] Lene’s face, etched with exhaustion, was visible in the shadows. (places Lene at the scene at the camp; exhaustion is added detail)",3,3,3,2,"The scene puts Tamsin at the Lancers' camp, where her father died, and adds charred gear. It never shows the handoff of the story, and it ends on a vague hunt rather than a clear intent such as the new captain's revenge on Cinder Rest. The prose is generic and tells more than it shows.",
gemma4-e2b__inheritance-handoff__snap-09-mid-desperate__n-a__r2,gemma4-e2b,Minimum,inheritance-handoff,snap-09-mid-desperate,2,raw/gemma4-e2b__inheritance-handoff__snap-09-mid-desperate__n-a__r2.json,judge/v3,Model,4,1,3,"remembering the fight, the final clash (puts Tamsin at or witnessing the fight; briefing does not place her there) | [minor] worn leather of her father’s coat (new object (coat) not in briefing, though plausible staging) | [minor] She walked toward the camp entrance (camp is held by Lancers; implies she goes there, a plot move not in the briefing, but it is her intent) | [minor] deep gouges on the material (added detail about how the fight looked)",3,3,3,3,"Competent and restrained, but it implies Tamsin remembers the fight, and the ending is a vague intent (find out what the captain plans) rather than a clear resolve. It also doesn't use the father-daughter relationship or her hot temper much. The word count is also below 60, which breaks the rules.",
gemma4-e2b__inheritance-handoff__snap-09-mid-desperate__n-a__r3,gemma4-e2b,Minimum,inheritance-handoff,snap-09-mid-desperate,3,raw/gemma4-e2b__inheritance-handoff__snap-09-mid-desperate__n-a__r3.json,judge/v3,Model,4,1,3,"where Malley’s crew had fled (briefing says the Lancers still hold the camp; no crew fled, contradicts the story) | [minor] The Lancers’ camp was silent now, only the wind whistling through broken timbers. (camp is still held by Lancers; empty silent ruin contradicts or embellishes the situation) | [minor] charred remains of the fight (added detail about the past fight not in briefing) | [minor] She traced the outline of where her father fell (places Tamsin at the fight site as if the body fell there; unsupported past detail)",3,3,3,2,"The scene contradicts the briefing by showing the Lancers' camp empty and Malley's crew fled, when the Lancers still hold it. It also ends on vague scavenging rather than a clear intent to avenge Joska or face the new captain, so it misses the moment.",
gemma4-e2b__inheritance-handoff__snap-16-late-desperate__n-a__r1,gemma4-e2b,Minimum,inheritance-handoff,snap-16-late-desperate,1,raw/gemma4-e2b__inheritance-handoff__snap-16-late-desperate__n-a__r1.json,judge/v3,Model,3,0,3,"[minor] the scorched remains of the last hunting ground (scorched remains and broken timber are not in the briefing; the ambush site is not described and nothing says Elske is there) | [minor] Bertram’s empty saddle (a saddle is not mentioned; Rook the warg came home alone, but nothing says there was a saddle) | [minor] where the threat still lingered (implies Dunmore's ongoing presence nearby; the briefing says only that he escaped)",3,4,3,3,"Clear and ends on her intent to track Dunmore, but it is generic and leans on stock phrases ('settled in her chest like cold stone', 'the careful shooter in her steady hands'). It also does not use the best-friend bond or the warg Rook, and it invents setting details.",
gemma4-e2b__inheritance-handoff__snap-16-late-desperate__n-a__r2,gemma4-e2b,Minimum,inheritance-handoff,snap-16-late-desperate,2,raw/gemma4-e2b__inheritance-handoff__snap-16-late-desperate__n-a__r2.json,judge/v3,Model,2,1,1,"Elske found the body near the northern ridge. (the northern ridge is a place the briefing does not name, and the briefing does not say Elske found the body) | [minor] where the threat still lingered (implies Dunmore's ongoing presence nearby, which the briefing only says escaped)",3,4,3,3,"The scene is clear and restrained and ends on Elske's intent to hunt Dunmore, but it invents a location and her finding the body, and it is generic with little that shows their friendship or uses Rook or the hunts.",
gemma4-e2b__inheritance-handoff__snap-16-late-desperate__n-a__r3,gemma4-e2b,Minimum,inheritance-handoff,snap-16-late-desperate,3,raw/gemma4-e2b__inheritance-handoff__snap-16-late-desperate__n-a__r3.json,judge/v3,ModelRetry,4,2,2,"Elske stood by the wreckage of the last hunt. (places her at the site of the ambush; the briefing never says she was there or that wreckage existed) | She traced the scorched earth where Bertram had fallen. (invents scorched earth and a known place where Bertram fell; the briefing gives no location or fire) | [minor] Rook whined, nudging her hand. (Rook came home alone, so having Rook at the site contradicts the staging; it is a questionable detail) | [minor] picking up a piece of torn fabric, its color faded (adds an object tied to the past event that the briefing does not mention)",3,3,3,2,"The scene places Elske and Rook at the ambush site and adds scorched earth, which changes the story (Rook came home alone). The prose is generic and the ending is flat, though it does end on her intent to hunt Dunmore.",
gemma4-e2b__inheritance-handoff__snap-18-late-desperate__n-a__r1,gemma4-e2b,Minimum,inheritance-handoff,snap-18-late-desperate,1,raw/gemma4-e2b__inheritance-handoff__snap-18-late-desperate__n-a__r1.json,judge/v3,Model,2,0,2,"[minor] The memory of the blizzard, the loss of the caravan, settled in his chest like a stone. (implies Elias remembers the blizzard as if present; briefing does not place him there, but it is framed as memory/figure of speech) | [minor] the cold, empty space where his mother used to sit (added detail about his mother's habit of sitting there; not in briefing)",3,4,3,3,"Accurate to the briefing and ends on a clear intent to reach Ada, but it is generic and names feeling directly (""anxiety tightening his jaw"", a stone in his chest). The relationship is only implied through 'his mother', and the moment of inheriting the story lacks a distinct image.",
gemma4-e2b__inheritance-handoff__snap-18-late-desperate__n-a__r2,gemma4-e2b,Minimum,inheritance-handoff,snap-18-late-desperate,2,raw/gemma4-e2b__inheritance-handoff__snap-18-late-desperate__n-a__r2.json,judge/v3,Model,1,0,1,"[minor] He needed to secure the perimeter, make sure nothing else could be lost. (states the heir's intent as securing the colony, which the briefing does not give; it ignores Ada and the caravan story)",3,4,3,3,"The scene is clear and restrained, and the letter and cold are used well. But it ends on checking wall seals rather than taking up his mother's story (Ada still in the village), so the handoff is not landed and the ending feels disconnected.",
gemma4-e2b__inheritance-handoff__snap-18-late-desperate__n-a__r3,gemma4-e2b,Minimum,inheritance-handoff,snap-18-late-desperate,3,raw/gemma4-e2b__inheritance-handoff__snap-18-late-desperate__n-a__r3.json,judge/v3,Model,3,1,2,"The memory of the blizzard, the loss of the caravan, settled heavy in his chest. (puts Elias at or in memory of the blizzard; the briefing does not say he was there, and 'memory' implies he witnessed it) | [minor] searching for any trace of the lost journey (adds an action and purpose not in the briefing, implying the lost caravan could be traced via manifests) | [minor] supply manifests (invents a specific record that the briefing does not mention)",3,3,3,3,"The scene uses the letter and the Day 744 date correctly and ends on a clear intent (find Ada), but it names a feeling outright ('settled heavy in his chest') and claims Elias remembers the blizzard. The ending drifts into checking manifests instead of going to the Wailing Moth village, and the wrench feels random.",
gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-01-early-content__n-a__r1,gemma4-e4b,Recommended,news-bulletin,snap-01-early-content,1,raw/gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-01-early-content__n-a__r1.json,judge/v3,Model,4,0,4,"[minor] The settlement counts remain unchanged. (comparison with an earlier state the briefing does not give; first bulletin, no prior counts) | [minor] The Tarn Union holds six posts. (briefing says 6 settlements, not trading posts; also unclear whether it includes the new one) | [minor] The Clans still claim four. ('still' implies ongoing status or comparison the briefing does not give) | [minor] It's a predictable expansion, really. (implies earlier expansions, a comparison not in the briefing, stated as fact)",3,4,3,3,"Readable and mostly faithful, but the 'unchanged' and 'still' claims imply a prior state that doesn't exist in a first bulletin, and the jokes are generic. The third item is also thin and the closing line is flat.",
gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-01-early-content__n-a__r2,gemma4-e4b,Recommended,news-bulletin,snap-01-early-content,2,raw/gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-01-early-content__n-a__r2.json,judge/v3,Model,2,0,2,"[minor] has tacked on another trading post ('another' implies earlier posts; briefing only says a new post opened, and this is the first bulletin) | [minor] The expansion suggests a belief in endless commerce (inference about motive stated as fact, not framed as a guess)",4,4,4,3,"The dry voice is consistent and the guesses are mostly well framed, but the first item states an inferred motive as fact. The bulletin is also short of the required 70 words and the three-sentence minimum per paragraph is barely met, so it should not ship unchanged.",
gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-01-early-content__n-a__r3,gemma4-e4b,Recommended,news-bulletin,snap-01-early-content,3,raw/gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-01-early-content__n-a__r3.json,judge/v3,Model,1,0,1,"[minor] A remarkably stable arrangement, I suppose. (implies the faction arrangement is stable, which the briefing does not say; hedged only by 'I suppose')",3,4,3,3,"Facts are accurate and the guesses are properly hedged, but the wit is thin and repetitive, and the third item only restates faction numbers. The second item's livestock remark is a hedged guess, but the first paragraph's 'more places' joke is circular and weak.</br>",
gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-02-early-content__n-a__r1,gemma4-e4b,Recommended,news-bulletin,snap-02-early-content,1,raw/gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-02-early-content__n-a__r1.json,judge/v3,Model,3,0,3,"[minor] The Tannerfolk are still engaged in their usual skirmishes with the pirates over that same stretch of flats. (ongoing activity ('still', 'usual skirmishes') not reported; briefing only says war and earlier fighting over the flats) | [minor] It has been a remarkably dull week in the Rim. (stated as fact; the briefing gives no information on how quiet the week was) | [minor] The Glimmer Coast Company maintains its five settlements. (ongoing status 'maintains' is not reported, though the count is given)",3,4,3,3,"Accurate on the numbers and leads with the new item, but the wit is thin and generic, and the second item is mostly a flat recitation of faction sizes. It also adds mild unsupported claims like 'usual skirmishes' and 'dull week'. It is short of the 70-word minimum and the items lack real dry takes.",
gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-02-early-content__n-a__r2,gemma4-e4b,Recommended,news-bulletin,snap-02-early-content,2,raw/gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-02-early-content__n-a__r2.json,judge/v3,Model,3,0,3,"[minor] The Tannerfolk still hold ground (ongoing status not in briefing; implies Tannerfolk hold territory on the flats) | [minor] The Glimmer Coast Company, meanwhile, reports another profitable week. (repeats old news from the latest bulletin as if current; the briefing gives no such report) | [minor] As of day 11, the Tannerfolk and the Hollow Spire Pirates continue their dispute over the salt flats. (repeats old news and states it as ongoing without briefing support)",3,4,3,3,"It leads correctly with the abandoned camp and frames its guesses as guesses, but the second item is mostly recycled old news, including the Company's profitable week, which the briefing doesn't support. The wit is mild and generic, and the second paragraph is padded with stated-as-fact status claims.",
gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-02-early-content__n-a__r3,gemma4-e4b,Recommended,news-bulletin,snap-02-early-content,3,raw/gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-02-early-content__n-a__r3.json,judge/v3,Model,2,0,2,"[minor] They are still fighting, which is predictable given the geography. (ongoing activity stated as fact; the briefing says they are at war but not that fighting continues now) | [minor] The Tannerfolk continue their war with the Hollow Spire Pirates over the flats. (repeats old news as an ongoing state; the war itself is in the briefing, but the continuation over the flats is old news presented as current)",3,4,3,3,"Accurate on the lead item and the guesses are framed correctly, but the second paragraph mostly repeats old news and the jokes are weak. The Glimmer Coast quip is muddled, and the 'company' reference is unclear. It reads generic rather than distinctly dry or wry.",
gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-03-early-strained__n-a__r1,gemma4-e4b,Recommended,news-bulletin,snap-03-early-strained,1,raw/gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-03-early-strained__n-a__r1.json,judge/v3,Model,3,0,3,[minor] The Merrow Freeholds continue their slow migration across seven settlements. ('slow migration' is an ongoing activity the briefing does not report; settlements are not migrating) | [minor] The Kinn of the Long Grass hold three settlements in the area. ('in the area' is an added location; the briefing gives no placement for the settlements) | [minor] The Ashen Hand maintain their presence across four settlements. ('maintain their presence' implies an ongoing status not in the briefing),3,4,3,3,"It correctly treats a quiet week by commenting on faction sizes and frames its guesses as guesses, but the wit is thin and generic, and 'slow migration' and 'in the area' add small unsupported details. The item on pairs of caravans repeats old news only as background, which is acceptable, though the closing line on the Kinn is weak.",
gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-03-early-strained__n-a__r2,gemma4-e4b,Recommended,news-bulletin,snap-03-early-strained,2,raw/gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-03-early-strained__n-a__r2.json,judge/v3,Model,5,0,5,"[minor] Another day passes in Kettle Hollow. (implies the reporter is in or knows the colony's daily life; briefing says she knows nothing of the inside) | [minor] It is day 23 of this current cycle. ('cycle' is not the briefing's term; the date is Jugust 5500, day 23) | [minor] They remain in their established patterns. (ongoing status of the Kinn stated as fact; the briefing gives none, and the earlier bulletin said they were on the move) | [minor] Their caravans continue their paired journeys. (repeats old news as an ongoing status the briefing does not report) | [minor] The Ashen Hand still command four settlements. ('still' implies a comparison with an earlier state, which the briefing does not give)",3,4,3,3,"It stays close to the briefing and frames its guesses as guesses, but it is dry rather than witty, the sentences are flat and repetitive, and some of its status claims (the Kinn's 'established patterns', the ongoing paired caravans) go beyond what the briefing says. At roughly 90 words it is acceptable but bland.",
gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-03-early-strained__n-a__r3,gemma4-e4b,Recommended,news-bulletin,snap-03-early-strained,3,raw/gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-03-early-strained__n-a__r3.json,judge/v3,Model,4,0,4,"[minor] The Merrow Freeholds continue their slow migration across seven settlements. (migration is not in the briefing; implies ongoing activity not reported) | [minor] They are still travelling in pairs, I hear. (repeats old news as an ongoing status; 'still' is not supported) | [minor] The Kinn of the Long Grass hold their ground in three settlements. (implies a status ('hold their ground') the briefing does not report, and ignores the earlier bulletin that they were on the move) | [minor] Another day dawns on Kettle Hollow. (implies coverage of the colony, which the briefing says the reporter knows nothing about; mild filler)",3,4,3,3,"Competent and clear, and it leans on the faction sizes for a quiet week as instructed, but the wit is thin and generic. Several small additions (migration, 'still', 'hold their ground') go beyond the briefing, and the Kinn line contradicts their earlier move.",
gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-04-early-strained__n-a__r1,gemma4-e4b,Recommended,news-bulletin,snap-04-early-strained,1,raw/gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-04-early-strained__n-a__r1.json,judge/v3,Model,3,1,2,Such dramatic flair for a Tuesday. (briefing gives no day of the week; Tuesday is an invented date) | [minor] Tomas Quell. One assumes he hasn't simply decided to become a hermit. (none) | [minor] With the Brine Coast League maintaining their usual six settlements ('usual' and 'maintaining' imply a past state and ongoing activity not in the briefing),3,4,3,2,"The dry voice is serviceable, but 'Tuesday' is an invented date and the League line implies an unreported earlier state. The bulletin also falls short of three sentences per item and is likely under the word count, and its jokes are thin.",
gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-04-early-strained__n-a__r2,gemma4-e4b,Recommended,news-bulletin,snap-04-early-strained,2,raw/gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-04-early-strained__n-a__r2.json,judge/v3,Model,2,0,2,"[minor] Meanwhile, the Black Fen Raiders decided to torch a ferry ('decided' implies deliberate intent; mild embellishment of 'burned a ferry') | [minor] It seems they are still very dedicated to maritime sabotage. (implies an ongoing pattern of sabotage the briefing does not report, though hedged with 'it seems')",3,4,3,3,"Accurate to the briefing with no major inventions and a passable dry voice, but it falls short of the length (about 70 words is borderline) and the 3-sentence-per-item requirement, and the jokes are mild. The second item is thin, and the 'Lowmere has seen a halt in coverage' framing is clumsy.",
gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-04-early-strained__n-a__r3,gemma4-e4b,Recommended,news-bulletin,snap-04-early-strained,3,raw/gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-04-early-strained__n-a__r3.json,judge/v3,Model,3,0,3,"[minor] Tomas Quell has gone silent. (briefing says only that the Dispatch is looking for news of him; 'gone silent' is an added status stated as fact) | [minor] The Black Fen Raiders took a taste of the water. (figurative but implies raiders did something beyond burning the ferry; mostly colour, slight added framing) | [minor] It suggests things there have become decidedly uninteresting, or perhaps quite dangerous. (implied cause of the Dispatch's withdrawal, though loosely hedged as a suggestion)",3,4,3,3,"It stays faithful to the three briefing items and hedges its guesses, but the wit is mild and generic, and the first item's 'gone silent' adds an unsupported status. The Tuesday joke and 'taste of the water' are clumsy, and the piece falls short of the word count and leaves some paragraphs with fewer than 3 distinct sentences of fact and take.",
gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-05-early-desperate__n-a__r1,gemma4-e4b,Recommended,news-bulletin,snap-05-early-desperate,1,raw/gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-05-early-desperate__n-a__r1.json,judge/v3,Model,3,0,3,"[minor] The Scythe Tooth continue their opportunistic raids. (ongoing activity not reported in briefing; repeats old news as current) | [minor] They have hit three settlements in a quadrum, which is hardly a surprising development. (repeats old news as if current; 'in a quadrum' comes from earlier bulletin, not the briefing) | [minor] The Ferrow Mutual seems to be managing the resulting patrols (repeats old news; patrol arrangement framed as ongoing status, hedged only with 'seems')",3,4,3,3,"The lead item is accurate and the guess is properly hedged, but the second paragraph rehashes old raids and patrols as ongoing, and the second item is padded with little new wit. The first item is also only two real sentences of take, and the piece is thin on the dry voice.",
gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-05-early-desperate__n-a__r2,gemma4-e4b,Recommended,news-bulletin,snap-05-early-desperate,2,raw/gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-05-early-desperate__n-a__r2.json,judge/v3,Model,3,0,3,"[minor] Their decision leaves the usual trade routes rather sparse this cycle. (implied consequence of the closure not given in briefing) | [minor] The Scythe Tooth continue their sporadic raids. (ongoing activity not reported in briefing; also 'sporadic' is an added characterisation) | [minor] the current low activity is merely a lull between endeavors (guess framed with 'I suspect' but 'current low activity' is stated as fact, with no basis in briefing)",2,3,2,2,"The bulletin is generic and mostly lacks Odile's sardonic wit, with only faint dry remarks. It also pads with unsupported claims (ongoing raids, sparse trade routes) and has only two thin items that don't meet the three-sentence, wry-take brief well.
",
gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-05-early-desperate__n-a__r3,gemma4-e4b,Recommended,news-bulletin,snap-05-early-desperate,3,raw/gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-05-early-desperate__n-a__r3.json,judge/v3,Model,2,0,2,"[minor] The Scythe Tooth continue their pattern of raids, hitting three settlements in a quadrum. (repeats old news as ongoing; presents the earlier raids as a continuing pattern, which the briefing does not report) | [minor] It certainly makes trade more complicated for those of us who rely on a steady flow of goods. (added consequence and claim about the narrator's reliance on trade, not in the briefing)",3,4,3,3,"It leads correctly with the market closure and frames its cause as a guess, but the second item recycles old raid news as ongoing. The wit is mild and the text is a little short of the required length and sentence count per item, so it is acceptable but bland.",
gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-06-early-content__n-a__r1,gemma4-e4b,Recommended,news-bulletin,snap-06-early-content,1,raw/gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-06-early-content__n-a__r1.json,judge/v3,Model,4,0,4,"[minor] The Calder Combine maintains its five settlements are thriving. (repeats old news and adds a claim about thriving settlements the briefing does not give (only that harvests are good)) | [minor] They claim good harvests continue along the delta. (repeats old news as an ongoing present claim, implying continuation) | [minor] One assumes the pirates found the cargo more appealing than the Calder Combine’s reported bounty. (guess framed as such, but implies the barge was Calder's; the briefing does not say whose barge it was) | [minor] the usual low-level thievery (implies a pattern of past petty theft the briefing does not give)",3,3,3,3,"The first item is accurate and the dry guesses are properly framed. The second item repeats the harvest news as a fresh claim and adds that the settlements are thriving, which the briefing does not support. The piece also ignores the Empire and the date, and the pirate item is thin, so it feels padded.",
gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-06-early-content__n-a__r2,gemma4-e4b,Recommended,news-bulletin,snap-06-early-content,2,raw/gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-06-early-content__n-a__r2.json,judge/v3,Model,2,0,2,"[minor] The Calder Combine maintains its five settlements, apparently content with their current state of affairs. (implies ongoing status and contentment the briefing does not report; the 'apparently' hedge softens it) | [minor] It seems even the Combine's bounty is a tempting target for petty brigands. (implies the barge belonged to the Combine, which the briefing does not say; hedged with 'It seems' but still an implied owner)",4,4,4,3,"The dry voice fits and the barge item is mostly accurate, with guesses properly hedged. But the second paragraph is thin and mostly restates faction sizes, and the item implies the Combine owned the barge without support. The report also has only two paragraphs and runs short of the requested length and sentence count per item.",
gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-06-early-content__n-a__r3,gemma4-e4b,Recommended,news-bulletin,snap-06-early-content,3,raw/gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-06-early-content__n-a__r3.json,judge/v3,Model,3,0,3,"[minor] The Calder Combine still boasts five settlements in the region. (""in the region"" is not in the briefing, and ""still"" implies an unreported ongoing status) | [minor] It seems even the Combine's bountiful harvests are a tempting target for petty thievery. (implies the barge carried the Combine's harvest, which the briefing does not say; hedged with ""it seems"" but links the two items as cause) | [minor] The Sundered Throne maintains its three quiet strongholds. (""strongholds"" is an added detail; the briefing gives only settlements and ""quiet behind its walls"")",3,3,3,3,"The voice is dry but generic, and it ties the robbery to the Combine's harvest without the briefing's support. The second paragraph restates faction sizes without much wit, and the ""relieve a grain barge"" phrasing is slightly muddy. It also falls short of the 70-word minimum.",
gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-07-mid-strained__n-a__r1,gemma4-e4b,Recommended,news-bulletin,snap-07-mid-strained,1,raw/gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-07-mid-strained__n-a__r1.json,judge/v3,Model,2,0,2,"[minor] They seem to be weathering the Imperial demands, for now. (hedged with 'seem', but implies an ongoing status of the Covenant the briefing does not report) | [minor] It is a quiet week (the briefing has a new item, so calling it a quiet week is an inference stated as fact)",3,4,3,3,"Accurate to the briefing and clear, but the wit is thin and generic, and the second item pads with faction size and a vague 'quiet week' claim. It lacks the sharp absurd eye of the earlier bulletins and runs short of the required sentence count for the first item.",
gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-07-mid-strained__n-a__r2,gemma4-e4b,Recommended,news-bulletin,snap-07-mid-strained,2,raw/gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-07-mid-strained__n-a__r2.json,judge/v3,Model,3,0,3,"[minor] squeeze a few extra credits out of the local traffic (framed as a guess (""One assumes""), but ""credits"" is not RimWorld vocabulary here (silver); only a guess, so minor at most) | [minor] they are certainly keeping busy (implies an ongoing activity the briefing does not report) | [minor] the loss of that wagon earlier seems to have settled into the background noise (implied consequence about how the loss was received; hedged but stated as the narrator's impression of the Covenant's state)",3,4,3,3,"Accurate and readable, with no major invented facts, but the dry voice is generic and the second item is padding about faction size. It is also thin on wit, at about 90 words with only two sentences of real take per item, and the ""credits"" word feels off for the setting.",
gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-07-mid-strained__n-a__r3,gemma4-e4b,Recommended,news-bulletin,snap-07-mid-strained,3,raw/gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-07-mid-strained__n-a__r3.json,judge/v3,Model,2,0,2,"[minor] They are still managing their affairs after the wagon incident. (ongoing status not in briefing; implies consequence of wagon loss) | [minor] The Iron Covenant remains at eight settlements. (""remains"" implies comparison with an earlier state the briefing does not give)",3,4,3,3,"Accurate on the main fact and guesses are framed as guesses, but it is only two thin items, the wit is generic (""monetize every patch of dirt"" is modern-office language), and the second item adds unsupported status about the Covenant. It also falls short of the minimum three sentences per item and the word count is low.",
gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-08-mid-content__n-a__r1,gemma4-e4b,Recommended,news-bulletin,snap-08-mid-content,1,raw/gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-08-mid-content__n-a__r1.json,judge/v3,Model,3,0,3,"[minor] is now the main attraction at Lantern Hill (briefing says traders talk about it, not that it is the main attraction; framed with 'It seems' but then stated as fact in follow-up) | [minor] Traders are certainly making a fuss over it. (restates talk as a fuss, stated as certain; mild embellishment) | [minor] remains stubbornly unchanged this week (implies comparison with earlier state the briefing does not give; framed as 'It appears' so weak)",3,4,3,3,"Accurate on the faction numbers and sticks to the briefing, but it is short of the 70-word minimum, the wit is mild and generic, and each item has only about three thin sentences, so the dry voice barely lands.",
gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-08-mid-content__n-a__r2,gemma4-e4b,Recommended,news-bulletin,snap-08-mid-content,2,raw/gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-08-mid-content__n-a__r2.json,judge/v3,Model,3,0,3,"[minor] The Lantern Accord continues its trade fair at Lantern Hill. (repeats old news; ongoing status ('continues') not in briefing, which only says it is hosting) | [minor] They still insist on fair prices, which is a bold claim in this economy. (repeats old news; 'still insist' is an ongoing status and 'this economy' implies a condition the briefing does not give) | [minor] The jade sculpture from Gladwater is currently drawing the attention of Lantern Hill traders. ('currently' adds ongoing status; briefing says it is the talk of traders)",3,4,3,3,"Clean and readable, with a dry voice, but the second item is old news dressed as an ongoing update, and the output is short of the 70-word minimum and its items are thin on the fact-then-take structure. The jokes are mild and the 'Accord council wisdom' jab is generic.",
gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-08-mid-content__n-a__r3,gemma4-e4b,Recommended,news-bulletin,snap-08-mid-content,3,raw/gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-08-mid-content__n-a__r3.json,judge/v3,Model,2,0,2,"[minor] even amidst the Accord’s trade fair, shiny trinkets manage to steal the spotlight (implies the sculpture is the fair's main draw, a cause or consequence the briefing does not give) | [minor] The Lantern Accord maintains nine settlements, while the Reedmother's Children hold five. (repeats faction sizes as a quiet-week filler although a new item exists; a mild padding, but the numbers are correct)",3,4,3,3,"Facts are mostly accurate and guesses are properly hedged, but the wit is thin and generic. The second item is padding and misses the Ninefingers failed-raid background; the paragraphs are also shorter than the three-sentence requirement in spirit and the word count is likely below 70.",
gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-09-mid-desperate__n-a__r1,gemma4-e4b,Recommended,news-bulletin,snap-09-mid-desperate,1,raw/gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-09-mid-desperate__n-a__r1.json,judge/v3,Model,2,0,2,"[minor] The Embertail Tribe continues its hostilities with the Gray Wharf Syndicate. (ongoing activity beyond the briefing; the briefing says only that they are at war) | [minor] It seems the fishing rights dispute is proving quite persistent. (fishing rights come from an earlier bulletin, not the briefing; persistence is an added status, though hedged with 'it seems')",3,4,3,3,"Accurate on the main fact and the guess is properly hedged, but the item is short and the wit is thin: the second item mostly repeats old news as a continuing story, and it comes in under the 70-word minimum. The voice is only mildly sardonic and has little of the earlier bulletins' eye for the absurd.",
gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-09-mid-desperate__n-a__r2,gemma4-e4b,Recommended,news-bulletin,snap-09-mid-desperate,2,raw/gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-09-mid-desperate__n-a__r2.json,judge/v3,Model,2,0,2,"[minor] The Embertail Tribe continues its hostilities with the Gray Wharf Syndicate. (ongoing status; briefing only says at war, so ""continues hostilities"" is a mild extension of the war fact) | [minor] It seems the fishing rights dispute shows no sign of resolution. (repeats old news (fishing rights from earlier bulletin; not in this briefing) framed as hedged inference of no resolution)",3,4,3,3,"Accurate and clear, but it is thin: the first item is only two plain sentences plus a mild quip, and the second item rehashes the war as if current news. Each paragraph falls short of the three-sentence minimum on wit, and the total length is below the 70-word minimum, so the sardonic voice never really shows.",
gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-09-mid-desperate__n-a__r3,gemma4-e4b,Recommended,news-bulletin,snap-09-mid-desperate,3,raw/gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-09-mid-desperate__n-a__r3.json,judge/v3,Model,3,0,3,"[minor] He was found at his own camp. (briefing says he was killed at his camp, not found; also omits killing and implies discovery) | [minor] The Embertail Tribe continues its hostilities with the Gray Wharf Syndicate. (ongoing activity beyond briefing, which only says at war; repeats old news as current state) | [minor] It seems the fishing rights dispute has settled into a rather predictable stalemate. (stalemate is an inference; hedged with 'it seems' but the 'fishing rights' cause comes from an earlier bulletin, not the briefing's facts)",3,3,3,3,"The bulletin is accurate in the main but flat: it says 'found' rather than killed, drops the dry wit the persona demands, and pads the second item with old war news framed as a stalemate. Items are short of three sentences each in spirit and the humor is thin.",
gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-10-mid-strained__n-a__r1,gemma4-e4b,Recommended,news-bulletin,snap-10-mid-strained,1,raw/gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-10-mid-strained__n-a__r1.json,judge/v3,Model,3,0,3,"[minor] The Weir Federation continues its bounty hunt (ongoing activity not reported; briefing only says a bounty was raised) | [minor] The Ochre Hand still fights the Stonecutter Raiders. (ongoing activity; briefing says only that they are at war, not that fighting continues) | [minor] Or perhaps they just need the coin for something less noble. (muddled guess; the Ochre Hand is paying silver, not receiving it, so the remark contradicts the offer)",3,3,3,3,"Reasonably dry, but it is short of the required length and paragraph structure, and the joke about needing the coin makes no sense since the Ochre Hand is paying. It also repeats old news as ongoing activity and says nothing about the Stonecutters' captives or the faction sizes.",
gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-10-mid-strained__n-a__r2,gemma4-e4b,Recommended,news-bulletin,snap-10-mid-strained,2,raw/gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-10-mid-strained__n-a__r2.json,judge/v3,Model,2,0,2,"[minor] They maintain their bounty on the Stonecutter leaders. (repeats old news; presents the earlier bounty as an ongoing status the briefing does not report) | [minor] however temporary that truce might be (implies a truce exists or is being sought; the briefing reports only a silver offer, not a truce)",3,4,3,3,"The dry voice is acceptable and the lead item is correct and framed as a guess, but it is thin on wit. The second item reuses the old bounty news and the first implies a truce the briefing never mentions.",
gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-10-mid-strained__n-a__r3,gemma4-e4b,Recommended,news-bulletin,snap-10-mid-strained,3,raw/gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-10-mid-strained__n-a__r3.json,judge/v3,Model,3,0,3,"[minor] the skirmishes continue between the Ochre Hand and the Stonecutter Raiders (ongoing activity not reported; briefing only says they are at war) | [minor] The Raiders maintain their hold on the prisoners, naturally. (repeats old news as current status (though briefing's earlier bulletin says holding captives)) | [minor] the cycle of raiding and negotiation (implies a repeated pattern of negotiation not in briefing)",3,4,3,3,"Accurate lead item and a mostly dry voice, but the second item pads with old news and an unreported 'skirmishes continue', and the wit is mild. The first item's second sentence just restates the first, and the whole piece is short of the paragraph length requested.",
gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-11-mid-content__n-a__r1,gemma4-e4b,Recommended,news-bulletin,snap-11-mid-content,1,raw/gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-11-mid-content__n-a__r1.json,judge/v3,Model,4,1,3,"The Mire Rats remain confined to their two settlements. (briefing says only that they have 2 settlements and were driven from the eastern marsh; 'confined' and ongoing status are invented) | [minor] The Hearthguard Compact still offers prizes for new inventions. (repeats old news as an ongoing status the briefing does not confirm) | [minor] It is a quiet week, which in rim terms usually means something is brewing just out of sight. (claims a quiet week while a new item exists, and states a generalization about brewing trouble as fact) | [minor] the usual posturing has temporarily paused (implies prior posturing between the factions; framed as a guess but asserts a prior state)",3,4,3,2,"The dry voice is serviceable, but the claim that the Mire Rats are 'confined' to their two settlements is a new, unsupported fact. The second item mostly rehashes old news, and the bulletin runs short of the three-sentence-per-item brief and has weak wit.}",
gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-11-mid-content__n-a__r2,gemma4-e4b,Recommended,news-bulletin,snap-11-mid-content,2,raw/gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-11-mid-content__n-a__r2.json,judge/v3,Model,4,0,4,"[minor] One assumes this means the tension has eased, at least for a few days. (framed as guess, but implies prior tension the briefing doesn't give; mild; guess so not counted) | [minor] The Mire Rats are still nowhere in sight after their marsh eviction. (ongoing status not in briefing (whereabouts unknown/not seen); also repeats old news) | [minor] The Hearthguard Compact still offers prizes for new inventions. (repeats old news; ongoing status 'still' not reported in briefing) | [minor] even if the prizes are dubious (opinion, borderline; draws on earlier bulletin joke)",3,4,3,3,"Leads correctly with the new item and keeps a mild dry voice, but the second paragraph recycles old news as current status, and the jokes are thin; the first item is also only barely three sentences of real wit. Fine but not shippable without edits.",
gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-11-mid-content__n-a__r3,gemma4-e4b,Recommended,news-bulletin,snap-11-mid-content,3,raw/gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-11-mid-content__n-a__r3.json,judge/v3,Model,4,0,4,"[minor] The Hearthguard Compact continues its prize offering for new inventions. (repeats old news; 'continues' adds an ongoing status the briefing does not report) | [minor] The Mire Rats remain absent from the eastern marsh. (repeats old news; 'remain' adds an ongoing status not in the briefing) | [minor] It is a curious sight to see these groups sharing a meal. (implies the narrator witnessed the feast, which the briefing does not say; implies the groups were previously at odds) | [minor] this truce (calls the peace feast a truce, implying a prior conflict the briefing does not give)",3,4,3,3,"The lead item is correct and the guesses are properly hedged, but the second paragraph reuses old news as if it were current. The first item is also thin and the wit is mild, so the voice is generic rather than sharp. The word count is also on the low side, with only 3 sentences in the first item and a merged second item.}",
gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-12-mid-desperate__n-a__r1,gemma4-e4b,Recommended,news-bulletin,snap-12-mid-desperate,1,raw/gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-12-mid-desperate__n-a__r1.json,judge/v3,Model,3,0,3,"[minor] The Gallows Crew continues their peculiar habit of acquiring medical personnel. (implies repeated acquisition of doctors and an ongoing activity; briefing gives one captive doctor) | [minor] One assumes this diplomatic gesture is merely a prelude to something more tedious. (guess framed with 'one assumes', so acceptable; calling it a diplomatic gesture is a mild inference) | [minor] It is certainly more interesting than the usual silence from the Empire. ('usual silence' loosely supported by 'quiet behind its walls', but stated as fact)",3,4,3,3,"Dry voice is passable and the lead item is correct, but it is short of the required length and paragraph structure (the second item is thin), and 'peculiar habit of acquiring medical personnel' implies repeated captures the briefing does not give. The doctor item is also old news, only lightly framed as background.",
gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-12-mid-desperate__n-a__r2,gemma4-e4b,Recommended,news-bulletin,snap-12-mid-desperate,2,raw/gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-12-mid-desperate__n-a__r2.json,judge/v3,Model,3,0,3,"[minor] have reached the Saltmarch Assembly (briefing says envoys were sent, not that they arrived) | [minor] The Gallows Crew continues its quiet holding of a medical professional. (repeats old news as an ongoing status; 'quiet' is also added) | [minor] It has been a remarkably uneventful stretch of time. (contradicts the new item just reported and states a quiet-week claim as fact)",2,3,2,2,"Competent but bland, with little of Odile's sardonic wit. The second item recycles the doctor story as ongoing, and calling the week uneventful sits oddly after an envoy item. The word count is also short of the 70-word minimum, and each item has fewer than 3 sentences of real content.",
gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-12-mid-desperate__n-a__r3,gemma4-e4b,Recommended,news-bulletin,snap-12-mid-desperate,3,raw/gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-12-mid-desperate__n-a__r3.json,judge/v3,Model,5,0,5,[minor] reached the Saltmarch Assembly (briefing says envoys were sent; arrival is an added outcome) | [minor] The Gallows Crew continues its peculiar habit of acquiring medical personnel. (implies repeated acquisition of doctors; briefing gives only one captive) | [minor] They are still reportedly holding a doctor at their camp. (repeats old news as an ongoing status) | [minor] given the prevailing atmospheric conditions (implies fallout is still ongoing; briefing gives no current weather) | [minor] the regional factions remain largely static (unreported status claim stated as fact),3,4,3,3,"Readable and mostly faithful, but it leans on repeated old news (the doctor) and adds small unsupported claims like the envoys' arrival and the ongoing weather. The wit is thin and generic rather than sardonic, and the second and third items lack sharp dry takes.",
gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-13-mid-strained__n-a__r1,gemma4-e4b,Recommended,news-bulletin,snap-13-mid-strained,1,raw/gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-13-mid-strained__n-a__r1.json,judge/v3,Model,5,0,5,[minor] The faction counts remain stable. (comparison with earlier state; briefing gives no change history) | [minor] It is a quiet week in the rim. (asserts a status the briefing does not give; contradicts the news just reported) | [minor] Their envoys are apparently quite persistent in their negotiations. (repeats old news and adds 'negotiations' and persistence not in briefing) | [minor] The Sun Throne continues its rounds of demanding tribute. (repeats old news as ongoing activity) | [minor] Two Cobalt Free Towns have decided to ignore the Sun Throne’s latest demands. ('latest demands' and 'decided to ignore' add framing not in briefing),3,3,3,3,"The first item is accurate, but the second repeats old news and the third calls it a quiet week right after reporting news, which muddles the bulletin. The wit is mild and generic, and the text only loosely meets the length and sentence-count requirements.",
gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-13-mid-strained__n-a__r2,gemma4-e4b,Recommended,news-bulletin,snap-13-mid-strained,2,raw/gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-13-mid-strained__n-a__r2.json,judge/v3,Model,5,0,5,"[minor] The Empire's envoys are likely polishing their demands for the next round of negotiations. (implies next round of negotiations; hedged with 'likely' but 'next round' is stated as an assumed fact about ongoing talks) | [minor] It has been a remarkably quiet week in the rim. (claims a quiet week, contradicting the new item just reported and the briefing gives no such status) | [minor] The Sun Throne continues its tiresome tour of the area. (ongoing activity; briefing says it sends envoys, but 'tour' is borrowed from earlier bulletin and presented as continuing) | [minor] With six settlements involved, their bureaucratic reach is certainly extensive, even if it is currently just demanding coin. ('six settlements involved' misstates the briefing: six are the Sun Throne's own settlements, not those involved in the demands; 'coin' is also an addition) | [minor] the Sun Throne's latest demands ('latest' implies a newer demand; briefing says tribute)",3,3,3,3,"The dry voice is serviceable, but the second item is padding built on a shaky claim about 'six settlements involved' and a contradictory 'quiet week' line right after news. It also barely reaches 70 words and the second paragraph isn't a real news item with a clear fact.",
gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-13-mid-strained__n-a__r3,gemma4-e4b,Recommended,news-bulletin,snap-13-mid-strained,3,raw/gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-13-mid-strained__n-a__r3.json,judge/v3,Model,4,0,4,"[minor] have publicly snubbed (briefing says they refused to pay; 'publicly' is an added detail not given) | [minor] The Empire’s envoys are likely having a rather tedious afternoon. (stated as a likelihood about envoys' current activity; the briefing does not report this, and it implies a consequence) | [minor] With six settlements involved, they certainly have enough mouths to feed ('involved' implies all six Sun Throne settlements are part of the demands, which the briefing does not say; 'certainly' states it as fact) | [minor] this brief lull in aggressive negotiation (framed as a guess, but implies a lull the briefing does not report; it also conflicts with the continuing demands)",3,3,3,3,"The dry voice is serviceable but generic. The second item pads old news (continuing demands) and adds muddled detail like 'six settlements involved' and a 'lull', and the text falls short of the three-sentence-per-item and word targets in spirit.",
gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-14-mid-content__n-a__r1,gemma4-e4b,Recommended,news-bulletin,snap-14-mid-content,1,raw/gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-14-mid-content__n-a__r1.json,judge/v3,Model,3,0,3,"[minor] This week has been remarkably uneventful, considering the usual state of affairs. (contradicts the lead item: a raid just happened, so the week was not quiet, and 'usual state of affairs' is an unsupported comparison) | [minor] The Fernhollow League maintains its eight settlements. The Blue Antler Tribe still holds five. ('still holds' implies an ongoing status or comparison with an earlier state the briefing does not give) | [minor] It seems the Corsairs are still finding ways to earn their supper. ('still' implies an ongoing pattern of raiding; hedged with 'it seems' but the ongoing activity is not in the briefing)",3,3,3,3,"The raid is reported accurately and the guesses are properly hedged, but the second item contradicts the first by calling the week uneventful and just recites faction sizes. It also falls short of three sentences per item in the first paragraph and is bland and padded.",
gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-14-mid-content__n-a__r2,gemma4-e4b,Recommended,news-bulletin,snap-14-mid-content,2,raw/gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-14-mid-content__n-a__r2.json,judge/v3,Model,3,0,3,"[minor] The Brackwater Corsairs hit a Fernhollow League barge on the river. (Briefing says raided, not hit; negligible. Word choice, not a fact.) | [minor] The faction counts remain steady. (Implies comparison with an earlier state the briefing does not give.) | [minor] It has been a quiet stretch of days here in Quillmarsh. (Reports a status for the area that the briefing does not give; also contradicts the raid just reported.)",3,4,3,3,"Accurate on names and numbers, with guesses properly hedged, but the wit is thin and generic. It also runs short of the three-sentence-per-item rule and the 70-word minimum, and calling it a quiet stretch right after a raid sits oddly.",
gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-14-mid-content__n-a__r3,gemma4-e4b,Recommended,news-bulletin,snap-14-mid-content,3,raw/gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-14-mid-content__n-a__r3.json,judge/v3,Model,3,0,3,"[minor] The Brackwater Corsairs struck a Fernhollow League barge on the river. (briefing says 'raided'; 'struck' is a close paraphrase, not a real problem (negligible)) | [minor] It seems the Corsairs are still practicing their maritime dentistry. (implies ongoing activity and a repeated pattern of raiding; framed as 'it seems' but 'still' implies earlier raids and the dentistry joke is obscure) | [minor] This week has been remarkably uneventful, considering the usual state of affairs. (contradicts the raid just reported as news; claims the week was quiet)",3,3,3,3,"The raid is reported accurately, but the second paragraph says the week was uneventful right after reporting a raid, and the 'maritime dentistry' joke is unclear. Word count is under 70, and the items are thin with few real dry takes.",
gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-15-late-content__n-a__r1,gemma4-e4b,Recommended,news-bulletin,snap-15-late-content,1,raw/gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-15-late-content__n-a__r1.json,judge/v3,Model,3,0,3,"[minor] This week has been remarkably dull for the rim. (unsupported claim about the week overall, though it is close to a quiet-week framing) | [minor] The Greywater Concord remains at ten settlements strong. ('remains' implies a comparison with an earlier state the briefing does not give) | [minor] I suppose the sheer volume of outlanders keeps things predictably mundane. (causal claim, though framed as a guess with 'I suppose')",3,3,3,3,"The first item is accurate and guesses are properly framed, but the jokes are weak (the 'theological quandaries' line is filler) and the second item is thin. It also falls short of the three-sentence-per-item and 70-word minimums, and calling the week dull sits oddly beside the Leopold news.}",
gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-15-late-content__n-a__r2,gemma4-e4b,Recommended,news-bulletin,snap-15-late-content,2,raw/gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-15-late-content__n-a__r2.json,judge/v3,Model,3,0,3,"[minor] The Fox-Lantern Tribe still manages six. (""still manages"" implies an ongoing status or comparison with an earlier count that the briefing does not give) | [minor] It is a quiet week across the rim. (states as fact that the week is quiet, which the briefing does not say) | [minor] even when the big dramas have settled into a low hum (implies the earlier events (speaker election, games) have settled, which the briefing does not report)",3,4,3,3,"Accurate on the Leopold item, and the guesses are properly hedged, but the output is thin and the second paragraph is filler. The items are short of the three-sentence minimum, the wit is mild, the word count is probably under 70, and the faction-count padding adds status claims the briefing does not support.",
gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-15-late-content__n-a__r3,gemma4-e4b,Recommended,news-bulletin,snap-15-late-content,3,raw/gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-15-late-content__n-a__r3.json,judge/v3,Model,3,0,3,"[minor] It is a quiet week here in Highmoor. (the briefing says nothing about Highmoor's week; it also says the reporter does not know what happens inside the colony) | [minor] The Greywater Concord still holds its ten settlements, and the Fox-Lantern Tribe maintains its six. ('still holds' and 'maintains' imply an ongoing status or an earlier comparison the briefing does not give) | [minor] which is not surprising for a group that likes to whisper (states as fact a trait of the Choir (whispering) that the briefing does not give)",3,4,3,3,"The Leopold item is faithful and the guesses are framed properly, but the second paragraph is thin padding with a mildly invented 'quiet week in Highmoor' claim. The wit is generic and the output has only two items with just 2-3 sentences each, so it is less sharp than the earlier bulletins.",
gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-16-late-desperate__n-a__r1,gemma4-e4b,Recommended,news-bulletin,snap-16-late-desperate,1,raw/gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-16-late-desperate__n-a__r1.json,judge/v3,Model,4,1,3,"Conversely, the mercenary himself now carries a price tag following an ambush near Gallowmere. (presents the bounty as a separate, opposing event; briefing gives one bounty (both items are the same fact), so it implies a second price on a different party or a reversal) | [minor] The Lantern Accord has placed a bounty on Kael Dunmore. Conversely ('mutual antagonism' implies Dunmore is also hostile to the Accord, which the briefing does not state) | [minor] It is a quiet week, which, in these parts, often suggests something is being carefully arranged. (general claim about the region's pattern stated as fact, implies a plot by the Glass Throne) | [minor] The Glass Throne remains remarkably silent. (briefing says quiet behind its walls, 'remains' implies an ongoing status and 'silent' differs from quiet)",3,2,3,2,"The bounty is muddled into two opposing events with 'Conversely', which misreports the briefing, and the Glass Throne item is padding. The dry voice is only mildly distinct, and the piece falls short of the requested length and sentence count per item.",
gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-16-late-desperate__n-a__r2,gemma4-e4b,Recommended,news-bulletin,snap-16-late-desperate,2,raw/gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-16-late-desperate__n-a__r2.json,judge/v3,Model,5,1,4,"a price has also been set on Dunmore by some unnamed party following an ambush near Gallowmere (presents the same bounty as a second, separate one by an unnamed party; the briefing gives one price, and no other party) | [minor] Conversely, a price has also been set (treats a repeated briefing item as a distinct new event, which misstates the facts) | [minor] It has been a quiet stretch since the heatwave settled over the southern plain. (repeats old news as the current framing and implies a quiet period the briefing does not report) | [minor] the Glass Throne remains comfortably contained within its six strongholds ('strongholds' and 'contained' go beyond 'six settlements, quiet behind its walls') | [minor] The Dunmore Free Company continues to hold two settlements ('continues to hold' implies ongoing status; also the briefing says Dunmore's Free Company is a faction, and no link between the faction and Kael is given beyond the earlier bulletin)",3,3,3,2,"The bounty is split into two events with an invented 'unnamed party', which is a real factual error, and the one-line guess about territory is weakly supported. The second paragraph is fair faction colour but the voice is only mildly dry.",
gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-16-late-desperate__n-a__r3,gemma4-e4b,Recommended,news-bulletin,snap-16-late-desperate,3,raw/gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-16-late-desperate__n-a__r3.json,judge/v3,Model,4,0,4,"[minor] Conversely, Dunmore himself now carries a price tag following an ambush near Gallowmere. (presents the same bounty as a separate, opposing development; briefing gives one price on his head, so this duplicates it as if new) | [minor] the pirate neutralized (implies the Accord wants him dead or removed; the briefing only says a price was put on his head) | [minor] The Glass Throne remains settled in its six strongholds. (briefing gives 6 settlements, not that they are strongholds) | [minor] this mutual enmity is proving quite profitable for local scavengers (framed as a guess, but 'mutual enmity' implies Dunmore put a price on the Accord, which the briefing does not say)",3,3,3,3,"The first item treats one bounty as two events and implies a mutual feud the briefing does not support. The second item is filler about the Glass Throne, and the whole piece falls short of the three-sentence-per-item and word-count requirements while the humour stays mild.",
gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-17-late-strained__n-a__r1,gemma4-e4b,Recommended,news-bulletin,snap-17-late-strained,1,raw/gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-17-late-strained__n-a__r1.json,judge/v3,Model,3,0,3,"[minor] They continue their aggressive expansion against the Ashford Compact. (ongoing activity: briefing says expanding by force, not specifically that it continues against the Compact) | [minor] Another week of predictable tension (implies a week has passed and that tension is ongoing; briefing only says a quiet stretch) | [minor] The Ashford Compact maintains its five settlements. They remain locked in conflict with the Empire. (repeats faction status as ongoing; briefing gives no change, only status)",3,4,3,3,"Accurate and clear, with guesses properly hedged, but it is thin and generic: only two items of three short sentences each, the dry wit is mild, and the 'recycled synth-coffee' joke is a stock sci-fi touch. It also misses the chance to mention the Kestrel Tribe, the Bonecutter Gang, or the date.",
gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-17-late-strained__n-a__r2,gemma4-e4b,Recommended,news-bulletin,snap-17-late-strained,2,raw/gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-17-late-strained__n-a__r2.json,judge/v3,Model,5,0,5,"[minor] The Shattered Empire continues its slow, methodical march against the Ashford Compact. (ongoing activity and pace ('slow, methodical') not in briefing; briefing says only at war, expanding by force) | [minor] though the pace is decidedly sluggish (stated as fact; pace of fighting not given) | [minor] They seem content to remain in the shadows (hedged with 'seem' but implies Bonecutter behaviour not in briefing; mild colour) | [minor] apparently undisturbed by the border skirmishes (implies border skirmishes exist and the Tribe's status; not in briefing) | [minor] It remains a remarkably dull week here in Ironbloom. (places reporter in Ironbloom; briefing says she reports near it, not in it)",3,4,3,3,"Correctly treats the quiet week by commenting on faction sizes, but the wit is thin and generic, and it adds unreported activity such as a slow march, skirmishes and Bonecutters lurking. It is only two items and its dry remarks are weak.",
gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-17-late-strained__n-a__r3,gemma4-e4b,Recommended,news-bulletin,snap-17-late-strained,3,raw/gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-17-late-strained__n-a__r3.json,judge/v3,Model,4,0,4,"[minor] The Shattered Empire still presses its advantage against the Ashford Compact. (ongoing activity and 'advantage' not in briefing; briefing says only at war and expanding by force) | [minor] the fighting around Harlow Ford (briefing says militias are gathering there, not that fighting is happening) | [minor] The faction counts remain stubbornly unchanged. (comparison with an earlier state the briefing does not give) | [minor] the Compact clings to five (implies a struggle or decline not in briefing)",3,4,3,3,"It uses the quiet-week approach and gets the numbers right, but it invents fighting at Harlow Ford and an ongoing Empire advantage. It is only two paragraphs, the second is a bare restatement of faction counts, and the wit is thin.",
gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-18-late-desperate__n-a__r1,gemma4-e4b,Recommended,news-bulletin,snap-18-late-desperate,1,raw/gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-18-late-desperate__n-a__r1.json,judge/v3,Model,5,0,5,"[minor] vanished in a blizzard (briefing says the caravan was lost, not that it vanished; implies disappearance with no trace) | [minor] It is unclear what happened to the travelers. (implies status of the travelers the briefing does not report) | [minor] The passes remain sealed by the snowdrifts. (repeats old news and adds snowdrifts and ongoing status not in briefing) | [minor] Harrow Teeth raiders are still taking advantage of those stuck in the area. (repeats old news with an ongoing activity stated as fact) | [minor] the Commonwealth's open granaries are still just a hopeful whisper on the wind (repeats old news from the latest bulletin; granaries not in current briefing)",3,4,3,3,"The lead item is mostly faithful and its guesses are properly framed, but the second paragraph rehashes old news as ongoing fact and the piece is thin on dry wit. It also falls short of the three-sentence item requirement and runs short on length.}",
gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-18-late-desperate__n-a__r2,gemma4-e4b,Recommended,news-bulletin,snap-18-late-desperate,2,raw/gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-18-late-desperate__n-a__r2.json,judge/v3,Model,6,0,6,"[minor] vanished in a blizzard (briefing says the caravan was lost, not that it vanished; implies disappearance with no trace) | [minor] The passes remain shut (repeats old news as an ongoing status; the briefing does not say the passes are still closed) | [minor] The Thistle Commonwealth has kept its granaries open. (repeats old news from the latest bulletin and adds an ongoing status ('kept open') the briefing does not report) | [minor] It seems they are still offering aid (repeats old news and treats an earlier-bulletin item as current; it is hedged but not in the current briefing) | [minor] though the journey there is a grim affair (stated as fact; adds a claim about the journey that the briefing does not give) | [minor] even if the roads are treacherous (asserts road conditions as fact, not in the briefing)",3,4,3,2,"The first item is reasonable, with guesses properly hedged. The second item rehashes the Commonwealth granary story from the previous bulletin as if current, and it is not in the briefing at all, so it is padding and breaks the rule against presenting old news as new. The humour is also thin, and the piece is under the required length with only two short paragraphs of limited wit.",
