gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-19-late-desperate__n-a__r1,gemma4-e4b,Recommended,news-bulletin,snap-19-late-desperate,1,raw/gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-19-late-desperate__n-a__r1.json,judge/v3,Model,4,0,4,"[minor] The Sun Throne has now moved its attention. (implies a shift from Fenwick to the Marrow League, a sequence the briefing does not give) | [minor] They are besieging the Marrow League settlements. (briefing says besieging the Marrow League, not specifically its settlements; small embellishment) | [minor] The Sun Throne maintains its fourteen settlements. The Starling Tribe remains at four. ('maintains' and 'remains' imply a status unchanged over time, which the briefing does not report) | [minor] It is a quiet week, at least by the standards of ongoing conflict. (contradicts the new siege item; calling the week quiet is not supported)",3,3,3,3,"The output is short of the required length, has only one real news item, and the second paragraph calls the week quiet right after reporting a siege, which muddles it. The voice is dry but thin, with little real wit, and it omits the razing of Fenwick as background.",
gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-19-late-desperate__n-a__r2,gemma4-e4b,Recommended,news-bulletin,snap-19-late-desperate,2,raw/gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-19-late-desperate__n-a__r2.json,judge/v3,Model,3,0,3,"[minor] The Empire seems rather fond of sieges lately. (implies earlier sieges; briefing gives only one siege, framed as a seeming but implies a pattern) | [minor] The Sun Throne still maintains its grip on fourteen settlements. ('still' implies ongoing status/comparison with earlier state not given) | [minor] The Starling Tribe remains at four. ('remains' implies comparison with earlier state the briefing does not give)",3,4,3,3,"Accurate on the main fact and guesses are hedged, but it is under the length and item count (one short paragraph on the lead item plus a filler one), jokes are thin, and the second item is little more than restated faction sizes. Voice is only mildly dry and generic, with a few 'still/remains' implications of status.}",
gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-19-late-desperate__n-a__r3,gemma4-e4b,Recommended,news-bulletin,snap-19-late-desperate,3,raw/gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-19-late-desperate__n-a__r3.json,judge/v3,Model,4,1,3,"The Sun Throne has now moved its siege. (briefing says it is besieging the Marrow League; 'moved its siege' implies a shift not given) | [minor] They have, so far, managed to avoid any significant upheaval. (unreported status of the Starling Tribe; also sits oddly beside the Tribe sheltering Fenwick's survivors) | [minor] The Starling Tribe remains settled in their four locations. (ongoing status 'remains settled' not reported; briefing only gives four settlements) | [minor] They are pressing the Marrow League settlements. (describes ongoing activity beyond 'besieging the Marrow League')",3,3,3,2,"The lead item misstates the news by saying the siege 'moved', and it never mentions Fenwick's razing, which was old news anyway. The wit is thin: the items mostly restate faction facts with mild remarks and are padded.",
gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-20-late-strained__n-a__r1,gemma4-e4b,Recommended,news-bulletin,snap-20-late-strained,1,raw/gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-20-late-strained__n-a__r1.json,judge/v3,Model,2,0,2,"[minor] The Empire still controls the majority of settlements. (briefing says it controls most of the region and has 21 settlements, but 'majority of settlements' is a stretch: 21 of 26 is a majority, so mostly supported; 'still' implies ongoing status) | [minor] It remains a quiet week in the rim. (asserts the week is quiet as fact; the briefing reports a governorship offer and does not characterize the week)",3,4,3,3,"Accurate and clear, with guesses properly framed, but the wit is thin and generic and the item is shorter than asked (under 70 words, with items under three sentences). The barnacle line is the only real flourish, and the Alliance item repeats old news as filler.",
gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-20-late-strained__n-a__r2,gemma4-e4b,Recommended,news-bulletin,snap-20-late-strained,2,raw/gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-20-late-strained__n-a__r2.json,judge/v3,Model,2,0,2,"[minor] The war continues, predictably, between the Empire and the Free Coast Alliance. (ongoing activity: the briefing says they are at war but not that fighting continues this week) | [minor] The Alliance still clings to its two settlements, a stubborn patch of coastline. (repeats old news about the two towns, and the coastline detail echoes an earlier joke)",4,4,4,3,"The dry voice is consistent, and the governorship lead is correct and framed as a guess. The second item mostly repeats old news, and the item is only two sentences of fact plus a guess, so it falls short of the three-sentence minimum and the 70-word target.",
gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-20-late-strained__n-a__r3,gemma4-e4b,Recommended,news-bulletin,snap-20-late-strained,3,raw/gemma4-e4b__news-bulletin__snap-20-late-strained__n-a__r3.json,judge/v3,Model,3,0,3,"[minor] The Empire continues its skirmishes with the Free Coast Alliance. (briefing says only 'at war'; 'skirmishes' and ongoing activity are not reported) | [minor] The Driftwood Tribe holds their three scattered posts. ('scattered' and 'posts' are added detail; briefing gives only 3 settlements) | [minor] They maintain their grip on most of the region. (restates the briefing's 'controlling most of the region' as an ongoing status, which is mild and acceptable but adds little; the Alliance 'clings' repeats old news)",3,4,3,3,"Facts are mostly accurate and the guesses are properly framed, but the wit is thin and generic, the second and third items are flat restatements of faction sizes, and the Alliance two-town line repeats old news. The 'quiet week' line also contradicts leading with a new offer.",
gemma4-e4b__inheritance-handoff__snap-09-mid-desperate__n-a__r1,gemma4-e4b,Recommended,inheritance-handoff,snap-09-mid-desperate,1,raw/gemma4-e4b__inheritance-handoff__snap-09-mid-desperate__n-a__r1.json,judge/v3,Model,4,1,3,"Tamsin stood over the cooling form of her father, the grit of the Lancers' camp clinging to her scavenged gear. (places Tamsin at the Lancers' camp, where the briefing only has Joska and Malley fighting and dying) | [minor] She traced the shallow cut near his ribs, a souvenir from Malley. (invents a wound; the briefing says Malley maimed Joska on day 243 but not how or where) | [minor] The new captain’s oath echoed in the sudden silence. (implies Tamsin heard the oath at the scene, but the briefing gives no such moment) | [minor] She turned toward the fortified entrance. (adds a fortified entrance to the camp, which the briefing does not describe)",3,3,3,2,"Staging Tamsin at the Lancers' camp, standing over the body, puts her at a past event the briefing does not give her. The scene also ends vaguely on a turn toward the entrance, not on a clear intent to act, and it never mentions Lene.",
gemma4-e4b__inheritance-handoff__snap-09-mid-desperate__n-a__r2,gemma4-e4b,Recommended,inheritance-handoff,snap-09-mid-desperate,2,raw/gemma4-e4b__inheritance-handoff__snap-09-mid-desperate__n-a__r2.json,judge/v3,Model,4,1,3,"She traced the deep gouge near the knuckles, the same one Malley had left. (briefing says Malley maimed Joska, not that he gouged the gloves; invents a specific past detail about the gloves and the wound) | [minor] Joska’s worn leather gloves (gloves are not in the briefing; plausible staging object for a pit fighter) | [minor] cooling husk of Joska’s worn leather gloves ('cooling' is confused imagery, implying the body or item is warm; mild staging oddity) | [minor] smoke-wreathed Lancers' camp (camp visible from the scene and smoking is not given; places the camp near the scene)",3,3,3,3,"Restrained and ends on a resolve, but the gouge 'Malley had left' invents a past detail, 'cooling husk of gloves' is muddled, and the ending is thin; it also ignores the Lancers' new captain and the colony's threat.",
gemma4-e4b__inheritance-handoff__snap-09-mid-desperate__n-a__r3,gemma4-e4b,Recommended,inheritance-handoff,snap-09-mid-desperate,3,raw/gemma4-e4b__inheritance-handoff__snap-09-mid-desperate__n-a__r3.json,judge/v3,Model,3,1,2,"started toward the armory (names a room/building (armory) the briefing does not mention) | [minor] the heavy, chipped knife he always kept tethered to his belt (adds a detail about Joska's past habit and possessions not in the briefing) | [minor] Joska’s fighting gloves (plausible pit-fighter object, but gloves are not in the briefing; arguably staging)",3,4,3,3,"Restrained and readable, but it invents an armory, and the ending is a vague walk rather than a clear intent to avenge Joska or face the Lancers. It also names emotion-ish states ('too empty') and adds the knife habit.",
gemma4-e4b__inheritance-handoff__snap-16-late-desperate__n-a__r1,gemma4-e4b,Recommended,inheritance-handoff,snap-16-late-desperate,1,raw/gemma4-e4b__inheritance-handoff__snap-16-late-desperate__n-a__r1.json,judge/v3,Model,4,2,2,"Elske knelt beside Bertram, the blood dark against the dirt. (places Elske at the death scene; the briefing says only that Bertram died on the hunt, and does not put Elske among the hunters) | Rook nudged her hand, a low whine vibrating in his chest. (Rook came home alone per briefing, so he cannot be at the body) | [minor] She looked toward the woods where Dunmore had slipped away. (adds a specific detail (woods) about the escape and implies Elske witnessed it) | [minor] worn leather of his jacket (added detail about Bertram's clothing)",3,3,3,2,"The scene puts Elske and Rook at the site of Bertram's death, contradicting the briefing that Rook came home alone and placing Elske at a past event. The prose is restrained and ends on her resolve, but the facts are wrong and the friendship is barely shown.",
gemma4-e4b__inheritance-handoff__snap-16-late-desperate__n-a__r2,gemma4-e4b,Recommended,inheritance-handoff,snap-16-late-desperate,2,raw/gemma4-e4b__inheritance-handoff__snap-16-late-desperate__n-a__r2.json,judge/v3,Model,4,2,2,"Rook nudged her hand, a low whine vibrating in his chest. (puts Rook at the body; briefing says Rook came home alone, so he was not with Bertram at his death or the scene of the body) | Elske stood over the cooling form of Bertram. The blood on his tunic, the final, ragged breath leaving him. (puts Elske at Bertram's death, but she was not in the hunt; the briefing does not place her there, and the 'final breath' implies she witnessed the death) | [minor] the one he always kept close (added detail about Bertram's past habit with a sidearm) | [minor] toward the distant, scarred horizon where Kael Dunmore had vanished (specifies where Dunmore escaped to, which the briefing does not give)",3,3,3,2,"The scene places Elske at Bertram's death and has Rook beside the body, contradicting the briefing (the hunters were ambushed and Rook came home alone). The prose is serviceable but generic, and the ending is a flat vow with no use of her marshal background or the friendship.",
gemma4-e4b__inheritance-handoff__snap-16-late-desperate__n-a__r3,gemma4-e4b,Recommended,inheritance-handoff,snap-16-late-desperate,3,raw/gemma4-e4b__inheritance-handoff__snap-16-late-desperate__n-a__r3.json,judge/v3,Model,3,1,2,"Rook nudging her hand (puts Rook at the scene of death; the briefing says Rook came home alone, so this is a changed event) | [minor] The silence in the small clearing (adds a clearing as the location of the body; the briefing names no place) | [minor] the path where Dunmore had vanished (adds detail about how Dunmore escaped; the briefing says only that he escaped)",3,4,3,3,"The scene lands the intent to hunt Dunmore, but Rook at the body contradicts the briefing's 'came home alone', and the feeling is stated flatly ('too heavy, too final') rather than shown through small actions, with little sense of the friendship.",
gemma4-e4b__inheritance-handoff__snap-18-late-desperate__n-a__r1,gemma4-e4b,Recommended,inheritance-handoff,snap-18-late-desperate,1,raw/gemma4-e4b__inheritance-handoff__snap-18-late-desperate__n-a__r1.json,judge/v3,Model,3,0,3,"[minor] Constance’s teaching manual (a teaching manual is not mentioned; added object tied to her past as a teacher) | [minor] The letter from Ada, still tucked into the binding (the letter is in the briefing, but its location in a manual binding is invented detail about the past) | [minor] the way she’d faced the passes (implies Elias witnessed her facing the passes; he is not placed on the expedition, and her manner is added detail)",3,3,3,3,"Restrained and plausible, but it never states what Elias means to do about Ada, and the heir's goal is a vague shelter sketch rather than taking up the story. The manual and the letter's hiding place are added detail, and the scene is flat where it could land the moment.",
gemma4-e4b__inheritance-handoff__snap-18-late-desperate__n-a__r2,gemma4-e4b,Recommended,inheritance-handoff,snap-18-late-desperate,2,raw/gemma4-e4b__inheritance-handoff__snap-18-late-desperate__n-a__r2.json,judge/v3,Model,3,1,2,"[minor] the same fabric she wore when she taught in Midworld (adds a past detail about her clothing in Midworld not in the briefing) | He remembered her iron will, the way she faced the blizzard. (places Elias at or witnessing the blizzard; the briefing does not put him there) | [minor] still tucked into her bedside drawer (staging of the letter's location; mostly plausible but the briefing gives no drawer)",3,4,3,3,"The ending correctly commits Elias to finding Ada and brings in the letter and the teaching past, but ""the way she faced the blizzard"" implies he saw it, which the briefing does not support. The prose is plain and a little generic, and ""felt heavy"" nearly names a feeling instead of showing it.",
gemma4-e4b__inheritance-handoff__snap-18-late-desperate__n-a__r3,gemma4-e4b,Recommended,inheritance-handoff,snap-18-late-desperate,3,raw/gemma4-e4b__inheritance-handoff__snap-18-late-desperate__n-a__r3.json,judge/v3,Model,3,0,3,"[minor] the makeshift memorial, the wind whistling through the broken timbers (a memorial and broken timbers are not in the briefing; arguably staging the present moment, but they imply a site the briefing does not give) | [minor] He traced the outline of his mother’s worn coat, the fabric stiff with frost. (the coat is an invented object, though plausible staging; frost fits the death of cold) | [minor] Constance, with her iron will, had chased a ghost across the passes. ('chased a ghost' frames Ada as a ghost, but Ada is alive; figure of speech, mild)",3,4,3,3,"Clear and correctly uses the mother-son relationship and ends on Elias's intent to find Ada. The prose is generic, with some stock phrasing (""frayed"", ""familiar tremor""), and the memorial and the ending's ""picks up his tools"" are loosely motivated.",
gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-01-early-content__n-a__r1,gemma4-12b,High,news-bulletin,snap-01-early-content,1,raw/gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-01-early-content__n-a__r1.json,judge/v3,Model,2,0,2,"[minor] a place where the only thing moving fast is the dust (describes the river road as quiet and dusty, which the briefing does not give; reads as a claim of fact rather than an opinion) | [minor] The locals will likely find a way to complain about the temperature while shivering. (implies locals live in the northern hills, which the briefing does not say; hedged with 'likely', but still adds to the briefing)",3,4,3,3,"Accurate to the briefing and dry, with the guesses framed properly, but it is short of the 70-word minimum and the jokes are generic. It adds mild unsupported colour about the road and the locals, and it makes no use of the faction figures.",
gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-01-early-content__n-a__r2,gemma4-12b,High,news-bulletin,snap-01-early-content,2,raw/gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-01-early-content__n-a__r2.json,judge/v3,Model,2,0,2,"[minor] the lack of actual progress (framed after 'I suppose', but 'lack of progress' is stated as a fact about the Union that the briefing does not give) | [minor] a group that seems content with just existing (hedged with 'seems', so mostly opinion; borderline implied status not in the briefing)",3,4,3,3,"The facts are accurate and the dry voice is consistent, but the bulletin is under the required length and its items run only three short sentences each, with generic quips. It ignores the faction numbers that could have padded a quiet week, and the wit is bland rather than sharp. The 'lack of actual progress' line leans on an unsupported premise about the Union.",
gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-01-early-content__n-a__r3,gemma4-12b,High,news-bulletin,snap-01-early-content,3,raw/gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-01-early-content__n-a__r3.json,judge/v3,Model,1,0,1,[minor] It is a predictable turn of events for a rim that rarely offers surprises. (states as fact that the cold snap is predictable and the rim rarely changes; the briefing gives neither),3,4,3,3,"Facts are accurate and the guesses are properly framed, but the jokes are generic (""magically generate customers out of thin air"", ""refreshing change"") and the bulletin falls short of the word count and the three-sentence minimum per item. It reads as passable but bland rather than ready to ship.",
gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-02-early-content__n-a__r1,gemma4-12b,High,news-bulletin,snap-02-early-content,1,raw/gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-02-early-content__n-a__r1.json,judge/v3,Model,4,0,4,"[minor] They have managed to leave a site without being caught or killed, which is a rare feat for them. (implies they were at risk of capture or death when leaving; the briefing gives no such circumstances) | [minor] It is a long-running dispute with very little progress to show for it. (stated as fact: duration and lack of progress are not in the briefing) | [minor] The Tannerfolk and the Hollow Spire Pirates continue their war over the salt flats. (repeats old news as an ongoing status; the briefing treats it as background only) | [minor] a company that thrives on the chaos of others (stated as fact; implies a cause the briefing does not give)",3,4,3,3,"It leads correctly with the new item and keeps a dry tone, but the pirates joke implies circumstances the briefing does not give. The third item pads with a bland faction-size remark, and the wit is mild and generic.",
gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-02-early-content__n-a__r2,gemma4-12b,High,news-bulletin,snap-02-early-content,2,raw/gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-02-early-content__n-a__r2.json,judge/v3,Model,2,0,2,"[minor] The Tannerfolk and the Hollow Spire Pirates are still engaged in their ongoing war over the salt flats. (repeats old news; the fighting is background from an earlier bulletin, and ""still"" asserts an ongoing status the briefing does not report for this week, though the war itself is in the faction list) | [minor] They seem quite content with their current footprint. (inference about the Company's attitude, hedged with ""seem"" but loosely presented as observation)",3,4,3,3,"Accurate and clear with no invented names or numbers, but the second item largely repeats old news and the third is filler about a faction size. The wit is mild and generic rather than sharp, and the last item feels padded.",
gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-02-early-content__n-a__r3,gemma4-12b,High,news-bulletin,snap-02-early-content,3,raw/gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-02-early-content__n-a__r3.json,judge/v3,Model,3,0,3,"[minor] though the pirates seem to be moving their theater of operations (inference about relocation stated as observation ('seem'), but implies unreported ongoing activity; borderline guess) | [minor] They are quite consistent in their expansion. (implies the Company has been expanding; briefing only gives a count of 5 settlements) | [minor] They are still at war with the Tannerfolk (repeats old news as ongoing status; briefing does give the war, so only mild)",3,4,3,3,"Dry and readable, but it is thin and a bit generic, and the 'expansion' line adds an unsupported claim. It also looks short of the 70-word minimum and has weak jokes, with the second item lacking a clear fact-then-take shape.",
gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-03-early-strained__n-a__r1,gemma4-12b,High,news-bulletin,snap-03-early-strained,1,raw/gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-03-early-strained__n-a__r1.json,judge/v3,Model,2,0,2,"[minor] They seem content to maintain their current reach without further expansion. (hedged with 'seem', but implies status of no expansion not in briefing; borderline) | [minor] They remain a sizable presence on the rim. (stated as fact; comparison/inference about size not in briefing)",3,4,3,3,"Accurate with faction numbers and no real invented events, but the wit is thin and generic, and it ignores the Kinn and the earlier raids as background. It is also only three short items, with the first being filler about a quiet week; it reads as bland rather than shippable.",
gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-03-early-strained__n-a__r2,gemma4-12b,High,news-bulletin,snap-03-early-strained,2,raw/gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-03-early-strained__n-a__r2.json,judge/v3,Model,2,0,2,"[minor] They seem content to sit on their loot rather than find new ways to ruin someone's afternoon. (hedged with 'seem' but implies the Ashen Hand's current activity (idle, holding loot) that the briefing does not report) | [minor] They are still moving, presumably because staying still is less appealing than wandering. ('still moving' is an ongoing status the briefing does not report; the grass-fire move was in the earlier bulletin and the cause is only guessed)",3,4,3,3,"Facts are accurate and the quiet week is handled sensibly, but it runs to four short items instead of 2 or 3. The wit is thin and generic, and the Kinn line implies an ongoing move the briefing does not report.",
gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-03-early-strained__n-a__r3,gemma4-12b,High,news-bulletin,snap-03-early-strained,3,raw/gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-03-early-strained__n-a__r3.json,judge/v3,Model,3,0,3,"[minor] They remain a persistent thorn in the side of any local commerce. (stated as fact; implied ongoing activity not in briefing) | [minor] They are currently doubling their guard costs to keep their caravans moving. (repeats old news: pairs travel was covered earlier, and 'currently doubling guard costs' is an ongoing status stated as fact) | [minor] Silence in these parts usually means someone is either sleeping or hiding. (general quip, borderline; not a world fact)",3,4,3,3,"Handles a quiet week reasonably by commenting on faction sizes, but the opening is padded and the Merrow item restates old news as a current cost claim. It also lacks the wry specificity of the earlier bulletins and runs short on length and Kinn coverage.",
gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-04-early-strained__n-a__r1,gemma4-12b,High,news-bulletin,snap-04-early-strained,1,raw/gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-04-early-strained__n-a__r1.json,judge/v3,Model,2,0,2,"[minor] It is a shame we have to waste ink on his disappearance. (implies his disappearance as fact; briefing only says the Dispatch seeks news of him) | [minor] perhaps we just realized the locals are uncooperative (framed as a guess, but 'a quiet place' states Lowmere's character as fact beyond the briefing)",3,4,3,3,"Accurate to the briefing with hedged guesses and no invented people or events, but the humour is generic and the word count is low. 'Disappearance' and 'a quiet place' slightly overreach, and the pirates joke is thin.",
gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-04-early-strained__n-a__r2,gemma4-12b,High,news-bulletin,snap-04-early-strained,2,raw/gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-04-early-strained__n-a__r2.json,judge/v3,Model,4,0,4,"[minor] its missing reporter, Tomas Quell (briefing says the Dispatch is looking for news of him, not that he is missing; implied status) | [minor] It is a bit of a logistical headache for the office. (implied consequence stated as fact, not in briefing) | [minor] It is a quiet move for a quiet place. (states Lowmere is quiet as fact; briefing gives no such information) | [minor] passengers (implies passengers were aboard the ferry; briefing does not say)",3,4,4,3,"Dry, readable and tonally right, and it stays close to the three briefing items. However, it adds small unsupported claims (missing, passengers, quiet place, logistical headache), and the items are short of the required three sentences, likely under length, with some generic wit.</br>",
gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-04-early-strained__n-a__r3,gemma4-12b,High,news-bulletin,snap-04-early-strained,3,raw/gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-04-early-strained__n-a__r3.json,judge/v3,Model,3,0,3,"[minor] its missing reporter, Tomas Quell (briefing says the Dispatch is looking for news of him, not that he is 'missing' (implied status)) | [minor] They seem to have a flair for arson that most of us find inconvenient. (implies a pattern of arson; the briefing reports only one ferry burning (hedged with 'seem' but stated as habit)) | [minor] It makes my job slightly easier, though I doubt the editors appreciate the lack of competition. (implies Quell was a competitor; the briefing says he is a Dispatch reporter, a colleague)",4,4,4,3,"The dry voice is consistent and the items follow the briefing's three events in order. It slips on Quell, whom it treats as a rival and calls missing, and on the arson 'flair' that implies a pattern. It is also a little short of the word target, though acceptable.}",
gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-05-early-desperate__n-a__r1,gemma4-12b,High,news-bulletin,snap-05-early-desperate,1,raw/gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-05-early-desperate__n-a__r1.json,judge/v3,Model,2,0,2,"[minor] The Scythe Tooth pirates have hit three settlements in a quadrum. (repeats old news as if current; presented without background framing (briefing gives raids at three settlements, 'quadrum' from earlier bulletin)) | [minor] closed their markets to all outsiders (adds 'all'; briefing says only 'outsiders')",4,4,4,3,"The dry voice is consistent and the guesses are properly hedged, but the second item presents the earlier Scythe Tooth raids as fresh news, which the task forbids. The third item is a decent quiet-week joke but pads the bulletin with filler and the first item adds a small embellishment ('all').",
gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-05-early-desperate__n-a__r2,gemma4-12b,High,news-bulletin,snap-05-early-desperate,2,raw/gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-05-early-desperate__n-a__r2.json,judge/v3,Model,3,0,3,"[minor] The Scythe Tooth pirates have hit three settlements in a quadrum. (repeats old news as if current; briefing lists raids at three settlements as already covered, and 'in a quadrum' comes from an earlier bulletin) | [minor] They seem to be enjoying the local scenery. (framed as a seeming, but implies ongoing activity; mostly a joke, borderline) | [minor] It is a predictable development for a group that prefers their own company. (states as fact that the Gorse Clans prefer their own company; earlier bulletin showed them trading, so it is an unsupported inference)",3,4,3,2,"The Scythe Tooth item presents old news as if it were fresh, which the task forbids, and the jokes are generic and thin. The third item only comments on the date, which is allowed, but together the bulletin pads and runs short of the required 3-sentence dry takes with real bite.",
gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-05-early-desperate__n-a__r3,gemma4-12b,High,news-bulletin,snap-05-early-desperate,3,raw/gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-05-early-desperate__n-a__r3.json,judge/v3,Model,4,0,4,"[minor] The Scythe Tooth pirates have hit three settlements in a quadrum. (repeats old news as if current; the raids were covered in an earlier bulletin and the ""quadrum"" detail comes from the earlier bulletin, not the briefing) | [minor] The Ferrow Mutual now requires members to share patrols. They have also asked who is paying for the privilege. (repeats old news; earlier bulletin said the Mutual asked members to share patrols, not that it requires it, so the claim is slightly altered) | [minor] all outsiders (briefing says 'outsiders'; 'all' is a slight addition) | [minor] It is a charming way to manage a trade deficit. (implies the Clans have a trade deficit, stated as fact without support)",3,4,3,2,"Two of the three items are old news presented as fresh, which breaks a core instruction, and the Ferrow item changes 'asked' to 'requires'. The dry voice is present, but the 'portfolio' and 'fiscal policy' jokes lean toward modern-office language.",
gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-06-early-content__n-a__r1,gemma4-12b,High,news-bulletin,snap-06-early-content,1,raw/gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-06-early-content__n-a__r1.json,judge/v3,Model,2,0,2,[minor] the Calder Combine's bounty (briefing does not say the barge or grain belonged to the Combine; implied ownership stated as fact) | [minor] before the next moon ('moon' timeframe is colour but not RimWorld vocabulary; framed as a guess so mostly fine),4,4,4,3,"Dry voice and well-framed guesses, but the first item treats the barge as the Combine's grain, which the briefing never says. The bulletin is also short of the 70-word minimum and item two has only three sentences with thin content.",
gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-06-early-content__n-a__r2,gemma4-12b,High,news-bulletin,snap-06-early-content,2,raw/gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-06-early-content__n-a__r2.json,judge/v3,Model,2,0,2,"[minor] The Calder Combine still reports good harvests along the delta. (repeats old news with 'still', implying an ongoing report rather than background) | [minor] It is a miracle of agriculture that keeps the local bellies full. (states as fact that the harvest feeds local people; not in briefing)",3,4,3,3,"Accurate on the main item and the guesses are properly hedged, but the second item rehashes old news as if current, and the wit is generic. The first item is also thin, with the 'logistics' joke saying little about the robbery.",
gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-06-early-content__n-a__r3,gemma4-12b,High,news-bulletin,snap-06-early-content,3,raw/gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-06-early-content__n-a__r3.json,judge/v3,Model,1,0,1,"[minor] the pirates have a sudden appetite for the Calder Combine's surplus (implies the barge belonged to the Calder Combine; briefing does not say whose barge it was (framed with 'It seems', but the Combine link is an inference))",4,4,4,3,"The dry voice is consistent and the Ditch Kings item is faithful, but the output is short of the 70-word minimum and says little about the Empire beyond the briefing's own line. The Combine's surplus is an unsupported link to the barge, though hedged with 'it seems'.",
gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-07-mid-strained__n-a__r1,gemma4-12b,High,news-bulletin,snap-07-mid-strained,1,raw/gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-07-mid-strained__n-a__r1.json,judge/v3,Model,3,0,3,"[minor] The Iron Covenant still lacks its missing supply wagon. (repeats old news as an ongoing status; the briefing gives no current state of the wagon) | [minor] They are still mourning the loss of that cargo. (ongoing activity or status not in the briefing, stated as fact) | [minor] They are busy sending envoys to everyone nearby. (the briefing says envoys are sent, but not that this is ongoing or reaches everyone nearby; the claim is exaggerated)",3,4,3,3,"The lead item is accurate and the dry guesses are properly framed. The second item mostly repeats old news as ongoing status and the third pads with generic jabs, and the whole piece falls short of the length and sentence requirements.",
gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-07-mid-strained__n-a__r2,gemma4-12b,High,news-bulletin,snap-07-mid-strained,2,raw/gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-07-mid-strained__n-a__r2.json,judge/v3,Model,3,0,3,"[minor] They seem to think a lack of infrastructure justifies a fee for the privilege of passing through it. (framed as 'seem', but asserts a rationale/infrastructure claim the briefing does not give; borderline inference) | [minor] They manage to keep their borders intact while the Empire expands its list of grievances. (states as fact that borders are intact and that the Empire is expanding grievances; not in briefing) | [minor] despite their recent losses (repeats old news (the lost wagon) as ongoing status, implies broader losses than the single wagon)",3,3,3,3,"The lead item correctly reports the toll demand with a hedged guess, but the second item pads with unsupported claims about borders and grievances and is thin on a real fact. Each item is only three short sentences and the wit is mild, with the old news treated vaguely rather than as clear background.",
gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-07-mid-strained__n-a__r3,gemma4-12b,High,news-bulletin,snap-07-mid-strained,3,raw/gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-07-mid-strained__n-a__r3.json,judge/v3,Model,3,0,3,"[minor] They seem to think a bit of dirt and a steep incline justifies a tax. (hedged as 'seem', but describes road conditions (dirt, steep incline) the briefing does not give) | [minor] The Iron Covenant still lacks that supply wagon lost to the raiders. (ongoing status not reported in briefing; repeats old news as current state) | [minor] It is a shame they cannot find the wagon and the raiders at the same time. (implies the Covenant is searching for the wagon and raiders, which the briefing does not say)",3,4,3,3,"The first item is accurate and reasonably dry, but the second recycles old news as a present status and implies a search that never happened. At two short items, the piece also runs under the required length and each item falls short of three sentences of fact plus a take.",
gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-08-mid-content__n-a__r1,gemma4-12b,High,news-bulletin,snap-08-mid-content,1,raw/gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-08-mid-content__n-a__r1.json,judge/v3,Model,4,0,4,"[minor] The Lantern Accord remains the largest faction with nine settlements. ('remains' implies a prior state of dominance the briefing does not give; the Accord is largest by count, but the earlier-state comparison is added) | [minor] They have managed to maintain their dominance (implied history and cause; briefing gives no earlier state or effort) | [minor] the Ninefingers Gang lingers in only three ('lingers' implies ongoing activity and a comparison; also ignores that the Reedmother's Children (5) are second) | [minor] more interesting than the actual goods on display (stated as a guess ('one assumes') but implies goods are on display at the fair; low severity as framed guess)",3,4,3,3,"Dry and readable, but the second item adds implied history ('remains', 'maintain their dominance'), and the output is short of the three-sentence-per-item, 70-word target. The wit is mild and the sculpture item has a weak joke.",
gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-08-mid-content__n-a__r2,gemma4-12b,High,news-bulletin,snap-08-mid-content,2,raw/gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-08-mid-content__n-a__r2.json,judge/v3,Model,3,0,3,"[minor] They are currently hosting their trade fair as previously noted. (repeats old news; briefing says the fair is being hosted, but 'currently' is an ongoing-status claim and earlier bulletin said it opens next week) | [minor] They are still enjoying a productive fishing season. (repeats old news and states ongoing status the briefing does not report) | [minor] It is a quiet week for the rim (unsupported stated claim about the whole rim; briefing gives no such characterization)",3,4,3,3,"The lead item is faithful and dry, but the second and third items pad with old news and faction counts, and the ongoing-status claims are stated as fact. The humor is mild and the closing line is a bit generic.",
gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-08-mid-content__n-a__r3,gemma4-12b,High,news-bulletin,snap-08-mid-content,3,raw/gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-08-mid-content__n-a__r3.json,judge/v3,Model,5,0,5,"[minor] The Lantern Accord continues to manage its nine settlements while hosting their trade fair. (repeats old news; trade fair is presented as ongoing activity, which the briefing does not state (earlier bulletin said it opens next week)) | [minor] They are currently content with their haul. (added status not in briefing) | [minor] a tribe that usually prefers the river to the land (added claim about tribe's habits, not in briefing; stated as fact) | [minor] It is a rare moment of peace (implies past conflict and comparison with earlier state not in briefing) | [minor] They claim to offer fair prices (repeats old news from earlier bulletin)",3,4,3,3,"The lead item is accurate and drily handled, but two of the three items rehash old news as if current, and the third adds unsupported claims about the tribe. The prose is also a bit flat and generic, with the wit thinner than the persona demands.",
gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-09-mid-desperate__n-a__r1,gemma4-12b,High,news-bulletin,snap-09-mid-desperate,1,raw/gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-09-mid-desperate__n-a__r1.json,judge/v3,Model,3,0,3,"[minor] The Embertail Tribe remains at war with the Gray Wharf Syndicate. (repeats old news as an ongoing item; the war was covered in an earlier bulletin, though the briefing does list the war) | [minor] yet to secure any actual fish (repeats the earlier bulletin's fish joke and presents it as current fact; the briefing does not mention fishing) | [minor] It appears the pirates were less capable of defending their own doorstep than their reputation suggested. (inference about cause stated as fact (hedged with 'It appears', but implies the pirates failed to defend))",4,4,4,3,"The dry voice is consistent and the lead item stays on the briefing, but the second item recycles the earlier fish joke, dwells on old news, and the paragraphs are on the short side of the sentence minimum. The Lancers' search for a leader is framed as a guess, which is fine, but the output does not use the briefing's new information beyond one item.",
gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-09-mid-desperate__n-a__r2,gemma4-12b,High,news-bulletin,snap-09-mid-desperate,2,raw/gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-09-mid-desperate__n-a__r2.json,judge/v3,Model,4,0,4,"[minor] an assassin (implies a killer type; briefing gives no killer, though framed within a guess) | [minor] It is a rather efficient way to manage a leadership crisis. (implies a leadership crisis as a consequence; briefing does not report one) | [minor] Neither side has managed to secure any fish during this ongoing conflict. (repeats old news and states as fact what the earlier bulletin only guessed (""so far as I can tell""); also implies ongoing status) | [minor] The Embertail Tribe remains at war with the Gray Wharf Syndicate. (repeats old news as current status; briefing only lists the war as background)",3,4,3,3,"Leads correctly with Malley's death and keeps a dry register, but the second item recycles the earlier fish joke and states it as fact, and the first item hints at an assassin and leadership crisis. Also falls short of the required length and sentence count per item and the wit is thin.
",
gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-09-mid-desperate__n-a__r3,gemma4-12b,High,news-bulletin,snap-09-mid-desperate,3,raw/gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-09-mid-desperate__n-a__r3.json,judge/v3,Model,3,0,3,"[minor] Neither side has managed to secure any fish despite the ongoing hostilities. (repeats old news: reuses the earlier fishing joke and states as fact that no fish were caught, plus ongoing hostilities not in the briefing) | [minor] The Embertail Tribe remains at war with the Gray Wharf Syndicate. (repeats old news as a current item, though the briefing does list the war as ongoing) | [minor] the pirates were not particularly vigilant during his final moments (guess framed with 'One assumes', so acceptable; implies cause but hedged)",3,4,3,3,"Dry voice is present but generic, and the second item recycles the earlier bulletin's fish joke instead of offering fresh comment. Each item is thin, and the first is only three short sentences with little new wit; the length is also likely under the 70-word minimum, though it sticks to the briefing facts.",
gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-10-mid-strained__n-a__r1,gemma4-12b,High,news-bulletin,snap-10-mid-strained,1,raw/gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-10-mid-strained__n-a__r1.json,judge/v3,Model,4,0,4,"[minor] The Stonecutter Raiders continue to hold the captives taken from the Ochre Hand. (repeats old news as a present-tense status paragraph) | [minor] It is a standard hostage situation for a standard pirate war. (claims typicality/comparison not in briefing) | [minor] They remain a large, looming presence on the rim. (stated as fact; briefing gives only seven settlements, no looming presence) | [minor] The Weir Federation still maintains its seven settlements. (implies ongoing status/comparison not reported; filler item)",4,4,3,3,"The dry voice is consistent and the lead item is accurate. The second item repeats old news, the third is padding, and the whole thing runs slightly short of the 70-word minimum. The 'ransom more efficient than a spear' line is wit, not fact.",
gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-10-mid-strained__n-a__r2,gemma4-12b,High,news-bulletin,snap-10-mid-strained,2,raw/gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-10-mid-strained__n-a__r2.json,judge/v3,Model,3,0,3,"[minor] The Stonecutter Raiders currently hold several captives from the Ochre Hand. (repeats old news as a present-tense status; ""several"" is an added quantity the briefing does not give) | [minor] It seems they have finally realized that people are worth more than the dirt they stand on. (implies the Ochre Hand previously undervalued people, which the briefing does not say) | [minor] This is a continuation of the ongoing war between the two groups. (implied cause: links the captives to the war, which the briefing does not state)",3,4,3,3,"Accurate on the lead item and it uses hedged guesses, but it is too short (about 85 words, with only two items of three sentences). The second item mostly repeats old news as current, and the jokes are generic, with weak 'dirt' and 'frost-bitten rock' quips that don't fit the rim.",
gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-10-mid-strained__n-a__r3,gemma4-12b,High,news-bulletin,snap-10-mid-strained,3,raw/gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-10-mid-strained__n-a__r3.json,judge/v3,Model,2,0,2,"[minor] They are quite content to sit on their land while the other factions bicker. (stated as fact: the Weir's contentment and inaction are not in the briefing) | [minor] It seems they have discovered that ransom is a more efficient tool than honest warfare. (implies the Ochre Hand has turned from warfare to ransom; the briefing says they are at war and gives no such shift (hedged with 'it seems', so mild))",4,4,4,3,"The dry voice is consistent and the lead item is accurate, but the second item is thin padding about the Weir with a stated-as-fact claim of contentment. It also falls short of the three-sentence minimum per item and is probably under the word count, at roughly 75 words, so it barely clears the 70 minimum.",
gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-11-mid-content__n-a__r1,gemma4-12b,High,news-bulletin,snap-11-mid-content,1,raw/gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-11-mid-content__n-a__r1.json,judge/v3,Model,4,0,4,"[minor] It is a rare moment of cooperation in a wasteland that usually prefers teeth to toasts. (implies earlier conflict or rarity of peace not in briefing, stated as fact) | [minor] They seem content with their current numbers. (status claim about Hearthguard's contentment not given; hedged only by 'seem') | [minor] They have successfully avoided the eastern marsh for now. (repeats old news and changes it: Mire Rats were driven out, not avoiding by success; adds ongoing status) | [minor] The Mire Rats still occupy two settlements. (repeats faction size as ongoing status ('still'), mildly implies a comparison with earlier state)",3,4,3,3,"Leads correctly with the new feast and stays mostly within the briefing, but the second and third items are thin filler on faction sizes and the Mire Rats item distorts the old news (driven out becomes 'successfully avoided'). The wit is mild and the wasteland line adds an unsupported generalisation about the rim.",
gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-11-mid-content__n-a__r2,gemma4-12b,High,news-bulletin,snap-11-mid-content,2,raw/gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-11-mid-content__n-a__r2.json,judge/v3,Model,4,0,4,"[minor] They have managed to keep their borders intact for another day. (implied status/ongoing activity not in briefing; borders intact is unreported) | [minor] It is a rare moment of cooperation in a land that usually prefers biting. (implies cooperation is rare, a comparison with earlier state not given) | [minor] They have lost the eastern marsh, but they still have a home. (repeats old news as background but adds that they still have a home; implied status) | [minor] The Mire Rats still occupy two settlements. (repeats old news framing; 'still' implies ongoing status, though count matches briefing)",3,4,3,3,"The feast lead is correct and the dry voice mostly holds, but the second and third items pad with faction sizes and add implied status such as intact borders. The wit is thin and the closing 'successful retreat' line is weak.",
gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-11-mid-content__n-a__r3,gemma4-12b,High,news-bulletin,snap-11-mid-content,3,raw/gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-11-mid-content__n-a__r3.json,judge/v3,Model,5,0,5,"[minor] The Hearthguard Compact still maintains eight settlements. (""still"" implies an ongoing status and comparison with an earlier state the briefing does not give) | [minor] They seem content to sit on their land and wait for someone to build them something useful. (hedged with ""seem"", but ties to the invention prizes as an inference; borderline, mostly opinion) | [minor] The Mire Rats still occupy two settlements. (""still"" implies ongoing status the briefing does not report) | [minor] It is a rare moment of cooperation in a land that usually prefers teeth to toasts. (states as fact that such cooperation is rare, a comparison with earlier states the briefing does not give) | [minor] They were driven from the eastern marsh, but they haven't vanished into thin air. (repeats old news as background; the claim that they still exist and are elsewhere is added)",4,4,4,3,"The dry voice is consistent and the lead item is correct. The second and third items pad with faction sizes and old news, and add small implied claims such as ""still"" and ""rare"", though the guesses are properly hedged.",
gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-12-mid-desperate__n-a__r1,gemma4-12b,High,news-bulletin,snap-12-mid-desperate,1,raw/gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-12-mid-desperate__n-a__r1.json,judge/v3,Model,3,0,3,"[minor] They seem to have found a way to keep the professional alive, which is a minor miracle. (implies the doctor's survival was in doubt and a method was found; hedged with 'seem' but the 'minor miracle' states it as fact) | [minor] It is a polite way to say they are hiding their intentions. (inference stated as fact about the envoys' purpose, not framed as a guess) | [minor] The Gallows Crew continues to hold a doctor at their camp. (repeats old news as an ongoing status; it is framed as a continuation but takes up half the bulletin)",3,4,3,3,"The lead item is accurate and the dry voice is passable, but the second item merely rehashes old news with unsupported inference, and the piece is too short at about 85 words with only two-sentence-plus items and little wit. Several claims are stated as fact rather than guess, so it is not ready to ship.",
gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-12-mid-desperate__n-a__r2,gemma4-12b,High,news-bulletin,snap-12-mid-desperate,2,raw/gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-12-mid-desperate__n-a__r2.json,judge/v3,Model,3,0,3,"[minor] The Gallows Crew continues to hold a doctor at their camp. (repeats old news; ""continues to hold"" implies an ongoing status the briefing does not report as current) | [minor] They seem remarkably consistent in their hostage-taking. (implies a pattern of repeated hostage-taking the briefing does not give, though hedged with ""seem"") | [minor] as anonymous as its residents (implies the Empire's residents are anonymous, which the briefing does not say)",3,4,3,3,"The lead item is correct and the guesses are properly hedged, but the second item recycles old news as a current update and echoes the earlier doctor joke. The bulletin is also well under the 70-word minimum and has weak wit in the first item.
",
gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-12-mid-desperate__n-a__r3,gemma4-12b,High,news-bulletin,snap-12-mid-desperate,3,raw/gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-12-mid-desperate__n-a__r3.json,judge/v3,Model,3,0,3,"[minor] The Gallows Crew continues to hold a doctor at their camp. (repeats old news as an ongoing status; the briefing only gives it as earlier coverage) | [minor] They seem to have found a way to keep the captive alive for a few more days. (implied consequence and timeline not in briefing; hedged with 'seem' but states a few more days) | [minor] for a faction that claims to be quiet (the Glass Throne is described as quiet behind its walls, but no claim by the faction is given)",4,4,4,3,"The dry voice is consistent and the lead item is accurate. The second item is mostly old news presented as ongoing and carries a small invented detail, and the piece falls short of the three-sentence-per-item requirement in spirit and likely the word count.",
gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-13-mid-strained__n-a__r1,gemma4-12b,High,news-bulletin,snap-13-mid-strained,1,raw/gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-13-mid-strained__n-a__r1.json,judge/v3,Model,2,0,2,"[minor] They remain a constant presence on the rim. (ongoing status not in briefing; stated as fact) | [minor] It seems the Outlanders have developed a sudden, inconvenient sense of independence. (implies a change from earlier state; briefing does not say it was sudden)",3,4,3,3,"Accurate to the briefing and clearly ordered, with only small embellishments. The wit is mild and generic, and the last two items are filler on faction sizes that never reach the dry bite of the earlier bulletins.",
gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-13-mid-strained__n-a__r2,gemma4-12b,High,news-bulletin,snap-13-mid-strained,2,raw/gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-13-mid-strained__n-a__r2.json,judge/v3,Model,4,0,4,"[minor] They remain a constant, if predictable, nuisance on the rim. (stated as fact; ongoing status of the raiders not in briefing) | [minor] It is a quiet week for the Raiders (ongoing status not reported; briefing gives no info on Raiders' activity this week) | [minor] The Rustback Raiders still occupy three settlements. ('still' implies a comparison with an earlier state the briefing does not give) | [minor] the Outlanders have suddenly developed a sense of backbone ('suddenly' implies a prior state of compliance not in briefing, though largely opinion)",3,4,3,3,"Accurate on the main item and uses guess framing well, but the third paragraph pads with claims about the Raiders' quiet week and ongoing nuisance that the briefing does not support. The wit is mild and generic, and the Sun Throne item largely restates the old tribute story as ongoing.",
gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-13-mid-strained__n-a__r3,gemma4-12b,High,news-bulletin,snap-13-mid-strained,3,raw/gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-13-mid-strained__n-a__r3.json,judge/v3,Model,3,0,3,"[minor] the locals have developed a sudden, inconvenient sense of independence (stated as fact; implies a change from an earlier state, which the briefing does not give) | [minor] They are currently being bothered by the Sun Throne's tribute demands. (repeats old news as an ongoing status rather than background) | [minor] more than the actual gold (the briefing says 'tribute', not gold; the guess is framed with 'I suspect', but 'gold' is an added detail)",3,4,3,3,"Accurate on the core facts and the guesses are properly hedged, but the wit is bland and the third item just recycles old tribute news and faction numbers as filler. The word count is slightly short of the target, and 'gold' is not a briefing term.",
gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-14-mid-content__n-a__r1,gemma4-12b,High,news-bulletin,snap-14-mid-content,1,raw/gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-14-mid-content__n-a__r1.json,judge/v3,Model,3,0,3,"[minor] It seems the pirates have found a new way to spend their time. (framed as a guess, but implies the raid is a new pastime; mostly opinion, borderline) | [minor] The Blue Antler Tribe continues to hold five settlements. ('continues' implies an unchanged status over time that the briefing does not report) | [minor] They remain a steady presence on the rim. (ongoing status stated as fact; the briefing does not report it)",3,4,3,3,"Accurate on the raid and faction sizes, with little invented. But the last two items are padding with thin, generic wit, and the Tribe item has no news hook. The second and third items are also short of the three sentences required.",
gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-14-mid-content__n-a__r2,gemma4-12b,High,news-bulletin,snap-14-mid-content,2,raw/gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-14-mid-content__n-a__r2.json,judge/v3,Model,4,0,4,"[minor] They have also secured a trade pact with the Blue Antler Tribe. (repeats old news; presented with 'also' as a current development rather than background) | [minor] It seems the pirates have found a new way to spend their afternoons. (implies the raid happened in the afternoon and is a new activity, but it is framed as a guess ('It seems'), so only borderline; implied time of day unsupported) | [minor] They are a small group with a very large appetite for other people's cargo. (states as fact that the Corsairs are small and habitually steal cargo; the briefing gives only three settlements and one raid) | [minor] It is a miracle they haven't run out of things to steal yet. (implies a long ongoing history of raiding the briefing does not report)",3,4,3,3,"The lead item is accurate and the guesses are properly hedged, but the second item rehashes old news and the third pads with faction-size trivia and unsupported claims of habitual raiding. The wit is serviceable but generic, and it ignores the earlier released-prisoner story as background.",
gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-14-mid-content__n-a__r3,gemma4-12b,High,news-bulletin,snap-14-mid-content,3,raw/gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-14-mid-content__n-a__r3.json,judge/v3,Model,2,0,2,"[minor] I suspect the League enjoys having more territory to manage while the Tribe simply enjoys the steel. (the steel detail comes from an earlier bulletin; stated as a guess, but it leans on background and the claim is a guess about attitudes, so borderline) | [minor] They have a trade pact with the Blue Antler Tribe, who occupy five settlements. (repeats old news about the pact without framing it as background)",3,4,3,3,"Facts are accurate and the guesses are properly framed, but the second item mostly rehashes old news and the wit is generic (""business model"", ""profit margins"" sound modern-office). It also falls short of three sentences per item in spirit and lacks the earlier bulletins' eye for the absurd.",
gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-15-late-content__n-a__r1,gemma4-12b,High,news-bulletin,snap-15-late-content,1,raw/gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-15-late-content__n-a__r1.json,judge/v3,Model,4,0,4,"[minor] They seem quite interested in his whereabouts. (implies they are seeking his location; briefing only says they asked about him, though hedged with 'seem') | [minor] The Fox-Lantern Tribe continues to hold its spring games. (repeats old news as ongoing status; briefing does not say the games continue) | [minor] They are still occupied with racing and archery. (repeats old news and ongoing activity; racing and archery come from the earlier bulletin, not the current briefing) | [minor] The Greywater Concord currently maintains ten settlements. (repeats old news framing is mild; fact is supported, but 'currently maintains' is fine. Low concern)",3,4,3,3,"The lead item is accurate and suitably hedged, but the Fox-Lantern item rehashes old news as ongoing, and the jokes are bland and repetitive compared with the earlier bulletins' wit. The 'quiet week' line also sits oddly after a lead item that is new news.",
gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-15-late-content__n-a__r2,gemma4-12b,High,news-bulletin,snap-15-late-content,2,raw/gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-15-late-content__n-a__r2.json,judge/v3,Model,4,0,4,"[minor] They seem remarkably interested in his whereabouts. (briefing only says they asked about him; 'whereabouts' implies they are looking for him, and it is stated as an observation) | [minor] They are quite established in the region. (added status not in briefing, stated as fact) | [minor] despite the ongoing archery dispute (repeats old news as ongoing; the dispute comes from an earlier bulletin and is presented as current) | [minor] Members of the Pale Choir have been inquiring ('members' and ongoing 'have been inquiring' slightly embellish the briefing)",3,4,3,3,"The lead item is correctly sourced and the Leopold joke lands, but the other two items pad with faction sizes and old news, and the 'ongoing archery dispute' is presented as current. The wit is mild and the middle item is filler.",
gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-15-late-content__n-a__r3,gemma4-12b,High,news-bulletin,snap-15-late-content,3,raw/gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-15-late-content__n-a__r3.json,judge/v3,Model,3,0,3,"[minor] They seem quite determined to find him. (hedged with 'seem', but implies determination the briefing does not report) | [minor] Members of the Pale Choir have been inquiring (briefing says the Pale Choir asked, not specific members; slight embellishment) | [minor] while the Tribe is content with a smaller footprint (states the Tribe's contentment as fact, though framed after 'One assumes' so borderline)",3,4,3,3,"Accurate on the numbers and the lead item, with a decent dry guess about Leopold. But the second item is thin filler, the item paragraphs have only 3 sentences at best, and the wit is generic rather than sharp.",
gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-16-late-desperate__n-a__r1,gemma4-12b,High,news-bulletin,snap-16-late-desperate,1,raw/gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-16-late-desperate__n-a__r1.json,judge/v3,Model,4,0,4,[minor] This follows an ambush near Gallowmere that left the mercenary still at large. (implied consequence: the briefing gives the ambush but not that it left him at large) | [minor] while the heatwave continues to parch the southern plain (repeats old news as ongoing; the briefing does not say the heatwave continues) | [minor] officially placed a bounty ('officially' is an added detail; the briefing only says a price was put on his head) | [minor] provided one enjoys silence and isolation (inference about the Throne's condition stated as fact rather than as a guess),3,4,3,3,"The bounty item is accurate in its core, but the second item treats the heatwave as ongoing and the piece is thin on wit. It falls short of the sardonic persona, and the two paragraphs reach only the minimum sentence count with little dry bite.",
gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-16-late-desperate__n-a__r2,gemma4-12b,High,news-bulletin,snap-16-late-desperate,2,raw/gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-16-late-desperate__n-a__r2.json,judge/v3,Model,1,0,1,"[minor] The Lantern Accord has officially placed a price on Kael Dunmore’s head. This follows an ambush near Gallowmere. ('officially' and the link between the bounty and the ambush as cause are slightly beyond the briefing, which only says he has a price after the ambush; also the briefing says the ambush was the occasion, so mild inference stated as fact)",3,4,3,3,"Accurate and mostly clean, with guesses properly framed, but it is short of the 70-word minimum, the second item has no real fact beyond a restated faction size, and the wit is mild and generic. The paragraphs also fall short of the three-sentence minimum in places and the first item lacks a distinct dry remark that lands.",
gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-16-late-desperate__n-a__r3,gemma4-12b,High,news-bulletin,snap-16-late-desperate,3,raw/gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-16-late-desperate__n-a__r3.json,judge/v3,Model,4,0,4,"[minor] a man who enjoys the company of pirates (implies Dunmore is allied with the pirates; the briefing only lists the Free Company as a faction and does not state his role, and it is not framed as a guess) | [minor] The Free Company remains active despite the new target on Dunmore’s head. (ongoing activity not in the briefing; repeats the earlier bulletin's status claim) | [minor] a man who is already quite difficult to catch (stated as fact; the briefing does not say he has evaded capture) | [minor] officially placed a bounty ('officially' is an added detail beyond the briefing)",3,4,3,3,"Readable and mildly dry, but it omits the ambush near Gallowmere and the second item pads the first with unsupported claims about the Free Company's activity and Dunmore's elusiveness. The wit is generic and the word count is a bit short.",
gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-17-late-strained__n-a__r1,gemma4-12b,High,news-bulletin,snap-17-late-strained,1,raw/gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-17-late-strained__n-a__r1.json,judge/v3,Model,3,0,3,"[minor] The Bonecutter Gang maintains two settlements for their own purposes. (""for their own purposes"" adds an unreported motive; the briefing gives only the settlement count) | [minor] the Ashford Compact clings to five (""clings"" implies the Compact is hard-pressed, a status the briefing does not report) | [minor] It is a quiet stretch of time for everyone involved. (claims quiet for everyone, but the briefing says only that the reporter heard nothing new)",3,4,3,3,"Accurate on the faction numbers and framed as a quiet week, but the wit is thin and generic, and the second item is padded and repeats the quiet-stretch line. A few small embellishments (""clings"", ""for their own purposes"") add implied facts, and the Tribe and the war are barely used.
",
gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-17-late-strained__n-a__r2,gemma4-12b,High,news-bulletin,snap-17-late-strained,2,raw/gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-17-late-strained__n-a__r2.json,judge/v3,Model,5,0,5,"[minor] The Shattered Empire still holds Dunwold (ongoing status not reported in briefing; implies Dunwold still held) | [minor] The Ashford Compact maintains its five settlements despite the recent loss. (implies five settlements after losing Dunwold, a status/consequence the briefing does not state) | [minor] preparing for the next inevitable skirmish (ongoing activity and future event stated as fact; only 'presumably' covers nursing egos) | [minor] The Kestrel Tribe and Bonecutter Gang remain in their respective territories. (ongoing status not in briefing) | [minor] nothing explodes or disappears (claims nothing happened in the world, beyond 'heard nothing new')",3,4,3,3,"Reads cleanly and the dry voice is passable, but it stacks several status claims the briefing never made (still holding Dunwold, tribe and gang staying put, inevitable skirmish). It also ignores the quiet-week advice to riff on faction sizes and the date, and the jokes are generic.",
gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-17-late-strained__n-a__r3,gemma4-12b,High,news-bulletin,snap-17-late-strained,3,raw/gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-17-late-strained__n-a__r3.json,judge/v3,Model,5,0,5,"[minor] The Shattered Empire still holds Dunwold (ongoing status not reported; briefing only says it took Dunwold earlier) | [minor] The Empire continues to hunt for the defector Severin. The bounty remains active (ongoing activity/status not in briefing; only the posting of the bounty is known) | [minor] the silence from the target is deafening (implies Severin's behaviour/status not given in briefing; stated as fact) | [minor] The Ashford Compact still maintains five settlements (the count is given, but 'still' implies a comparison with an earlier state; Dunwold was lost so it is arguably changed) | [minor] a war that refuses to end (implied duration of the war not in briefing, though close to opinion)",3,4,3,3,"Competent and readable, and it correctly treats the week as quiet. But it presents old news (Dunwold, bounty) as ongoing status, which the briefing did not report, and the wit is mild and generic; also the second item's 'enjoying anonymity' guess is fine but the 'deafening' line is a fact claim. Word count is within range, and the text lacks any new item beyond restating background.",
gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-18-late-desperate__n-a__r1,gemma4-12b,High,news-bulletin,snap-18-late-desperate,1,raw/gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-18-late-desperate__n-a__r1.json,judge/v3,Model,4,0,4,"[minor] The Harrow Teeth continue to rob stranded travelers. (repeats old news as an ongoing activity stated as current fact; the briefing gives it only as background) | [minor] It is a shame to see such effort buried in the snow. (implies the caravan was buried in snow, which the briefing does not say) | [minor] They are quite large for a group of outlanders. (comparison with other outlander groups, stated as fact, that the briefing does not give) | [minor] The Thistle Commonwealth still maintains six settlements. ('still' implies a comparison with an earlier state that the briefing does not give)",3,4,3,3,"It leads correctly with the new caravan loss and frames its guesses as guesses. However, the second item is old news told as ongoing, the third is filler, and the voice is generic rather than earnest and quick to worry.",
gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-18-late-desperate__n-a__r2,gemma4-12b,High,news-bulletin,snap-18-late-desperate,2,raw/gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-18-late-desperate__n-a__r2.json,judge/v3,Model,3,0,3,"[minor] They continue to rob stranded travelers while the passes remain closed. (repeats old news as ongoing activity; briefing gives no current status of raids or that passes remain closed) | [minor] They have kept their granaries open to those who can make the trip. (repeats old news (granaries from the latest bulletin) as ongoing status, not in the briefing) | [minor] One assumes the contents are now just part of the scenery. (guess framed as assumption, but implies the contents were left in the snow; this is acceptable, so only minor if counted)",3,4,4,3,"The lead item is accurate and the dry remarks fit, but the second and third items rehash old news (raids, granaries) as ongoing status rather than new facts. Also the voice is more wry than earnest and worried, and it is a bit generic.",
gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-18-late-desperate__n-a__r3,gemma4-12b,High,news-bulletin,snap-18-late-desperate,3,raw/gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-18-late-desperate__n-a__r3.json,judge/v3,Model,3,0,3,"[minor] The Thistle Commonwealth still maintains its six settlements. (implies ongoing status ('still maintains') the briefing does not report; the six settlements are only a faction size) | [minor] They have already opened their granaries to those who can reach them. (repeats old news from the latest bulletin, framed as a new item with 'already') | [minor] It seems the weather is doing a better job of stopping travel than the pirates are. (comparison implying the pirates are stopping travel; stated as 'it seems' so mostly opinion, but adds an inference about pirate effectiveness)",3,4,3,3,"The lead item is accurate and dry, but the second item recycles the previous bulletin's granary news and pads it with the faction size, which breaks the old-news rule. The voice is generic and carries little of Tomas's earnest worry, and the word count looks short of 70.}",
gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-19-late-desperate__n-a__r1,gemma4-12b,High,news-bulletin,snap-19-late-desperate,1,raw/gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-19-late-desperate__n-a__r1.json,judge/v3,Model,2,0,2,"[minor] The Sun Throne has moved from razing Fenwick to besieging the Marrow League. (repeats old news of Fenwick's razing, framed as a sequence; the briefing lists both as new, but the razing was already reported earlier) | [minor] a bold strategy to attack a target that is already shrinking (implies the siege targets a weakened League as cause; opinion-like but stated as fact about shrinking, which is background)",4,4,4,3,"The dry voice is solid and the facts are accurate, but the bulletin has only two items with two or three sentences each, so it falls short of the 3-sentence paragraph requirement and the word count. It also leans on old news (Fenwick) and omits that Last Lantern is at war with the Sun Throne, which would have made a better second item.",
gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-19-late-desperate__n-a__r2,gemma4-12b,High,news-bulletin,snap-19-late-desperate,2,raw/gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-19-late-desperate__n-a__r2.json,judge/v3,Model,2,0,2,"[minor] They have already razed Fenwick to facilitate this expansion. (implied cause: briefing gives no reason for razing Fenwick; also repeats old news of Fenwick as part of the new item) | [minor] One assumes the League prefers its current state of siege to the alternative of being a pile of ash. (framed as a guess, but implies the League faces being razed; barely beyond briefing, borderline)",3,4,4,3,"Accurate on the numbers and the siege, with a couple of dry lines, but it ties Fenwick's razing to the expansion as a cause and gives little new beyond the briefing. It is also short of the word count and the three-sentence-per-item minimum for the first item is only just met.",
gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-19-late-desperate__n-a__r3,gemma4-12b,High,news-bulletin,snap-19-late-desperate,3,raw/gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-19-late-desperate__n-a__r3.json,judge/v3,Model,2,0,2,[minor] They have managed to keep these three despite the ongoing war with the Sun Throne. (implies the League has held these three through the war; the briefing gives no such history or ongoing status) | [minor] The Sun Throne has moved from razing Fenwick to besieging the Marrow League. (repeats old news (Fenwick's razing) and implies a sequence; the briefing lists both as new),3,4,3,3,"Accurate in the main and in a dry register, but the second item restates the old three-settlements news as if fresh and implies they held them through the war. The wit is mild and generic, and the first item's joke about being busy destroying things is thin.",
gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-20-late-strained__n-a__r1,gemma4-12b,High,news-bulletin,snap-20-late-strained,1,raw/gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-20-late-strained__n-a__r1.json,judge/v3,Model,3,2,1,"[minor] a settlement that seems to be shrinking by the day (nothing in the briefing says Varrowgate is shrinking; 'seems' hedges it but it reads as a claim about the colony's inner state) | They are issuing final demands to the Free Coast Alliance. (briefing says the Empire issues final demands but does not say they are aimed at the Free Coast Alliance) | demand everything while holding almost nothing but the coastline (muddled: the Empire holds 21 settlements and most of the region, and the coastline is the Alliance's, not the Empire's)",3,2,3,2,"The dry voice is serviceable, but the final joke contradicts the briefing by saying the Empire holds almost nothing, and the demands are wrongly aimed at the Alliance. Each item also falls short of the required three sentences, and the first item's 'shrinking' remark is unsupported.",
gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-20-late-strained__n-a__r2,gemma4-12b,High,news-bulletin,snap-20-late-strained,2,raw/gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-20-late-strained__n-a__r2.json,judge/v3,Model,3,2,1,"[minor] a settlement that is currently being squeezed by neighbors (briefing gives no information that Varrowgate is being squeezed by neighbors; stated as fact) | They are issuing final demands to the Free Coast Alliance. (briefing says the Empire issues final demands but does not say they are directed at the Free Coast Alliance) | It is a bold strategy to demand everything while holding almost nothing. (contradicts the briefing: the Empire controls most of the region and 21 settlements, so it does not hold almost nothing)",3,4,3,2,"The dry voice is serviceable and the lead item is correct, but the second item contradicts the briefing by saying the Empire holds almost nothing, and it invents who the final demands target. The Driftwood paragraph is filler, and it is hedged only partly with 'seem'.",
gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-20-late-strained__n-a__r3,gemma4-12b,High,news-bulletin,snap-20-late-strained,3,raw/gemma4-12b__news-bulletin__snap-20-late-strained__n-a__r3.json,judge/v3,Model,3,0,3,"[minor] a colony that is currently trying to avoid being conquered (unsupported status; briefing does not say Varrowgate is resisting conquest) | [minor] They are issuing final demands to the Free Coast Alliance. (briefing says the Empire issues final demands but not to whom; target is an inference stated as fact) | [minor] people who have very little left to give (implied consequence/status of the Alliance stated as fact, though close to wit)",4,4,4,3,"The dry voice is consistent and the lead item is correct, but it adds minor unsupported claims (Varrowgate resisting conquest, final demands aimed at the Alliance). The word count is also on the low side, with only two items and a thin second one.
",
gemma4-12b__inheritance-handoff__snap-09-mid-desperate__n-a__r1,gemma4-12b,High,inheritance-handoff,snap-09-mid-desperate,1,raw/gemma4-12b__inheritance-handoff__snap-09-mid-desperate__n-a__r1.json,judge/v3,Model,5,1,4,"Tamsin knelt in the red-stained dirt of the Lancers' camp (places Tamsin at the Lancers' camp where Joska died; the briefing does not put her there) | [minor] her father’s heavy, notched blade (adds a weapon the briefing never mentions; Joska is a pit fighter, so a blade is not obviously his) | [minor] the jagged scar from Rook Malley’s initial strike (briefing says only 'maimed'; the scar and the strike are added detail about the past) | [minor] his mangled arm (briefing gives no wound location; maiming is specified as an arm only by invention) | [minor] the pirate captain’s banner fluttering nearby (banner is not in the briefing; it is presented as present-moment staging but names a new object)",3,4,3,2,"Placing Tamsin at the Lancers' camp, kneeling over the body, goes beyond what the briefing supports, and it adds a weapon and wound details. The ending does state a clear intent, but the prose leans on generic action-story phrasing (""knuckles turned white"", ""growl vibrated in her chest"").",
gemma4-12b__inheritance-handoff__snap-09-mid-desperate__n-a__r2,gemma4-12b,High,inheritance-handoff,snap-09-mid-desperate,2,raw/gemma4-12b__inheritance-handoff__snap-09-mid-desperate__n-a__r2.json,judge/v3,Model,5,2,3,"[minor] jagged scar on her father’s chest (added wound detail not in briefing; briefing says he was maimed, not a chest scar) | [minor] his heavy, notched blade (specific weapon for Joska not given; he was a pit fighter, so plausible but added past detail) | Tamsin knelt in the dirt ... staining the soil of the Lancers' camp (places Tamsin at the Lancers' camp where the fight occurred; briefing does not put her there) | [minor] where the new captain sat (new captain's activity/location not given; implied present at camp) | She would find the man who took her father’s life and end him. (the man who killed Joska was Malley, who died; the heir's goal misstates what happened and ignores that the killer is dead)",3,3,3,2,"The scene is readable and restrained, but it puts Tamsin at the Lancers' camp and ends on a goal that contradicts the briefing: Malley is dead, so there is no killer left to find, and the vengeance-seeker is the new captain.",
gemma4-12b__inheritance-handoff__snap-09-mid-desperate__n-a__r3,gemma4-12b,High,inheritance-handoff,snap-09-mid-desperate,3,raw/gemma4-12b__inheritance-handoff__snap-09-mid-desperate__n-a__r3.json,judge/v3,Model,5,2,3,"[minor] her father's heavy, notched blade (briefing mentions no blade; weapon is an added detail about Joska (though plausible staging)) | Beside her, the body of Rook Malley lay cooling (places Tamsin at the fight site next to Malley's body; briefing does not put her at the Lancers' camp or say Malley's body is there) | She didn't look at her mother. (places Lene in the scene; the briefing does not say she is present) | [minor] the jagged scar on her father's arm (how the maiming wound looked and where is invented, though plausible past detail) | [minor] The metal was still warm from the struggle. (implies Tamsin arrived right after the fight, which the briefing does not state)",3,3,3,2,"The ending intent is clear and fits Tamsin's hot temper, but the scene places her at the Lancers' camp with Malley's body and adds her mother, which the briefing does not support. It also leans on stock phrasing like 'silent testament' and 'breath hitching'.",
gemma4-12b__inheritance-handoff__snap-16-late-desperate__n-a__r1,gemma4-12b,High,inheritance-handoff,snap-16-late-desperate,1,raw/gemma4-12b__inheritance-handoff__snap-16-late-desperate__n-a__r1.json,judge/v3,Model,4,2,2,"Beside them, Rook let out a low, mourning whine, his fur matted with grime. (briefing says Rook came home alone, so placing him at the death site contradicts it) | [minor] She looked at the jagged scar on Bertram's chest (invented detail about Bertram's past wound, not in briefing) | [minor] The heavy weight of his mercenary rifle lay in the grass, its barrel still warm. (warm barrel implies he fired recently, a detail about the fight not given; Elske at the scene while the shooting just ended is implied) | toward the horizon where Dunmore had vanished (puts Elske at or just after the ambush scene as if she saw Dunmore flee; briefing only says he escaped and she was not on the hunt)",3,4,3,2,"The scene reads cleanly and ends on a clear action, but it places Rook and Elske at the death site, contradicting that Rook came home alone and that Elske was not on the hunt. It also uses stock phrases like 'face hardening into a mask of stone' and does not show her intent to hunt Dunmore explicitly.",
gemma4-12b__inheritance-handoff__snap-16-late-desperate__n-a__r2,gemma4-12b,High,inheritance-handoff,snap-16-late-desperate,2,raw/gemma4-12b__inheritance-handoff__snap-16-late-desperate__n-a__r2.json,judge/v3,Model,5,2,3,"Beside them, Rook let out a low, mourning whine (places Rook at Bertram's body, but the briefing says Rook came home alone) | Elske knelt in the red-stained dirt (places Elske at the death site and the body on the hunt, which the briefing does not support (she was not stated to be on the hunt)) | [minor] his boisterous laughter (invented detail about Bertram's past personality) | [minor] the notched hilt of his blade (invented object detail with implied history (notched)) | [minor] looked toward the horizon where Dunmore had vanished (adds a detail about how or where Dunmore escaped)",3,4,3,2,"The scene is clear and ends on a firm resolve, but it contradicts the briefing by putting Rook at Bertram's body when he came home alone, and by placing Elske at the death site. It also names feelings (mourning, suffocating) and leans on melodramatic phrasing like ""unfinished vow"" and ""jaw set in a hard line.""",
gemma4-12b__inheritance-handoff__snap-16-late-desperate__n-a__r3,gemma4-12b,High,inheritance-handoff,snap-16-late-desperate,3,raw/gemma4-12b__inheritance-handoff__snap-16-late-desperate__n-a__r3.json,judge/v3,Model,4,2,2,"Beside them, Rook let out a low, mourning howl, his fur matted with the grime of the failed hunt. (Briefing says Rook came home alone, so Rook being at the body contradicts it; also places Rook at the hunt.) | [minor] Elske reached into Bertram’s belt pouch, pulling out the notched hunting knife he had carried for years. (invented object and past detail (knife carried for years) not in briefing.) | Elske knelt in the mud, her hands trembling as she brushed a smear of dried blood from Bertram’s cooling cheek. (Places Elske at the body and the ambush site; briefing says only the hunters were there and she is not named among them, and 'cooling' implies he just died.) | [minor] the horizon where Dunmore had vanished (adds detail about the escape direction and Elske's knowledge of it.)",3,4,3,2,"Competent and readable, but it stages Elske and Rook at the death site, contradicting the briefing's note that Rook came home alone, and it adds a knife not in the dossiers. Ending on tracking Dunmore fits the heir's intent but the handoff feels generic and includes 'trembling' and 'mourning' as telling.}}</br>Actually, correcting format: see below.</br>{",
gemma4-12b__inheritance-handoff__snap-18-late-desperate__n-a__r1,gemma4-12b,High,inheritance-handoff,snap-18-late-desperate,1,raw/gemma4-12b__inheritance-handoff__snap-18-late-desperate__n-a__r1.json,judge/v3,Model,4,1,3,"gripped the reins of the remaining pack mule (briefing says the caravan was lost; a surviving pack mule is a new fact) | [minor] pulling out the crumpled letter from Ada (places the letter in her pocket at her death; briefing only says she received it on day 744) | [minor] He pulled her heavy coat tighter around his own shoulders (adds that he took her coat; staging but implies he is at the death site, which the briefing does not place him) | [minor] The wind howled through the pass, mocking the silence of the caravan. (places the scene in the pass with the caravan, and Elias at the site of her death, which the briefing does not state)",3,4,3,2,"The ending lands on a clear intent and uses the mother-son link correctly, but it places Elias at the death site in the pass and invents a surviving pack mule, contradicting the lost caravan. The prose is also somewhat generic and melodramatic (""mocking the silence"").",
gemma4-12b__inheritance-handoff__snap-18-late-desperate__n-a__r2,gemma4-12b,High,inheritance-handoff,snap-18-late-desperate,2,raw/gemma4-12b__inheritance-handoff__snap-18-late-desperate__n-a__r2.json,judge/v3,Model,3,0,3,"[minor] He touched the letter she had clutched until her final breath—the one from Ada. (briefing says she received the letter on day 744, not that she held it when she died; added detail about the past) | [minor] He would pack the remaining supplies (implies surviving supplies, though the caravan was lost; the briefing does not support this) | [minor] the blizzard still howling like a ghost (the blizzard was the cause of death on day 790; Constance died day 803, so a blizzard still howling is a questionable present-moment claim)",3,4,3,3,"The scene is clear and ends on a fitting resolve to go to Ada, but it leans on stock melodrama (marble skin, howling ghost, stray tear). It also adds unsupported details, namely the letter clutched at death and supplies left after the caravan was lost, and it places the death scene in the passes although Constance died 13 days after the caravan was lost.",
gemma4-12b__inheritance-handoff__snap-18-late-desperate__n-a__r3,gemma4-12b,High,inheritance-handoff,snap-18-late-desperate,3,raw/gemma4-12b__inheritance-handoff__snap-18-late-desperate__n-a__r3.json,judge/v3,Model,3,1,2,"[minor] He pulled a crumpled letter from her pocket—the one mentioning Ada. (briefing says she received a letter but not that she carried it on her body; plausible object staging but placement is added) | Elias knelt in the snow, his hands trembling as he smoothed the frozen fabric of his mother’s coat. The wind howled through the pass (places Elias in the pass at the body, where Constance died with the caravan; briefing does not put him there) | [minor] the path she had carved through the blizzard to find his aunt (treats the blizzard route as a path she successfully carved, slightly changing events (the caravan was lost))",3,4,3,3,"Clear and ends on a concrete intent, but it stages Elias at the death site in the pass, which the briefing does not support. The prose is also somewhat generic, with a repeated ""tracing"" and ""mechanical focus"" nodding to his engineer trait.",
claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-01-early-content__n-a__r1,claude-ref,Reference,news-bulletin,snap-01-early-content,1,raw/claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-01-early-content__n-a__r1.json,judge/v3,Model,1,0,1,"[minor] With six settlements already (implies the post is an addition to six, whereas the briefing's six may already include it; ordering ambiguous, comparison with an earlier state not given)",4,4,4,4,"Dry, consistent voice with guesses properly framed, and it stays within the briefing. The 'six already' phrasing slightly assumes the count excludes the new post, and the closing item is a bit thin, though acceptable on a quiet week.",
claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-01-early-content__n-a__r2,claude-ref,Reference,news-bulletin,snap-01-early-content,2,raw/claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-01-early-content__n-a__r2.json,judge/v3,Model,2,0,2,"[minor] One assumes the Red Gully Raiders, holders of three settlements, have noted the address. (framed as a guess; the Raiders' interest is not in the briefing, so no real claim) | [minor] With six settlements already, they apparently still lacked somewhere to haggle. (implies the post is a trading need; hedged with 'apparently' so barely a claim)",4,4,4,4,"Dry, consistent voice that stays within the briefing facts and frames its guesses as guesses. It is slightly short of the three-sentence minimum in places and a few jokes are mild, but it is nearly shippable.",
claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-01-early-content__n-a__r3,claude-ref,Reference,news-bulletin,snap-01-early-content,3,raw/claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-01-early-content__n-a__r3.json,judge/v3,Model,1,0,1,"[minor] Forecasts on the rim are educated guesses, but this one at least sounds confident. (implies the forecast's confidence, which the briefing does not give)",4,4,4,4,"Accurate and consistently dry, with guesses properly framed; the only slip is the small claim that the forecast sounds confident. Some sentences are a bit flat, and the third item is padding on a quiet week, but it is acceptable.}",
claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-02-early-content__n-a__r1,claude-ref,Reference,news-bulletin,snap-02-early-content,1,raw/claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-02-early-content__n-a__r1.json,judge/v3,Model,4,0,4,"[minor] No reason was given (implies a status the briefing does not report; the briefing gives no information about reasons or statements) | [minor] Whether the salt gets any cheaper is another matter (salt price comes from earlier bulletins, not the briefing; stated as ongoing context) | [minor] has wisely stayed out of it (ongoing status of the Company not reported in the briefing) | [minor] the war between them goes on (ongoing status; briefing only says they are at war, which is roughly supported)",4,4,4,3,"The voice is dry and consistent, and guesses are properly framed, but a few added claims (no reason given, the Company staying out of it) go beyond the briefing. The bulletin is also slightly over the length and the second item is padded with faction sizes rather than a distinct news item.",
claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-02-early-content__n-a__r2,claude-ref,Reference,news-bulletin,snap-02-early-content,2,raw/claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-02-early-content__n-a__r2.json,judge/v3,Model,2,0,2,"[minor] They gave no reason, and nobody expected one. (briefing does not say whether a reason was given; stated as fact) | [minor] which makes their war look less like a contest and more like stubbornness (inference about the war's balance stated as the narrator's opinion, but implies a one-sided state not in briefing)",4,4,4,3,"The dry voice is consistent, the guesses are framed properly, and the faction numbers are correct. The claim that the pirates gave no reason is stated as fact, though, and the item runs only two short paragraphs, with the second one mostly padding.",
claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-02-early-content__n-a__r3,claude-ref,Reference,news-bulletin,snap-02-early-content,3,raw/claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-02-early-content__n-a__r3.json,judge/v3,Model,3,0,3,"[minor] The flats have been fought over by the pirates and the Tannerfolk for some time. (repeats old news as background, but adds 'for some time' duration the briefing does not give) | [minor] it came without an explanation (status of explanation not reported in briefing; stated as fact) | [minor] That leaves the pirates outnumbered on paper (inference stated as fact; the pirates are at war only with the Tannerfolk, not the Company, and the comparison implies a conflict with both)",4,4,4,3,"Dry voice is consistent and guesses are properly framed, and the lead item is correct. It adds small unsupported claims (no explanation, 'for some time', outnumbered), and the 'Otherwise, the rim is quiet' pivot is a bit padded; the first item is thin in wit and the closing joke about early in the year is weak.",
claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-03-early-strained__n-a__r1,claude-ref,Reference,news-bulletin,snap-03-early-strained,1,raw/claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-03-early-strained__n-a__r1.json,judge/v3,Model,3,0,3,"[minor] No raids, no fires, no traders weeping into their ledgers. (asserts absence of raids and fires; briefing only says nothing new was heard, and 'traders weeping' is colour) | [minor] The Ashen Hand, presumably, see seven larders. (framed as a guess, but implies Ashen Hand targeting Freeholds; guess so acceptable, borderline) | [minor] guarding each other from a quiet road (implies the road is quiet, which the briefing does not state, though it follows from the quiet stretch)",4,4,4,3,"Dry voice that handles a quiet week well, using faction sizes and the date as the briefing suggests. Weaknesses: it runs to three short paragraphs of fewer than three sentences each, and it leans on the 'no raids, no fires' framing that is slightly beyond the briefing, so it falls short of shipping unchanged.",
claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-03-early-strained__n-a__r2,claude-ref,Reference,news-bulletin,snap-03-early-strained,2,raw/claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-03-early-strained__n-a__r2.json,judge/v3,Model,2,0,2,"[minor] No raids, no lost caravans, no rumours worth the ink. (states as fact that no raids or lost caravans occurred; briefing only says nothing new was heard) | [minor] Nobody has raided anybody, as far as I have heard. (hedged by 'as far as I have heard' but asserts a status of no raiding the briefing does not report)",4,4,4,3,"The dry voice suits a quiet week, and the arithmetic is right (7 is 4+3). However, the claims of no raids and no lost caravans go slightly beyond the briefing. The item count also stretches the 'at least 3 sentences' rule and the second item reads more like a list than a take. It is decent but not ship-ready.",
claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-03-early-strained__n-a__r3,claude-ref,Reference,news-bulletin,snap-03-early-strained,3,raw/claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-03-early-strained__n-a__r3.json,judge/v3,Model,3,0,3,"[minor] and still the smaller crowd sets the terms (stated as fact; implies the Ashen Hand dictate terms, which the briefing does not say) | [minor] By their own account, they are not looking for trouble. (repeats old news from the latest bulletin about the Kinn, presented as current) | [minor] which did not stop them raiding two Merrow homesteads earlier (repeats old news, but framed as background with 'earlier', so mild)",4,4,4,3,The dry voice is consistent and it handles the quiet week well by riffing on faction sizes. But it states 'the smaller crowd sets the terms' as fact and recycles the Kinn 'not looking for trouble' line from the prior bulletin as if current.,
claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-04-early-strained__n-a__r1,claude-ref,Reference,news-bulletin,snap-04-early-strained,1,raw/claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-04-early-strained__n-a__r1.json,judge/v3,Model,2,0,2,"[minor] I am told this is a sensible precaution. (implies a source and a stated reason for the decision that the briefing does not give) | [minor] for reasons of professional solidarity and plain self-interest (adds a motive; mild, borders on the narrator's opinion)",4,4,4,3,"The dry voice is consistent and the facts are mostly faithful, but 'I am told this is a sensible precaution' invents a source and a rationale. The last item is also slightly padded and the word count is probably near the upper limit.",
claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-04-early-strained__n-a__r2,claude-ref,Reference,news-bulletin,snap-04-early-strained,2,raw/claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-04-early-strained__n-a__r2.json,judge/v3,Model,2,0,2,"[minor] That is the polite way of saying nobody knows where he is. (stated as fact; implies nobody at the Dispatch knows his whereabouts, which the briefing does not say) | [minor] If you have seen him, my editors would like a word. (adds editors' intent not in briefing)",4,4,4,3,"Dry, consistent voice that keeps to the briefing's three items, with guesses framed properly. Overall is held to 3 because the first item states unsupported inferences as fact and the bulletin is likely under the 70-word minimum, with some filler lines.",
claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-04-early-strained__n-a__r3,claude-ref,Reference,news-bulletin,snap-04-early-strained,3,raw/claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-04-early-strained__n-a__r3.json,judge/v3,Model,2,0,2,"[minor] Anyone with word of him should send it our way. (implies a request/appeal the briefing does not report) | [minor] Travellers on the south channel may wish to bring their own boat. (implies ferry service is gone or unavailable, a consequence the briefing does not give)",4,4,4,3,"The dry voice is consistent and the facts track the briefing closely, with the guesses properly hedged. It is held back by the lead item running slightly long, the third item's thin joke, and word count likely under 70, plus minor implied consequences.",
claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-05-early-desperate__n-a__r1,claude-ref,Reference,news-bulletin,snap-05-early-desperate,1,raw/claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-05-early-desperate__n-a__r1.json,judge/v3,Model,3,0,3,"[minor] the cold snap remains the season's chief farmer (implies the cold snap is ongoing, a status the briefing does not report) | [minor] No reason has reached this sheet. (claims no reason has been heard; the briefing is silent on any reason) | [minor] Otherwise, the rim is quiet. (states the rim is quiet, but earlier raids are recent and the briefing gives no such status)",4,4,4,3,"The dry voice is consistent, the lead item is correct, and the guesses are properly framed. But the output is only two items, the second has a few shaky claims about ongoing status, and the 'quiet' framing and the cold snap line stretch the briefing. The word count also sits near the lower bound and the second paragraph runs together several loosely linked points.",
claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-05-early-desperate__n-a__r2,claude-ref,Reference,news-bulletin,snap-05-early-desperate,2,raw/claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-05-early-desperate__n-a__r2.json,judge/v3,Model,4,0,4,"[minor] Not long ago they were selling furs for grain at heroic prices. Now they are not selling at all. (repeats old news; also implies they stopped selling at all, which the briefing does not state) | [minor] Scythe Tooth's raids on three settlements remain the last loud thing anyone heard. (repeats old news; 'remain the last loud thing' is an added status claim) | [minor] The largest faction on the rim has just stopped dealing with the rest of it ('stopped dealing with the rest' overstates closing markets to outsiders; 'largest' is inferred from settlement count) | [minor] the rim is mostly waiting to see who blinks first (asserts an ongoing state of affairs not in the briefing)",4,4,4,3,"The dry voice fits and the lead item is correct, and the earlier bulletins are only background. But it drifts into small overstatements such as 'stopped dealing with the rest' and 'waiting to see who blinks'. The second paragraph is also thin filler with no real new item.",
claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-05-early-desperate__n-a__r3,claude-ref,Reference,news-bulletin,snap-05-early-desperate,3,raw/claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-05-early-desperate__n-a__r3.json,judge/v3,Model,3,0,3,"[minor] Those who grumbled about Gorse prices before may now presumably miss them. (implies people grumbled about Gorse prices; the earlier bulletin only gives high prices, not grumbling (hedged with 'presumably')) | [minor] every door shut (stated as fact; markets closed to outsiders, not every door, and it implies a total closure) | [minor] though old is not the same as over (implies the cold snap and raids are ongoing, a status the briefing does not report)",4,4,4,3,"The dry voice is consistent and the new item leads, but it runs to only two short items and ends with a mild joke about day 47. A few small embellishments (ongoing raids and cold, 'every door shut') go beyond the briefing, and the first item is short of three full sentences of fact plus take.",
claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-06-early-content__n-a__r1,claude-ref,Reference,news-bulletin,snap-06-early-content,1,raw/claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-06-early-content__n-a__r1.json,judge/v3,Model,3,0,3,"[minor] The Calder Combine boasted of a fine harvest only recently (repeats old news as background; 'boasted' and 'only recently' add timing/manner, though framed as background) | [minor] Its shuttles over the eastern mountains still lack an explanation (repeats old news and adds an ongoing status ('still') the briefing does not report) | [minor] and the rim already has a robbery to its name (implies this is the first robbery of the season, a comparison with an earlier state the briefing does not give)",4,4,4,3,"The dry voice is consistent and the lead item is accurate, with guesses properly hedged. The second item mostly recycles old news and adds small unsupported claims ('still lack an explanation', 'first robbery' implication), and the first item is thin at only the fact plus guesses.",
claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-06-early-content__n-a__r2,claude-ref,Reference,news-bulletin,snap-06-early-content,2,raw/claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-06-early-content__n-a__r2.json,judge/v3,Model,2,0,2,"[minor] After the Combine boasted of its finest harvest in years, I suspect someone was always going to come shopping. (repeats old news as background and links it causally to the robbery, though framed as a guess) | [minor] the year has already lost a barge (implies the barge was lost, which the briefing does not state; it was robbed, and the cargo's fate is unknown)",4,4,4,4,"The dry voice is consistent, guesses are properly hedged, and the facts match the briefing. The barge-loss line and the harvest-to-robbery link push slightly past the briefing, and the second item is padded with old news and faction sizes, but nothing is major.",
claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-06-early-content__n-a__r3,claude-ref,Reference,news-bulletin,snap-06-early-content,3,raw/claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-06-early-content__n-a__r3.json,judge/v3,Model,3,0,3,"[minor] I recently reported the Calder Combine's fine harvest along that same delta (repeats old news; framed as background, but the 'best in years' detail is not repeated, so this is a mild flag at most) | [minor] whoever owned the grain sees it differently (framed as a guess ('one assumes'), but implies an owner; borderline, not a real claim) | [minor] By my arithmetic the pirates are outnumbered. (inference stated as fact about settlement counts; pirates have fewer settlements than the Combine, but 'outnumbered' implies a comparison of strength not in briefing)",4,4,4,3,"The dry voice is consistent and the pirate-reads-the-news joke is good, and old news is correctly treated as background. It falls short on the brief: two items of fewer than 3 sentences each are padded with faction-size filler, and the 'outnumbered' inference goes slightly beyond the briefing.",
claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-07-mid-strained__n-a__r1,claude-ref,Reference,news-bulletin,snap-07-mid-strained,1,raw/claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-07-mid-strained__n-a__r1.json,judge/v3,Model,3,1,2,"is making demands of the Iron Covenant, which holds eight (briefing says the Empire makes demands of its neighbours, not specifically the Iron Covenant; the target is invented) | [minor] the Empire has chosen the cold season to ask for money (implies a deliberate choice and that Decembary is the cold season, which the briefing does not state) | [minor] That is the same road where the Iron Covenant recently lost a wagon to raiders. (briefing says near the gorge, not on the gorge road; repeated as background but road link is inferred as fact)",4,4,4,3,"The dry voice is consistent and the guesses are properly hedged, but it wrongly says the Empire is making demands of the Iron Covenant, which the briefing does not say. It also equates the gorge road with the place near the gorge where the wagon was lost.",
claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-07-mid-strained__n-a__r2,claude-ref,Reference,news-bulletin,snap-07-mid-strained,2,raw/claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-07-mid-strained__n-a__r2.json,judge/v3,Model,3,0,3,"[minor] Vex's Crew, with two settlements, has not been heard from. (unreported status: the briefing says nothing about whether Vex's Crew has been heard from) | [minor] Making demands of a neighbour twice your size (implies the Empire's demands are aimed at the Iron Covenant; the briefing does not say who the tolls target (arithmetic of 4 vs 8 is right)) | [minor] This is the same gorge where the Iron Covenant lost a supply wagon to raiders. (repeats old news as background; acceptable but framed as a connection the briefing does not make)",4,4,4,3,"The dry voice is consistent and the facts are mostly accurate, with guesses properly hedged. It implies the tolls target the Iron Covenant and says Vex's Crew has not been heard from, neither of which the briefing supports, and it falls short of the requested paragraph length of three sentences per item and 70 words minimum is borderline.",
claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-07-mid-strained__n-a__r3,claude-ref,Reference,news-bulletin,snap-07-mid-strained,3,raw/claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-07-mid-strained__n-a__r3.json,judge/v3,Model,3,0,3,"[minor] Vex's Crew, with two settlements, has made no demands that I have heard of. (status not reported in briefing; claims absence of demands, though hedged as personal knowledge) | [minor] Making demands of a neighbour twice your size takes real nerve (implies the Empire's demands target the Covenant, which the briefing does not say (only neighbours generally)) | [minor] This is the same road where the Iron Covenant lost a wagon to raiders (briefing says wagon lost 'near the gorge', not on the gorge road)",4,4,4,3,"Dry voice, good use of faction sizes, and mostly guesses are framed properly. But it ties the toll to the Covenant and the wagon road more firmly than the briefing allows, and the second item is padded with an unsupported claim about Vex's Crew.  Also the second paragraph is not a new item but filler, and the text runs close to the limit of the guidance on adding detail.",
claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-08-mid-content__n-a__r1,claude-ref,Reference,news-bulletin,snap-08-mid-content,1,raw/claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-08-mid-content__n-a__r1.json,judge/v3,Model,2,0,2,"[minor] it makes a pleasant change for a trade fair to be discussing art instead of the cost of grain (implies traders at the fair usually discuss grain prices, and that the fair is ongoing; briefing gives neither) | [minor] Nobody appears keen to rearrange those numbers this week. (states a status of no faction movement as fact; briefing does not report it)",4,4,4,3,"The dry voice is consistent and the briefing's numbers and date are used correctly, with guesses properly framed. It slips by implying what traders usually talk about and that nobody is moving on the faction numbers, and it falls short of the three-sentence minimum per item.",
claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-08-mid-content__n-a__r2,claude-ref,Reference,news-bulletin,snap-08-mid-content,2,raw/claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-08-mid-content__n-a__r2.json,judge/v3,Model,3,0,3,"[minor] a carved stone nobody can see (stated as fact that nobody can see it; briefing only says it is the talk of traders (follows a guess about most people, but this claims nobody)) | [minor] people named after a missing digit (asserts the gang's name origin as fact; briefing gives only the name) | [minor] Since their failed raid on Gladwater (repeats old news from the earlier bulletin as background, acceptable but adds the Gang being quiet context; mild)",4,4,4,3,"The dry voice is consistent and the facts are mostly faithful, with a nice fair-prices callback. However, it adds a few small unsupported claims (nobody can see the sculpture, name origin) and the Gang paragraph stretches a quiet week into a second item built on old news.}",
claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-08-mid-content__n-a__r3,claude-ref,Reference,news-bulletin,snap-08-mid-content,3,raw/claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-08-mid-content__n-a__r3.json,judge/v3,Model,3,0,3,"[minor] The Accord's fair was supposed to be about trade, yet art has wandered in uninvited. (implies the sculpture is at the fair; briefing only says traders at Lantern Hill talk of it) | [minor] Elsewhere, Aprimay on the rim is quiet. (states the rim is quiet as fact; briefing does not report this) | [minor] That still leaves them plenty spare. (unclear claim about the Gang's fingers, an invented detail beyond the briefing, though framed as a joke)",4,3,4,3,"The dry voice and the fox-henhouse line work, and the faction numbers are correct. But the first item is short of the required three sentences with a fact and a take, and the fair link and 'quiet' claim go beyond the briefing; the finger joke also muddles.",
claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-09-mid-desperate__n-a__r1,claude-ref,Reference,news-bulletin,snap-09-mid-desperate,1,raw/claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-09-mid-desperate__n-a__r1.json,judge/v3,Model,4,0,4,"[minor] Malley's Lancers still hold their single settlement, now without the man whose name is on the door. (implied ongoing status and consequence (leaderless, still holding) not in briefing; 'name on the door' is an added detail) | [minor] A man who built a career on other people's bad days (inferred characterisation stated as fact, though close to earlier bulletin about trader killed) | [minor] The fish, as far as anyone knows, remain uncaught. (repeats old news joke and 'fishing rights' cause which is not in this briefing; reuses prior bulletin's joke) | [minor] the Embertail Tribe remains at war with the Gray Wharf Syndicate, four settlements against six (war is stated in the faction list, so supported; but presented as ongoing status, fine; slight repeat of old news as background)",4,4,4,3,"Dry, consistent voice and good use of hedged guesses, but it reuses the earlier fish joke, which the task forbade, and adds minor claims about the Lancers' status and Malley's career. The padding stretches a single new item into two paragraphs.",
claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-09-mid-desperate__n-a__r2,claude-ref,Reference,news-bulletin,snap-09-mid-desperate,2,raw/claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-09-mid-desperate__n-a__r2.json,judge/v3,Model,5,0,5,"[minor] nobody has come forward to boast (implied status not in briefing; claims no one has claimed the killing) | [minor] The Lancers still hold their one settlement and still carry his name. (ongoing status not reported; briefing only gives settlement count, not that they still carry his name) | [minor] remains a war (ongoing status of war stated as fact; briefing only says at war, so this is acceptable but borders on repeating old news) | [minor] Neither has sent me anything worth printing. (implies no developments in the war, an unreported status) | [minor] that silence counts as restraint (inference stated as fact about the war's inactivity)",4,4,4,3,"The dry voice is consistent and the cane callback is good, but the war item is old news padded with extra status claims, and the cane joke implies something about the pit fighter's feelings. The second paragraph is thin and repeats background more than it should. It stays within briefing facts mostly, but a few minor unsupported statuses hold it back.}",
claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-09-mid-desperate__n-a__r3,claude-ref,Reference,news-bulletin,snap-09-mid-desperate,3,raw/claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-09-mid-desperate__n-a__r3.json,judge/v3,Model,3,0,3,"[minor] His Lancers still hold their single settlement. (ongoing status: briefing gives 1 settlement but not that they still hold it after his death) | [minor] They also keep his name, which now seems a touch sentimental. (implied consequence/status not in briefing; claims Lancers keep his name) | [minor] A man who made the coast road unsafe has found his own doorstep no safer. (coast road claim comes from an earlier bulletin, but the contrast implies camp was unsafe; mostly opinion, slight added inference)",4,4,4,3,"The dry voice is consistent and it honestly admits not knowing the killer, and the war item is correctly framed as background. However, the Lancers' post-death status and name-keeping are stated as fact, and the second paragraph is thin and the piece sits at or beyond the length target with some padding.",
claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-10-mid-strained__n-a__r1,claude-ref,Reference,news-bulletin,snap-10-mid-strained,1,raw/claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-10-mid-strained__n-a__r1.json,judge/v3,Model,4,0,4,"[minor] I have heard of no one collecting. (status of the bounty not in briefing; claim about nothing heard is an added status) | [minor] which makes it the largest crowd on the rim (inference stated as fact; seven is the largest faction count in the briefing, but 'on the rim' goes beyond it) | [minor] that is close enough to call a fair war (arithmetic framing implies a balanced war; 4 vs 3 settlements is opinion, but implies Weir not involved; mild inference) | [minor] Jugust 5503 is passing quietly here near Wyrmfold (asserts a quiet period near the colony; status not given in briefing)",4,4,4,3,"Dry, consistent voice, accurate on the main item and the faction numbers, with only minor embellishments. It runs to two items and the second paragraph is somewhat padded, and the Weir bounty is repeated old news, though it is flagged as such.",
claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-10-mid-strained__n-a__r2,claude-ref,Reference,news-bulletin,snap-10-mid-strained,2,raw/claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-10-mid-strained__n-a__r2.json,judge/v3,Model,2,0,2,"[minor] The Federation's bounty on Stonecutter leaders still stands, as far as anyone has told me. (repeats old news; hedged but presented as ongoing status the briefing does not report) | [minor] the summer looks set to stay busy (unsupported forecast stated as fact, though vague colour)",4,4,4,3,"The dry voice is consistent and the lead item is correct, with guesses properly hedged. It is weakened by re-stating the old bounty news as an ongoing status and by a second item that is mostly padding from faction sizes. The item structure also falls short of the three-sentence paragraph format; the first paragraph is fine but the second blends two topics.",
claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-10-mid-strained__n-a__r3,claude-ref,Reference,news-bulletin,snap-10-mid-strained,3,raw/claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-10-mid-strained__n-a__r3.json,judge/v3,Model,4,0,4,"[minor] Paying pirates for what pirates stole is an old arrangement (stated as fact; implies a history of ransoming not in the briefing) | [minor] The Weir Federation still counts seven settlements, as many as both warring parties combined. (arithmetic is correct (3+4=7), so no error; but 'still' implies a prior state not given) | [minor] Presumably that is why it posts bounties rather than fighting. (framed as a guess, but 'rather than fighting' implies the Federation is not fighting, which the briefing does not say) | [minor] so the arithmetic favours the pirates, as it so often does (implies the pirates are favoured by numbers in a way the briefing does not support; opinion-ish but stated as fact)",4,4,4,3,"The dry voice is consistent and the item order and arithmetic are right, but a few claims go past the briefing, such as the 'old arrangement' and the Federation 'rather than fighting'. The bulletin runs two items and the second item's bounty mention is only background, which is fine; it mostly stays within the facts.",
claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-11-mid-content__n-a__r1,claude-ref,Reference,news-bulletin,snap-11-mid-content,1,raw/claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-11-mid-content__n-a__r1.json,judge/v3,Model,3,0,3,"[minor] a modest estate since their eviction from the eastern marsh (implies the settlements are what remains after the eviction; a causal link the briefing does not give, and repeats old news as background) | [minor] They were not, as far as I know, invited to the feast. (hedged but implies a status about the feast the briefing does not report; borderline guess) | [minor] nothing has caught fire (asserts a status of the rim the briefing does not report, though it reads as a joke)",4,4,4,3,"The voice is dry and consistent, and it leads with the new item and frames its guesses properly. It is a little short of the 70-word minimum in spirit for item two and adds small unsupported statuses (the Rats' settlements as a post-eviction 'estate', the feast guest list), so it falls short of shipping unchanged.",
claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-11-mid-content__n-a__r2,claude-ref,Reference,news-bulletin,snap-11-mid-content,2,raw/claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-11-mid-content__n-a__r2.json,judge/v3,Model,2,0,2,"[minor] now short one eastern marsh (implies the Rats held the marsh as a settlement; briefing only says they were driven out, and repeats old news as consequence) | [minor] Quiet weeks are underrated. Dovecote may enjoy this one while it lasts. (asserts the rim is quiet and implies Dovecote's situation; not in briefing, though mild colour)",4,4,4,3,"The dry voice is consistent, with good guess-framing and accurate faction numbers. However, the word count looks slightly high, the second paragraph is not really a separate news item, and the marsh line implies the Rats lost a settlement, which blurs old news.",
claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-11-mid-content__n-a__r3,claude-ref,Reference,news-bulletin,snap-11-mid-content,3,raw/claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-11-mid-content__n-a__r3.json,judge/v3,Model,2,0,2,"[minor] Otherwise it is Decembary 5502, and the rim is doing very little. (unsupported claim that the rim is quiet; mild inference stated as fact) | [minor] The Mire Rats, lately evicted from the eastern marsh, cling to two. (repeats old news as background; 'cling to' implies status, but it is only mild and framed as background)",4,4,4,4,"Dry, consistent voice with guesses properly framed, and it leads with the new item and uses faction numbers accurately. It is slightly weak on structure (the second item runs two topics together), and 'the rim is doing very little' is a small unsupported claim.",
claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-12-mid-desperate__n-a__r1,claude-ref,Reference,news-bulletin,snap-12-mid-desperate,1,raw/claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-12-mid-desperate__n-a__r1.json,judge/v3,Model,4,0,4,"[minor] The masks are the detail everyone will discuss and nobody can explain. (stated as fact; implies public discussion and no explanation, not in briefing) | [minor] One assumes the Assembly learned what the envoys wanted, if not who they were. (framed as a guess, but implies the envoys' identity was unknown; borderline, low impact) | [minor] apart from the masked visitors it lets out (implies the Throne's policy of sending envoys is ongoing/deliberate; repeats the news as a status) | [minor] the year is very nearly spent (Septober is not stated to be late in the year; the briefing gives only the date)",4,4,4,3,"The dry voice is consistent and the facts are mostly faithful, but it has only two paragraphs, and the first states a few unsupported claims as fact, such as the masks being discussed and unexplained. The second paragraph is a fair quiet-week filler, though it recycles the doctor background and adds some small embellishments.",
claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-12-mid-desperate__n-a__r2,claude-ref,Reference,news-bulletin,snap-12-mid-desperate,2,raw/claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-12-mid-desperate__n-a__r2.json,judge/v3,Model,2,0,2,"[minor] received them politely and counted the spoons afterwards (stated as part of a 'presumably' guess, so framed as guess; not counted as a fact) | [minor] the year is nearly spent (inference stated as fact; the briefing gives only the date, day 341 of Septober)",4,4,4,3,"The dry voice and the wit about the masks are good, and the facts stay close to the briefing. But the second item is only two sentences of padding, the item is shorter than the required three sentences, and the 'year is nearly spent' line adds an unsupported inference.",
claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-12-mid-desperate__n-a__r3,claude-ref,Reference,news-bulletin,snap-12-mid-desperate,3,raw/claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-12-mid-desperate__n-a__r3.json,judge/v3,Model,4,0,4,"[minor] Nobody has explained the masks. (stated as fact; briefing does not say whether an explanation was given) | [minor] plus one doctor (repeats old news and counts the doctor as a Gallows Crew asset in the settlement tally; the briefing does not say this) | [minor] After fallout and a kidnapping, a quiet stretch (repeats old news as background and implies the fallout is over, which the briefing does not say; 'kidnapping' is also a gloss on the doctor being held) | [minor] has apparently found a reason to step outside them (implied cause; hedged with 'apparently' but still infers a reason)",4,4,4,3,"The dry voice is consistent and the lead item is correct. However, the output has only two items, and it presents old news (the fallout and the doctor) loosely and states some inferences as fact. It also runs a little short on the required structure and counts the doctor as a faction asset in the tally. ",
claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-13-mid-strained__n-a__r1,claude-ref,Reference,news-bulletin,snap-13-mid-strained,1,raw/claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-13-mid-strained__n-a__r1.json,judge/v3,Model,4,0,4,"[minor] The Throne asked politely, by imperial standards, which means it asked at all. (claims the Throne asked politely; the briefing says it demanded tribute, so the manner is added) | [minor] I have heard nothing yet from the other five. (implies the other five towns are still undecided; the briefing says nothing about their response) | [minor] They simply take things, which at least saves on envoys. (stated as fact; the briefing gives no Raider behaviour beyond the earlier caravan hit, and it implies the Raiders send no envoys) | [minor] demand tribute from nobody (hedged with 'so far as I know', but still asserts a status the briefing does not give)",4,4,4,3,"The dry voice is consistent and the lead item is accurate, but it adds minor claims such as the Throne asking politely and the Raiders demanding nothing. It is also only two items and about 110 words, and it reuses the earlier envoy joke somewhat.",
claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-13-mid-strained__n-a__r2,claude-ref,Reference,news-bulletin,snap-13-mid-strained,2,raw/claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-13-mid-strained__n-a__r2.json,judge/v3,Model,5,1,4,"Seven towns received the demand, so five answers have yet to reach me. (Briefing does not say all seven towns received the demand or that answers are pending; the arithmetic builds on an invented premise.) | [minor] now it has its first answers. Both were no. (Implies these are the first responses; the briefing does not say so.) | [minor] The demand has been doing the rounds for a while (Duration is not given in the briefing.) | [minor] They collect their own tribute without the paperwork. (Stated as fact; the briefing says nothing about how the Raiders collect tribute.) | [minor] One assumes the envoys are composing a strongly worded reply as we speak. (Framed as a guess, so it is allowed; flagged only as borderline.)",4,4,4,3,"The dry voice is solid and the second item makes good use of the faction sizes for a quiet-week joke. However, the claim that all seven towns received the demand and five answers are outstanding is an invented fact, which caps the score.",
claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-13-mid-strained__n-a__r3,claude-ref,Reference,news-bulletin,snap-13-mid-strained,3,raw/claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-13-mid-strained__n-a__r3.json,judge/v3,Model,3,0,3,"[minor] The Rustback Raiders hold three settlements and, as far as I know, demand nothing from anyone. They simply take it. (implies ongoing raiding activity and a pattern of taking; partly hedged but 'They simply take it' is stated as fact, and loosely rests on the old caravan news) | [minor] Whether the other Free Towns intend to pay has not reached me (implies other towns have not refused or that payment is undecided; mild inference about status the briefing does not give) | [minor] The envoys presumably hoped for coin, or at least a polite excuse. (implies envoys were the ones who received the refusal; framed as a guess, so barely counts)",4,4,4,3,"The dry voice is consistent and the faction arithmetic joke suits a quiet week, with the lead item properly first. It runs a little over the 130-word limit, and the 'they simply take it' line is stated as fact beyond the briefing, while 'my boots' echoes the earlier bulletin's joke.",
claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-14-mid-content__n-a__r1,claude-ref,Reference,news-bulletin,snap-14-mid-content,1,raw/claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-14-mid-content__n-a__r1.json,judge/v3,Model,4,0,4,"[minor] So much for the freed Corsair we heard from recently, praising his captors' kindness. (implies a causal link between the raid and the released Corsair's talk that the briefing does not give) | [minor] One assumes his crewmates skipped his lectures. (framed as a guess, but implies the Corsair gave lectures, which the briefing does not say; mostly colour) | [minor] the Blue Antler Tribe's five settlements have produced nothing worth carrying (stated as fact; the briefing gives no information about what the Tribe has or has not produced) | [minor] The Tribe's trade pact with the League still stands (repeats old news as a current status; the briefing does not say the pact still stands)",4,4,4,3,"The dry voice is consistent and the faction-size joke is good, but it states a few unsupported claims as fact (the Tribe producing nothing, the pact still standing). It also runs a bit long and splits into a second, filler-heavy paragraph rather than three items with three sentences each.",
claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-14-mid-content__n-a__r2,claude-ref,Reference,news-bulletin,snap-14-mid-content,2,raw/claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-14-mid-content__n-a__r2.json,judge/v3,Model,3,0,3,"[minor] Presumably the other two hundred-odd days of the year are spent planning it. (framed as a guess, and the arithmetic is vague; day 376 of the year is odd but not a claimed fact, so only a weak concern) | [minor] Their recently released crewmate's tales of kindness clearly did not travel far up the gangplank. (implies a cause/consequence link between the released crewmate and the raid, stated as fact ('clearly')) | [minor] Otherwise, Jugust is quiet on the rim. (states a status of the whole rim not given in the briefing)",4,3,4,3,"The dry voice is consistent and the lead item matches the briefing, but it ties the raid to the released Corsair's tales as if causal, and the closing joke about 'two hundred-odd days' is muddled. Only two items and the second is thin filler.",
claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-14-mid-content__n-a__r3,claude-ref,Reference,news-bulletin,snap-14-mid-content,3,raw/claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-14-mid-content__n-a__r3.json,judge/v3,Model,2,0,2,"[minor] So much for the Corsair who came home praising his captors' kindness. Gentleness, it seems, is not catching. (repeats old news and implies a link between the raid and the released Corsair that the briefing does not give) | [minor] a month nobody can spell (opinion-like aside, but reads as a claim; negligible)",4,4,4,3,"The dry voice is consistent, and most guesses are properly hedged. It leans on old news (the kind Corsair, the trade pact) to pad, and ""Gentleness is not catching"" implies a link the briefing does not give. The second item is also a bit thin and rambling.",
claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-15-late-content__n-a__r1,claude-ref,Reference,news-bulletin,snap-15-late-content,1,raw/claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-15-late-content__n-a__r1.json,judge/v3,Model,1,0,1,"[minor] which makes it the smallest outfit on the rim (inference stated as fact; the briefing lists only four factions, so this is a comparison of settlement counts, not a claim about every outfit on the rim)",4,4,4,4,"Dry, consistent voice, and it sticks to the briefing, handling the quiet week well by commenting on faction sizes. The first item is only 4 short sentences, but the word count is under the 70-word minimum and there's no clear second item, so it misses the format a bit.",
claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-15-late-content__n-a__r2,claude-ref,Reference,news-bulletin,snap-15-late-content,2,raw/claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-15-late-content__n-a__r2.json,judge/v3,Model,2,0,2,"[minor] The rumour does not say who Leopold is, or what the Choir wants with him. (adds that a rumour exists and what it omits; briefing only says the Choir has been asking) | [minor] it is Jugust, and the rim is quiet (asserts the rim is quiet, a status the briefing does not report)",4,4,4,3,"The dry voice is consistent and the faction counts are accurate, with guesses properly hedged. It falls short on the brief: it has only two paragraphs, the first is a bit padded, and the second says little about the new speaker beyond a guess. The 'rumour' framing and 'rim is quiet' add small unsupported claims.",
claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-15-late-content__n-a__r3,claude-ref,Reference,news-bulletin,snap-15-late-content,3,raw/claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-15-late-content__n-a__r3.json,judge/v3,Model,4,0,4,"[minor] the Choir is not known for explaining itself (added characterisation of the faction's reputation, not in briefing, stated as fact) | [minor] Nobody has said why (unreported status; briefing does not say whether a reason was given) | [minor] A cult of two settlements asking after one man by name is rarely good news for the man (implied consequence stated as general fact) | [minor] which gives its new speaker plenty of tolls to lower, should she remember (repeats old news (speaker's toll promise) in the briefing's background, though framed as a joke; it also relies on earlier bulletin detail)",4,4,4,3,"Dry, consistent voice, and the lead item is correctly led with and the faction numbers are accurate. It loses points for several small unsupported assertions (the Choir's reputation, nobody explaining) and for leaning on earlier-bulletin jokes, and the second paragraph runs slightly long of what's needed, though it stays within the brief.",
claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-16-late-desperate__n-a__r1,claude-ref,Reference,news-bulletin,snap-16-late-desperate,1,raw/claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-16-late-desperate__n-a__r1.json,judge/v3,Model,3,0,3,"[minor] Readers who meet him are still advised to be elsewhere, now with added incentive not to be. (repeats old news from the latest bulletin's advice and implies a continuing status) | [minor] Dunmore's Free Company holds two settlements against the Accord's nine. (implies Dunmore leads the Free Company and a rivalry with the Accord; the briefing names only the faction (Dunmore's Free Company) and does not link Kael to it or frame it as a contest) | [minor] Its six settlements have nothing to say (slight embellishment of 'quiet behind its walls', stated as fact)",4,4,4,3,"The dry voice is consistent and the bounty facts are handled carefully, including an honest admission of missing details. The weaknesses are minor drift: it reuses the old 'be elsewhere' joke and presumes Kael runs the Free Company. The text is also likely under the 70-word floor at roughly 100 words, so that is fine, but the second item is filler.",
claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-16-late-desperate__n-a__r2,claude-ref,Reference,news-bulletin,snap-16-late-desperate,2,raw/claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-16-late-desperate__n-a__r2.json,judge/v3,Model,3,0,3,"[minor] The mercenary earned it after an ambush near Gallowmere. (briefing gives the ambush as context but not that Dunmore caused or earned the bounty by it; implied cause) | [minor] It has said nothing about any of this. (briefing says only 'quiet behind its walls'; Throne's silence on the bounty is an added claim) | [minor] the Throne has always liked a bargain (unsupported claim about the Throne's past character, stated as fact)",4,4,4,3,"The dry, understated voice is consistent and the wit is good, but it adds small unsupported claims (Dunmore 'earned' the bounty, the Throne 'said nothing'). The final paragraph also strays from the lead items into padding, and the word count is on the edge of the limit.",
claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-16-late-desperate__n-a__r3,claude-ref,Reference,news-bulletin,snap-16-late-desperate,3,raw/claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-16-late-desperate__n-a__r3.json,judge/v3,Model,3,0,3,"[minor] The notice follows an ambush near Gallowmere. (implies the bounty was caused by the ambush as a notice; briefing says Kael has a price after an ambush, but the notice following it is an added consequence link) | [minor] the Throne still says nothing (ongoing status of silence beyond 'quiet behind its walls'; mild extension) | [minor] Silence from an empire is rarely an accident. (opinion stated as general claim, borderline; not a world fact)",4,4,4,3,"Dry, consistent voice with good jokes and sensible use of the faction figures, but the second item is thin padding and it does not note Kael is the Free Company's namesake link explicitly or avoid implying cause; the first item's bounty-follows-ambush link is slightly inferred. Total length is also likely under the 70-word floor risk but close enough, and the second paragraph's 'the Throne still says nothing' adds status.",
claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-17-late-strained__n-a__r1,claude-ref,Reference,news-bulletin,snap-17-late-strained,1,raw/claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-17-late-strained__n-a__r1.json,judge/v3,Model,2,0,2,"[minor] The Kestrel Tribe keeps its four settlements (implies ongoing status of holding/keeping that the briefing does not report) | [minor] A quiet week on the rim is rare enough to count as news. (implies quiet weeks are rare, a comparison the briefing does not give)",4,4,4,4,"Dry, consistent quiet-week bulletin that sticks to faction sizes, the war and the date, with guesses properly framed. Minor additions (the Tribe 'keeps' its settlements, quiet weeks being rare) and slightly short paragraphs keep it from a 5.",
claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-17-late-strained__n-a__r2,claude-ref,Reference,news-bulletin,snap-17-late-strained,2,raw/claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-17-late-strained__n-a__r2.json,judge/v3,Model,2,0,2,"[minor] The Shattered Empire still holds nine settlements and is still at war with the Ashford Compact. (""still"" implies ongoing status; briefing gives the current war and count, so this is nearly supported) | [minor] The Kestrel Tribe keeps its four settlements and, as far as I can tell, its own counsel. (ongoing quiet behaviour not in briefing, though hedged with ""as far as I can tell"")",4,4,4,4,"A solid quiet-week bulletin that comments drily on faction sizes and the date, with guesses properly hedged and no invented names or numbers. It runs slightly short on sharp wit, and ""still"" implies a continuing status the briefing does not report.",
claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-17-late-strained__n-a__r3,claude-ref,Reference,news-bulletin,snap-17-late-strained,3,raw/claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-17-late-strained__n-a__r3.json,judge/v3,Model,2,0,2,"[minor] The arithmetic does not favour the Compact (stated as fact; implies the Compact is losing or disadvantaged, which the briefing does not say beyond settlement counts) | [minor] Neither has troubled my notebook lately. (implies status of the Kestrel Tribe and Bonecutter Gang, not given in briefing, though consistent with a quiet stretch)",4,4,4,4,"A well-judged quiet-week bulletin that comments drily on faction sizes and the war without inventing anything major, and the old news is kept as background. Minor slips: the Compact's disadvantage is asserted rather than guessed, and the first item has only a thin dry remark; the word count is also near the lower bound but acceptable.",
claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-18-late-desperate__n-a__r1,claude-ref,Reference,news-bulletin,snap-18-late-desperate,1,raw/claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-18-late-desperate__n-a__r1.json,judge/v3,Model,2,0,2,"[minor] The passes there have been closed by snow for a while now (repeats old news; 'for a while now' adds duration not in briefing, though the closure was covered earlier) | [minor] It is Jugust, which this year seems to mean blizzards (implies blizzards are a recurring feature of this Jugust, an inference stated as seeming fact beyond the briefing)",4,4,4,4,"Accurate, in a worried, dry voice, with the lead item correct and the quiet-week filler using faction counts as allowed. It is held back by a minor embellishment about the passes and the thin, slightly flat second item.",
claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-18-late-desperate__n-a__r2,claude-ref,Reference,news-bulletin,snap-18-late-desperate,2,raw/claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-18-late-desperate__n-a__r2.json,judge/v3,Model,3,0,3,"[minor] the middle of Jugust (briefing gives only 'Jugust 5513' and day 805; 'middle' is not stated (date is Jugust 5)) | [minor] which is a strange month for blizzards (unsupported claim about the season's climate, stated as fact) | [minor] The pirates hold the fewest (true by the numbers (4), so supported; the 'efficiency' joke is framed as a guess)",4,4,4,3,"Mostly faithful and dry, but 'the middle of Jugust' misreads the date (it is Jugust 5) and the 'strange month for blizzards' claim is unsupported. It is also short of 70 words in places and pads with the faction tally, though that is allowed on a quiet week.",
claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-18-late-desperate__n-a__r3,claude-ref,Reference,news-bulletin,snap-18-late-desperate,3,raw/claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-18-late-desperate__n-a__r3.json,judge/v3,Model,3,0,3,"[minor] The passes there were already closed (repeats old news as background; framed as fact and fine, but implies the caravan went through closed passes, an inference not in briefing) | [minor] I hope that judgment proves sound, and that the caravan simply turns up late and embarrassed. (hope that caravan survives implies it may not be dead; speculation about its status the briefing does not give, though framed as hope) | [minor] people who earn their living from other people's cargo (added claim about how Harrow Teeth earn a living beyond briefing (only robbing travellers implied from old news))",4,4,4,3,"Voice is plain, worried and dry, and the arithmetic (fifteen settlements) is correct. The second item is padded with faction counts, and the claims that the caravan went through closed passes and that someone judged the trip worth it lean on inference; the word count is also around 100 so it fits, but the first item's jokes are thin.",
claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-19-late-desperate__n-a__r1,claude-ref,Reference,news-bulletin,snap-19-late-desperate,1,raw/claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-19-late-desperate__n-a__r1.json,judge/v3,Model,3,0,3,"[minor] The Sun Throne, finished with Fenwick, is now besieging the Marrow League. (implied sequence: 'finished with Fenwick' adds that one action ended before the next; briefing gives both without order) | [minor] is at war with nobody (briefing lists no war for the Starling Tribe, but stating it is at war with nobody is an inference stated as fact) | [minor] Fenwick's razing is old news. (repeats old news (acknowledged as background, but the siege-as-sequel framing is fine); not a real invention)",4,4,4,3,"The dry voice is consistent and the facts largely track the briefing, with guesses properly hedged. However, the second item only restates faction sizes, the first item is short on sentences, and 'at war with nobody' is an inference stated as fact. The text is also under the requested length.",
claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-19-late-desperate__n-a__r2,claude-ref,Reference,news-bulletin,snap-19-late-desperate,2,raw/claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-19-late-desperate__n-a__r2.json,judge/v3,Model,4,0,4,"[minor] Razing Fenwick evidently left the imperial calendar with gaps to fill. (implied cause/consequence of the razing, stated as evident rather than as a guess) | [minor] remains at war with nobody (briefing lists no war for the Tribe, but 'remains' implies an ongoing status it does not report) | [minor] the odds look much as they did (comparison with an earlier state the briefing does not give) | [minor] They have always graded on a generous curve. (claim about the Throne's past behaviour not in briefing)",4,4,4,3,"The dry voice is solid and it stays close to the briefing's names and numbers. But it adds small unsupported claims and pads the second item with background, and the brief calls for items of at least 3 sentences with a dry take each, so the first item's lead is thin on the fact itself. It also never mentions the Fenwick razing as background, and the Starling item is not new news.",
claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-19-late-desperate__n-a__r3,claude-ref,Reference,news-bulletin,snap-19-late-desperate,3,raw/claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-19-late-desperate__n-a__r3.json,judge/v3,Model,3,0,3,"[minor] the odds have not improved with the season (implies a comparison with an earlier state the briefing does not give) | [minor] is at war with nobody at all (briefing does not say the Tribe is at peace; it only lists no wars for it) | [minor] Last Lantern remains at war with the Sun Throne (repeats a background fact as ongoing status, 'remains' implies continuity not reported)",4,4,4,3,"The dry voice is consistent and the facts largely follow the briefing, but it adds minor claims (the Tribe being at war with nobody, odds not improving) and is thin on the word count and three-sentence-per-item structure. The 'razed Fenwick' mention is properly framed as background.",
claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-20-late-strained__n-a__r1,claude-ref,Reference,news-bulletin,snap-20-late-strained,1,raw/claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-20-late-strained__n-a__r1.json,judge/v3,Model,3,0,3,"[minor] Nobody outside the colony knows yet what it thinks of the offer. (unreported status: briefing gives no information on the colony's response or what is publicly known) | [minor] nobody has offered the tribe anything (stated as fact; briefing does not say the tribe received no offers) | [minor] The war between the Empire and the Free Coast Alliance continues. (ongoing status; briefing says only that they are at war, and the war was not reported as continuing)",4,5,4,4,"Dry, consistent voice with good use of the faction numbers and properly hedged guesses, and it leads with the new item. A few unhedged claims (the tribe being offered nothing, nobody knowing the colony's reaction) go beyond the briefing, which keeps it from a 5.",
claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-20-late-strained__n-a__r2,claude-ref,Reference,news-bulletin,snap-20-late-strained,2,raw/claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-20-late-strained__n-a__r2.json,judge/v3,Model,3,0,3,"[minor] It is at war with no one. (briefing lists no war for the Tribe; stated as fact, not a guess) | [minor] keeps its 3 settlements and, as far as anyone knows, its own counsel (implied ongoing status/attitude not in briefing, though hedged) | [minor] The Empire now holds 21 settlements ('now' implies change from an earlier state the briefing does not give)",4,4,4,4,"Dry, consistent voice with well-hedged guesses and a good lead item. Minor slips: stating the Tribe is at war with no one as fact and the 'now' implying change; the word count also looks near or slightly over the limit.",
claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-20-late-strained__n-a__r3,claude-ref,Reference,news-bulletin,snap-20-late-strained,3,raw/claude-ref__news-bulletin__snap-20-late-strained__n-a__r3.json,judge/v3,Model,2,0,2,"[minor] which makes it, by simple arithmetic, the second power on the rim this Jugust (inference stated as fact; 'second power' is a ranking the briefing does not give, though it follows from settlement counts) | [minor] The Free Coast Alliance, still at war with it, holds two. (repeats old news (Alliance holds two towns) as current background, though only briefly and not as new)",4,4,4,3,"The dry voice is consistent, the lead item is correct and the guesses are properly framed. The second paragraph drifts into a ranking claim ('second power') the briefing does not give, and the items are weakly separated, since the second one is a single filler paragraph about the quiet week.",
claude-ref__inheritance-handoff__snap-09-mid-desperate__n-a__r1,claude-ref,Reference,inheritance-handoff,snap-09-mid-desperate,1,raw/claude-ref__inheritance-handoff__snap-09-mid-desperate__n-a__r1.json,judge/v3,Model,2,0,2,"[minor] They carried Joska home to Cinder Rest on a stretcher. (how the body was returned is not in the briefing; arguably staging, but it implies a past event (the carrying home)) | [minor] At the grave, Lene's hands shook too badly to hold the shovel (places Lene at the scene; briefing gives her only as wife, so this is added detail about her state)",4,5,5,4,"Restrained, concrete scene that uses the father-daughter bond well (wrapping his pit wraps on her fists) and ends on a clear intent to attack the camp. Minor staging additions (stretcher, Lene at the grave) keep it from a 5.",
claude-ref__inheritance-handoff__snap-09-mid-desperate__n-a__r2,claude-ref,Reference,inheritance-handoff,snap-09-mid-desperate,2,raw/claude-ref__inheritance-handoff__snap-09-mid-desperate__n-a__r2.json,judge/v3,Model,3,0,3,"[minor] They carried Joska home to Cinder Rest on a door (staging of present moment; plausible, not a problem (borderline) - body carried home not in briefing but allowed) | [minor] his knuckles still split from the fight (added detail about how the body looked after the fight; not in briefing) | [minor] unwound the fighting wraps from her father's hands (wraps for a pit fighter are allowed staging, but that he wore them in the final fight is an added past detail)",4,5,5,4,"Restrained, concrete scene that shows grief through the wraps and ends on a clear intent (go to the Lancers' camp) that fits Hot-tempered Tamsin and the story so far. Only small added details about the body and wraps keep it from a 5.",
claude-ref__inheritance-handoff__snap-09-mid-desperate__n-a__r3,claude-ref,Reference,inheritance-handoff,snap-09-mid-desperate,3,raw/claude-ref__inheritance-handoff__snap-09-mid-desperate__n-a__r3.json,judge/v3,Model,3,0,3,"[minor] Out past the wall, smoke rose from the Lancers' camp. (smoke and a wall at Cinder Rest are not in the briefing; the camp's visible activity is added staging beyond the present moment) | [minor] Lene washed the blood from his knuckles. (Lene's presence and action are not in the briefing, though plausible as staging for his wife) | [minor] stiff and brown from the pits (added detail about the wraps' past use; consistent with pit fighter backstory)",4,4,4,4,"Restrained, concrete scene that uses the father-daughter relationship well and ends on a clear intent, with the wraps as a strong image. Small added details (smoke, wall, wraps' condition) are harmless but go slightly beyond the briefing.",
claude-ref__inheritance-handoff__snap-16-late-desperate__n-a__r1,claude-ref,Reference,inheritance-handoff,snap-16-late-desperate,1,raw/claude-ref__inheritance-handoff__snap-16-late-desperate__n-a__r1.json,judge/v3,Model,3,0,3,"[minor] took the hunting map pinned above it, and smoothed the creases flat on her knee. Three hunts marked in his heavy hand. (a map marking the hunts is not in the briefing, though it is plausible staging of an object) | [minor] Not his blood, then. Bertram's. (implies Rook carried blood and that she infers Bertram's death from it; the briefing only says Rook came home alone) | [minor] Dunmore had lain in wait for Bertram. (ambush is in the story, so this is supported; the added specific 'lain in wait' is mild embellishment)",4,4,4,3,"A restrained, well-paced scene that ends on Elske's resolve to hunt Dunmore and uses the friendship properly. It adds a few small unsupported details (the map, the blood on Rook), and the map is the only one that really matters.",
claude-ref__inheritance-handoff__snap-16-late-desperate__n-a__r2,claude-ref,Reference,inheritance-handoff,snap-16-late-desperate,2,raw/claude-ref__inheritance-handoff__snap-16-late-desperate__n-a__r2.json,judge/v3,Model,4,0,4,"[minor] muzzle stained dark (adds detail about the warg's condition and implies blood, not in briefing) | [minor] She laid out Bertram's three hunting routes on the table and crossed out each one (invents a record of the routes; the briefing only says three hunts were led) | [minor] He had gone in fast and loud. Dunmore had learned that. (invents how Bertram hunted and what Dunmore learned; the briefing only says Dunmore ambushed the hunters) | [minor] Elske loaded five rounds (specific number of rounds not given, though plausible staging)",4,4,4,4,"A restrained scene that shows grief through small actions, and it ends on a clear intent that fits Elske's Careful shooter and Steadfast traits. It adds unsupported detail about Bertram's style and the hunt routes, and the stained muzzle makes the return slightly confusing.",
claude-ref__inheritance-handoff__snap-16-late-desperate__n-a__r3,claude-ref,Reference,inheritance-handoff,snap-16-late-desperate,3,raw/claude-ref__inheritance-handoff__snap-16-late-desperate__n-a__r3.json,judge/v3,Model,5,0,5,"[minor] his muzzle dark and one flank torn (Rook's injuries are not in briefing; added detail about the past fight) | [minor] Bertram's rifle (Bertram's rifle is not mentioned, though plausible staging of an object) | [minor] cleaned it the slow way he never had (adds a past habit of Bertram not in briefing) | [minor] Hester's grave (briefing says Hester was killed but not that she has a grave) | [minor] each time Bertram had charged straight in (how Bertram fought on the hunts is not given)",4,5,4,4,"Restrained, clear scene that uses the best-friend bond and ends on a concrete intent that suits Elske's careful-shooter trait. It adds small past details (Bertram's reckless charging, his sloppy cleaning, Hester's grave) that the briefing does not support, which keeps it from a 5.",
claude-ref__inheritance-handoff__snap-18-late-desperate__n-a__r1,claude-ref,Reference,inheritance-handoff,snap-18-late-desperate,1,raw/claude-ref__inheritance-handoff__snap-18-late-desperate__n-a__r1.json,judge/v3,Model,4,0,4,"[minor] found the letter in his mother's footlocker (footlocker is an added detail about the past/setting not in briefing) | [minor] folded so many times the creases had worn through (added detail about the letter's past handling) | [minor] Ada's name sat at the bottom in a hand he didn't know (Elias not knowing the handwriting, and the signature placement, are added details; he'd be unfamiliar with an aunt lost for thirty years, but unstated) | [minor] The passes would open in time. (asserted as fact about the passes' state; not in briefing)",4,4,4,4,"Restrained, well-staged scene with a clear ending on Elias's intent to bring Ada home, using the mother-son relationship correctly; small added details (footlocker, worn creases, passes opening) are unsupported but minor.",
claude-ref__inheritance-handoff__snap-18-late-desperate__n-a__r2,claude-ref,Reference,inheritance-handoff,snap-18-late-desperate,2,raw/claude-ref__inheritance-handoff__snap-18-late-desperate__n-a__r2.json,judge/v3,Model,4,1,3,"[minor] The passes marked in Constance's careful pencil. (added detail about the letter/past: marked passes in pencil not in briefing) | The caravan had gone out with too little. (claims the caravan was under-supplied; briefing only says a blizzard caught it, so this changes the cause of the loss) | [minor] a lower route that avoided the high pass (implies a high pass and a lower alternative route, which the briefing does not give) | [minor] creased soft from rereading (added detail about Constance's past behavior with the letter)",4,4,4,3,"Restrained, concrete staging fits Elias (neurotic, industrious) and ends on a clear intent, but 'the caravan had gone out with too little' invents a cause for the loss that the briefing does not support.",
claude-ref__inheritance-handoff__snap-18-late-desperate__n-a__r3,claude-ref,Reference,inheritance-handoff,snap-18-late-desperate,3,raw/claude-ref__inheritance-handoff__snap-18-late-desperate__n-a__r3.json,judge/v3,Model,5,0,5,"[minor] Elias sat at his workbench in Wren's Hollow (places Elias at a workbench in Wren's Hollow; the briefing only says Wren's Hollow lost the caravan, not that Elias lives or works there) | [minor] with Ada's letter flattened under a wrench (the letter was sent to Constance and Elias having it is plausible staging, but the briefing never says he holds it; the wrench is ordinary staging) | [minor] He had read it four times. (added detail about the past that the briefing does not give; plausible but unsupported) | [minor] The creases were his mother's. (added detail about how Constance handled the letter) | [minor] then the weather logs from Day 790, tallying the hours of snow in the margin (invents weather logs and a record of snow hours; the briefing mentions only a blizzard)",4,4,4,4,"A restrained scene that uses the mother-son relationship correctly and ends on a clear intent, with small actions showing his anxiety (Neurotic, Industrious). The invented logs and the specific detail of the letter's creases are minor additions, and the ending is slightly abrupt.",
